{"openapi":"3.1.0","paths":{"/v1/accounts/lookalikes":{"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `accounts:read`.\n\nSend 1–50 companies by companyId, linkedinUrl, website or name, and a limit (default 100, maximum 500). companyId is an exact company dataset ID (number or numeric string), not a workspace account UUID. When supplied, it takes precedence; a missing ID is reported without trying other fields. Otherwise each company resolves by LinkedIn first, then its marketing website including redirects, then its name. Duplicate matched identities contribute once. No saved accounts are required. Optional hard filters minEmployees, maxEmployees, countries (ISO-2 codes or country names), regions and industries drop candidates outside them, including those with an unknown value for a filtered field unless includeUnknown is set; an employee bound replaces the seed size range.\n\nReturns candidates sorted by similarity to the closest seed, with preliminary high/medium/low bands. Matched seeds and candidates include companyId for reuse in later searches. Check seeds for each matched identity and whether it contributed. Unmatched or unindexed seeds are reported and skipped. If none can contribute, companies is empty. A search failure returns 503. The seed companies themselves are excluded; other existing workspace accounts may appear.\n\nSynchronous, read-only and unmetered. Allow more than 45 seconds for the client timeout. Returns up to limit candidates in one response, with no pagination. Import selected results using POST /v1/accounts/batch.","operationId":"findLookalikeCompanies","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/LookalikeSearchBodyDto"},"examples":{"companies":{"value":{"companies":[{"linkedinUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/stripe","website":"https://stripe.com","name":"Stripe"}],"limit":100}},"companyIds":{"value":{"companies":[{"companyId":6871792},{"companyId":"851530"}],"limit":100}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/LookalikeSearchResponseDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"503":{"description":"`lookalike_search_not_configured` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Lookalike search is unavailable. Retrying will not help. Contact support.\n\n`lookalike_search_failed` (`retry: retry_later`) — Lookalike search failed or exceeded its time budget. Nothing was saved; retry the same request shortly.\n\n`company_resolution_timed_out` (`retry: retry_later`) — Resolving the company by name timed out under load before we could answer. This is NOT a \"we do not have it\" result: nothing was recorded, and the same request sent again shortly will usually resolve. Companies sent by website or LinkedIn page do not take this path.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Find companies similar to a list of seed companies","tags":["Accounts"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["accounts:read"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/accounts/lookalikes\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"companies\":[{\"companyId\":1}]}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/accounts/lookalikes\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"companies\":[{\"companyId\":1}]})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/companies/competitors":{"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `accounts:read`.\n\nSend one company ({ self: true } for your own workspace, or companyId / linkedinUrl / website / name) and get back a ranked roster, default 15 and at most 50. Rank 1 is your first pin when you send pins, else the category incumbent, else the closest match on product and buyer. Candidates are drawn from companies similar to the subject plus companies named while the roster is generated; each is judged direct, adjacent or not a competitor, with 0..100 product and ICP alignment.\n\nThe roster is stored per workspace and subject. A repeat call with the same pins and an equal or smaller cap returns the stored roster (reused: true) and does not generate a new one, so a changed positioning has no effect until you send refresh: true. Sending pins replaces the stored pins for that subject; a new roster is generated when the pin set changes. Sending pins stores them for the workspace under the same accounts:read scope. Synchronous. Generation typically takes 10 to 25 seconds; allow 45 seconds for the client timeout.","operationId":"generateCompetitorRoster","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/CompetitorRosterBodyDto"},"examples":{"self":{"value":{"company":{"self":true}}},"withPins":{"value":{"company":{"website":"qodo.ai"},"pins":[{"website":"coderabbit.ai"}],"cap":10}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/CompetitorRosterResponseDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`company_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — We could not identify this company — not from the account's own record, nor from a LinkedIn page, website (including its redirect), or name — so there are no people to search. Retrying will not help. Send the company's own website if you did not; for any company, `POST /v1/find` on the contacts lane searches the web instead. From `POST /v1/find` with `filters.companyWebsites`, this means NO website resolved and nothing was searched; the message names every website. For one that is ambiguous (several possible companies on the domain) it also names the candidates and their ids: send the right id as `filters.companyIds`. When only some websites fail, the search runs over the rest and lists the others in `unresolvedWebsites`.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"503":{"description":"`competitor_roster_not_configured` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Competitor rosters are unavailable in this environment. Retrying will not help. Contact support.\n\n`competitor_roster_failed` (`retry: retry_later`) — Competitor roster generation failed or exceeded its 45 second budget. Nothing was saved; the previous roster, if any, is unchanged. Retry the same request shortly.\n\n`company_resolution_timed_out` (`retry: retry_later`) — Resolving the company by name timed out under load before we could answer. This is NOT a \"we do not have it\" result: nothing was recorded, and the same request sent again shortly will usually resolve. Companies sent by website or LinkedIn page do not take this path.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Rank the competitors of one company","tags":["Accounts"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["accounts:read"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/companies/competitors\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"company\":{\"self\":true}}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/companies/competitors\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"company\":{\"self\":True}})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/accounts":{"get":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `accounts:read`.\n\nA page of accounts, most recently created first. PAGINATES: follow `nextCursor` until `hasMore` is false.","operationId":"listAccounts","parameters":[{"description":"Case-insensitive substring match against `name` only — does not search `url` or anything else. This is how you look up whether an account already exists, and find its `id` to pass as `accountId` on `POST /v1/people`.","required":false,"name":"q","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"description":"Send a plain date — `2026-06-07`, read as midnight UTC — or a full ISO-8601 timestamp — `2026-06-07T14:30:00Z` — when you need the time of day. **Relative words are not accepted:** `yesterday`, `last-quarter`, `7d` and anything else that has to be resolved against \"now\" is rejected with a 400 (`invalid_date`). Compute the date yourself and send it. Returns accounts with `updatedAt >=` this value.","required":false,"name":"updatedSince","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"description":"Opaque pagination cursor from a previous page's `nextCursor`. Omit for the first page. Do not construct or parse this value — it is a base64url-encoded implementation detail and may change shape without notice.","required":false,"name":"cursor","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"description":"Page size, default 25. Values above 100 are silently CAPPED to 100, not rejected. Note the deliberate contrast with the two other bounds in this API: `POST /v1/find`'s `limit` is rejected above 100 (and a sentence search returns at most 50), and a `/v1/…/batch` array of more than 200 items is an ERROR rather than a clamp — silently dropping rows would lose records the caller believes it created. A `limit` that is zero, negative or not an integer is rejected here too; only the upper bound clamps.","required":false,"name":"limit","in":"query","schema":{"minimum":1,"maximum":9007199254740991,"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AccountListDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.\n\n`malformed_cursor` (`retry: fix_input`) — `cursor` was not a value this API issued. Send a previous page's `nextCursor` verbatim, or omit it to start over.\n\n`invalid_date` (`retry: fix_input`) — A date filter (`updatedSince`, `since`, `detectedSince`) did not parse. Send a plain date (`2026-06-07`, read as midnight UTC) or a full ISO-8601 timestamp (`2026-06-07T14:30:00Z`). Relative words such as `yesterday` or `last-quarter` are not accepted. `param` names the field.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"List accounts","tags":["Accounts"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["accounts:read"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/accounts\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/v1/accounts\", headers=HEADERS)\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]},"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `accounts:write`.\n\nAn account is a name, an optional URL and an optional LinkedIn handle. That is the whole record — see `AccountDto` for what reads back. `name` is the only required field: an account you have no website for is created with `url: null` rather than refused, the same way `POST /v1/people` treats a `company` with no `domain`. Send `url` whenever you have it — it is this route's deduplication key. Supply `linkedinHandle` whenever you know the company page: use the bare handle (for example `stripe`), not the full LinkedIn URL. It is the strongest way to identify the company and takes precedence over the website and name.\n\nYou can start discovery immediately after creating an account. These outcomes apply to every signal type, including `news`. While a run is active, keep polling the same run. `account_not_ready` means Trayo could not search the account this time. After the run settles, retry the affected account IDs. `company_not_found` means Trayo could not identify the company from the supplied details. For `company_not_found`, check the named accounts before starting another discovery. If an identity is wrong, send the correct `linkedinHandle` with `trayo_update_account` over MCP, or with `PATCH /v1/accounts/{id}` and a workspace API key over REST. When no handle is known, send a corrected website `url` instead. Both need `accounts:write`. `trayo_update_account` also reports whether Trayo can now identify the company. Importing the same hostname again skips the existing account and does not update it. After the current run settles, start a new discovery for the corrected account IDs.\n\nPublic REST and MCP usage is recorded without daily usage caps, workspace quota cutoffs or lookup quotas for now. Workspace request pacing still applies. **This call adds the account only, never people.** Finding people and adding them are separate steps: search with `POST /v1/find` as many times as you need, then add the people you chose with `POST /v1/people/batch`.\n\nTo attach people to future events, first set the workspace stakeholder definition with `PATCH /v1/workspace`, then start discovery with `people: \"add\"`. This definition does not add people to older events.\n\n**A `POST /v1/find` company row is NOT postable verbatim.** Its `id`, `website`, `linkedinUrl`, `industry`, `headcount`, `hq`, `fundingStage`, `foundedYear`, `companyType`, `description`, `why`, `known`, `state` fields are all refused with `validation_failed`, and the message names the offending keys. They are refused rather than accepted-and-dropped on purpose: these company details cannot be saved through this route. Select the accepted fields first: `jq '.data[] | select(.state == \"selectable\" and .url) | {name, url}'`.","operationId":"createAccount","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/CreateAccountDto"}}}},"responses":{"201":{"description":"Account created.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AccountDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"Malformed body — e.g. a missing `name`, a `url` without a scheme, or an unknown field. Posting a `POST /v1/find` accounts row unprojected is the common case: `param` names the first extra key.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"402":{"description":"`quota_exceeded` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — This workspace has insufficient quota for this operation. Retrying or changing the request does not help; raise the quota or wait for it to renew.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Create an account","tags":["Accounts"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["accounts:write"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/accounts\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"name\":\"<name>\"}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/accounts\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"name\":\"<name>\"})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/accounts/batch":{"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `accounts:write`.\n\nCreate up to 200 accounts in one call — the import path for bulk results (e.g. from `POST /v1/find`), where creating one account per HTTP call is the wrong shape. Every created account is assigned to the user your API key acts as, and starts becoming searchable, exactly like `POST /v1/accounts`. Read that route's description for what is and is not true of a new account; it applies to every row created here. Like that route, this call adds accounts only, never people.\n\n**This call does not wait for the background work each new account needs.** That work is started without waiting for it, so 200 rows cost 200 inserts plus one website check that is capped at a few seconds; the accounts become searchable by `jobs` and `job_change` over the following minutes, and a discovery run tells you which are not ready yet rather than silently returning nothing for them.\n\n**Each created row carries a prediction of which company it is.** Before answering, the websites of the created rows are checked together, and each row in `created` carries `identity`: `resolved` (with the company in `matchedCompany`), `uncertain` (several possible companies on that website, listed in `alternatives`), `not_found` (no company for that website: discovery will fail with `company_not_found`), or `pending` (no `url`, a `linkedinHandle` the website did not confirm, or the check did not answer in time; these are identified in the background, and a discovery run reports any that fail). Fix an `uncertain` or `not_found` account with `PATCH /v1/accounts/{id}` (its own website or its `linkedinHandle`), or delete it, before running discovery. `identity` is a prediction from the website: discovery runs its own match for each new account afterwards, and that match can land on a different company or on none. A discovery run lists any account it could not identify in `blockedSignals`; over MCP, `trayo_get_account_matches` reads the final result. Skipped rows carry none of this. These fields are on this response only, not on the account itself.\n\n**Project a find result before posting it — it is not accepted verbatim.** A find company row carries `id`, `website`, `linkedinUrl`, `industry`, `headcount`, `hq`, `fundingStage`, `foundedYear`, `companyType`, `description`, `why`, `known`, `state` alongside `name` and `url`, this route accepts none of them, and an unprojected batch therefore lands EVERY row in `skipped` (the reason names the keys). The import that works:\n\n```\ncurl -s .../v1/find -d '{\"target\":\"companies\",\"query\":\"...\"}' | jq '{accounts: [.data[] | select(.state == \"selectable\" and .url) | {name, url}]}' \\\n  | curl -s .../v1/accounts/batch -H 'content-type: application/json' -d @-\n```\n\nThe `select(.state == \"selectable\")` half matters as much as the projection: an `alreadyAdded` row would be skipped as a duplicate anyway.\n\n**Partial success is the contract.** A malformed row, or one that collides with another row in the SAME batch or with an account you already have, is reported in `skipped` by its 0-based index and a reason — never as a request error. This response is always `200`, even if every row was skipped. Only a problem with the REQUEST itself fails the call, and an array over the 200-item cap is one of those: it ERRORS rather than clamping, unlike `POST /v1/find`'s `limit`.\n\nPublic REST and MCP usage is recorded without daily usage caps, workspace quota cutoffs or lookup quotas for now. Workspace request pacing still applies. **Dedup is best-effort, not a guarantee.** A row is a duplicate when its `url`'s hostname matches, lowercased and with a leading `www.` stripped (`https://acme.com` and `https://www.acme.com/careers` collide, and so does a stored value kept without a scheme, `acme.com`). Failing that, a row is a duplicate when its `linkedinHandle` matches — so a company you already have under a different domain (a rebrand, a regional TLD, an account whose `url` is empty) is still recognised. That comparison folds together every shape the handle is stored in: case, percent-encoding (`airbus%2Dhelicopters`), and a full company URL rather than the bare slug. Last, a row is a duplicate by `name`, case-insensitively, and how far that key reaches depends on what else the row carries. A row with NEITHER a `url` NOR a `linkedinHandle` has only its name, so it is matched against every account in your workspace, those with a website as well as those without — a name-only import is not created twice, and it attaches to the company you already have. A row that DOES carry a `url` or a handle and missed on it is matched by name only against an account that has NEITHER a usable website NOR a `linkedinHandle` — the only case where a name is the sole thing the two records share. Two accounts that each have a real website are never matched on name, so two different companies with the same name both land. The `reason` on the skip names WHICH of the three keys collided.\n\n**A duplicate skip still attaches you to the account.** The account named by `existingId` is assigned to the user your key acts as, exactly as a created one is, so importing a company a teammate added already makes it eligible for your discovery runs. Importing a duplicate does not otherwise update the existing account; use `PATCH /v1/accounts/{id}` to correct its `name`, `url` or `linkedinHandle`.\n\nThis check happens in APPLICATION CODE — `Account.domain` has no unique database index, deliberately, because that migration needs a data backfill of its own. The consequence: two batches racing each other can both pass the duplicate check for the same key before either has committed, and both create an account. This endpoint cannot detect or prevent that race, there is no `Idempotency-Key` support here (unlike `POST /v1/discoveries`), and replaying the exact same request is not guaranteed to be a no-op. If your workflow cannot tolerate an occasional duplicate under concurrent imports, serialize your batch calls.","operationId":"batchCreateAccounts","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BatchCreateAccountsDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The request was processed. Check `skipped` — a `200` does not mean every row was created; it means the call itself succeeded.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BatchCreateAccountsResultDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"The request itself is malformed: `accounts` is missing, not an array, or has more than 200 items (`param: \"accounts\"`). A malformed INDIVIDUAL row never produces this status — it is reported in the `200` response's `skipped` instead.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"402":{"description":"The workspace quota cannot cover the accounts this batch would create. Nothing was created.\n\n`quota_exceeded` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — This workspace has insufficient quota for this operation. Retrying or changing the request does not help; raise the quota or wait for it to renew.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Batch create accounts","tags":["Accounts"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["accounts:write"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/accounts/batch\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"accounts\":[\"<accounts>\"]}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/accounts/batch\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"accounts\":[\"<accounts>\"]})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/accounts/{id}":{"get":{"operationId":"getAccount","parameters":[{"name":"id","required":true,"in":"path","schema":{"format":"uuid","type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AccountDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`id` is not a UUID.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"No such account, OR it belongs to another workspace — the two are indistinguishable on purpose.\n\n`account_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such account in your workspace. Another workspace's account is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Get an account","tags":["Accounts"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["accounts:read"]}},"description":"**Required permissions:** `accounts:read`.","x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"# Replace {id} with the real value.\ncurl \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/accounts/{id}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nid = \"...\"  # the {id} in the path\nr = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/v1/accounts/{id}\", headers=HEADERS)\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]},"patch":{"operationId":"updateAccount","parameters":[{"name":"id","required":true,"in":"path","schema":{"format":"uuid","type":"string"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/UpdateAccountDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The account after the update.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AccountDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"Malformed body.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`account_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such account in your workspace. Another workspace's account is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Update an account","tags":["Accounts"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["accounts:write"]}},"description":"**Required permissions:** `accounts:write`.","x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"# Replace {id} with the real value.\ncurl -X PATCH \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/accounts/{id}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"name\":\"<name>\"}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nid = \"...\"  # the {id} in the path\nr = requests.patch(f\"{BASE}/v1/accounts/{id}\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"name\":\"<name>\"})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]},"delete":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `accounts:delete`.\n\nSoft delete. Returns 200, not 204, with the account as it was — nothing in the response body distinguishes it from a normal GET, and there is no `deletedAt` field in this API's Account shape. The proof of deletion is behavioral: this id now 404s (`account_not_found`) on the account routes, is rejected as a `POST /v1/discoveries` `accountIds` entry with a 400 (`unknown_account`), and no longer appears in `GET /v1/accounts`. Only the account record goes: the events and people already discovered for it stay, so `GET /v1/events` and `GET /v1/people` keep returning rows carrying the deleted `accountId`.","operationId":"deleteAccount","parameters":[{"name":"id","required":true,"in":"path","schema":{"format":"uuid","type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The account as it existed immediately before deletion.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AccountDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`id` is not a UUID.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`account_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such account in your workspace. Another workspace's account is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Delete an ac