king.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Update a signal","tags":["Signals"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["settings:write"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"# Replace {signalKey} with the real value.\ncurl -X PATCH \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/signals/{signalKey}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"detects\":\"<detects>\"}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nsignal_key = \"...\"  # the {signalKey} in the path\nr = requests.patch(f\"{BASE}/v1/signals/{signal_key}\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"detects\":\"<detects>\"})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]},"delete":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `settings:write`.\n\nThe response shape differs from every other delete in this API — it is a confirmation, not the deleted resource. The `signalKey` becomes immediately reusable in a new `POST /v1/signals` call.","operationId":"deleteSignal","parameters":[{"name":"signalKey","required":true,"in":"path","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Confirmation, not the deleted signal.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/SignalDeleteResultDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`signal_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such signal key, or it is product-managed/person-entity and not addressable here.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Delete a signal","tags":["Signals"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["settings:write"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"# Replace {signalKey} with the real value.\ncurl -X DELETE \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/signals/{signalKey}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nsignal_key = \"...\"  # the {signalKey} in the path\nr = requests.delete(f\"{BASE}/v1/signals/{signal_key}\", headers=HEADERS)\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/discoveries":{"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `events:write`.\n\n**ASYNCHRONOUS.** Returns 202 immediately with a run whose `status` is `running` — nothing has been searched yet. Poll `GET /v1/discoveries/{runId}` until `settledAt` is non-null, then read the events that stand for its scope with `GET /v1/events?discoveryRunId={runId}`. `settledAt` is set when the run is final — searched AND every event written — and `status` reads `completed` or `failed` at the same instant. `candidatesScreened`, `candidatesMatched` and `eventsNew` are frozen execution counters; the scoped event page holds everything this run wrote — including events dated outside the lookback, as a job change dated by its start month can be — plus matching canonical events written by earlier runs.\n\n**Re-running an identical discovery is safe.** Results deduplicate against everything already in the workspace, so the same accounts/signals/lookback typically returns `eventsNew: 0` the second time and creates no duplicate events. That is success.\n\n**Idempotency:** send `Idempotency-Key` on every call you might retry. Repeating the same key with the byte-identical body returns the ORIGINAL run with the same `id`, without starting another search, but with its CURRENT state, not a frozen copy: if the original has since completed, the replay shows `status: completed` and real counts. The same key with a DIFFERENT body is a 409. Keys are not scoped to a time window in this version.\n\n**A 202 does not guarantee events will follow.** If none of the requested accounts are eligible — every account must be assigned to a user, which accounts created via `POST /v1/accounts` always are — the run still returns 202 and then immediately reads `status: completed`, `eventsNew: 0`, with `error` explaining why. This is the single most likely way a first-time caller sees \"no events\": check `error` before assuming discovery is still running or that your signals match nothing.\n\nYou can use new accounts and signal keys immediately. Poll the same run until `settledAt` is set.\n\nPublic REST and MCP usage is recorded without daily usage caps, workspace quota cutoffs or lookup quotas for now. Workspace request pacing still applies. **People:** by default (`people: \"none\"`) a run adds no people to your workspace — its events come back with `people: []`. A `job_change` event still names the person who changed jobs; add them with `POST /v1/people` if you want them. Send `people: \"add\"` to have the people who matter to each event added to your workspace and listed on it.\n\nRead `blockedSignals` before reporting an empty result. These outcomes apply to every signal type, including `news`. While a run is active, keep polling the same run. `account_not_ready` means Trayo could not search the account this time. After the run settles, retry the affected account IDs. `company_not_found` means Trayo could not identify the company from the supplied details. For `company_not_found`, check the named accounts before starting another discovery. If an identity is wrong, send the correct `linkedinHandle` with `trayo_update_account` over MCP, or with `PATCH /v1/accounts/{id}` and a workspace API key over REST. When no handle is known, send a corrected website `url` instead. Both need `accounts:write`. `trayo_update_account` also reports whether Trayo can now identify the company. Importing the same hostname again skips the existing account and does not update it. After the current run settles, start a new discovery for the corrected account IDs.\n\n**Each blocked entry NAMES the accounts** in `accountIds` (the first 200 of them; `accountsAffected` is the true total), so a re-run can be scoped to exactly those rather than everything you sent.","operationId":"startDiscovery","parameters":[{"name":"Idempotency-Key","in":"header","description":"Free-form string. Supported on THIS route only — no other `/v1` route reads it.","required":false,"schema":{"type":"string"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/StartDiscoveryDto"}}}},"responses":{"202":{"description":"Run accepted (or, for a replayed Idempotency-Key, the original run's current state).","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Sent only while the run has not settled: seconds to wait before reading it again, the same value as `progress.retryAfterSeconds`. Absent once `settledAt` is set.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DiscoveryRunDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`unknown_account` (`retry: fix_input`) — One or more `accountIds` do not exist in your workspace. `message` lists them. Create them first or drop them from the request.\n\n`unknown_signal` (`retry: fix_input`) — One or more `signalKeys` do not exist in your workspace. `message` lists them.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"402":{"description":"`quota_exceeded` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — This workspace has insufficient quota for this operation. Retrying or changing the request does not help; raise the quota or wait for it to renew.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"409":{"description":"`idempotency_key_reused` (`retry: fix_input`) — This `Idempotency-Key` was already used with a different request body. Repeating this request unchanged will keep failing; use a new key.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Start a discovery run","tags":["Discoveries"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["events:write"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/discoveries\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"accountIds\":[\"11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111\"],\"lookbackDays\":1}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/discoveries\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"accountIds\":[\"11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111\"],\"lookbackDays\":1})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]},"get":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `events:read`.\n\nEvery run in your workspace, most recently started first. No filter by status or account — pagination only. PAGINATES: follow `nextCursor` until `hasMore` is false.","operationId":"listDiscoveries","parameters":[{"description":"Opaque pagination cursor from a previous page's `nextCursor`. Omit for the first page. Do not construct or parse this value — it is a base64url-encoded implementation detail and may change shape without notice.","required":false,"name":"cursor","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"description":"Page size, default 25. Values above 100 are silently CAPPED to 100, not rejected. Note the deliberate contrast with the two other bounds in this API: `POST /v1/find`'s `limit` is rejected above 100 (and a sentence search returns at most 50), and a `/v1/…/batch` array of more than 200 items is an ERROR rather than a clamp — silently dropping rows would lose records the caller believes it created. A `limit` that is zero, negative or not an integer is rejected here too; only the upper bound clamps.","required":false,"name":"limit","in":"query","schema":{"minimum":1,"maximum":9007199254740991,"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DiscoveryRunListDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.\n\n`malformed_cursor` (`retry: fix_input`) — `cursor` was not a value this API issued. Send a previous page's `nextCursor` verbatim, or omit it to start over.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"List discovery runs","tags":["Discoveries"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["events:read"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/discoveries\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/v1/discoveries\", headers=HEADERS)\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/discoveries/{runId}":{"get":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `events:read`.\n\nTHE POLL. Call this until `settledAt` is non-null, then read the events that stand for the run's scope. `settledAt` and `status: completed` arrive together and mean the run is over in full: searched, and every event it produced written. From that moment the candidate and event counts are frozen and `GET /v1/events?discoveryRunId=` returns the complete scope: everything this run wrote, at any event date, plus the account × signal × lookback matches, including events an earlier run wrote. The counters remain about this execution and are not the size of that page — though a settled run paged to the end yields at least `eventsNew`, which one page need not. The same read before settlement returns what the run has written so far. There is no timer to wait out.\n\nTwo things NOT to poll on. `completedAt` marks only the first half, the search: it can be set while `status` is still `running`, because the events from that search are still being written. And do not watch `eventsNew` stop changing — a pause between two writes looks exactly like the end of a run and is not one. Read `error` even when `status` is `completed`.\n\n**How long to wait.** `progress` says how many accounts are finished and, once there is enough data, `etaSeconds` and `estimatedSettleAt` estimate when the run settles. While the run is unsettled the response carries a `Retry-After` header (and `progress.retryAfterSeconds`): read the run again after that many seconds rather than on a fixed short timer.","operationId":"getDiscovery","parameters":[{"name":"runId","required":true,"in":"path","schema":{"format":"uuid","type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The run's current state. Recomputed on every call while the run is live; served from the run's own frozen receipt once `settledAt` is set.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Sent only while the run has not settled: seconds to wait before reading it again, the same value as `progress.retryAfterSeconds`. Absent once `settledAt` is set.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DiscoveryRunDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`runId` is not a UUID.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`discovery_run_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such run in your workspace.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Get a discovery run","tags":["Discoveries"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["events:read"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"# Replace {runId} with the real value.\ncurl \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/discoveries/{runId}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nrun_id = \"...\"  # the {runId} in the path\nr = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/v1/discoveries/{run_id}\", headers=HEADERS)\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/events":{"get":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `events:read`.\n\nWhat discovery found. Defaults to `state=live` — dismissed events are excluded unless you ask for them explicitly. PAGINATES: follow `nextCursor` until `hasMore` is false.\n\nAfter a discovery run reports `status: completed`, filter by `?discoveryRunId={runId}` to read every event that stands for that run: everything the run wrote, at any `eventDate` — a job change carries the month the job STARTED, which can predate the lookback — plus every event matching its account × signal × lookback scope, including ones written by earlier runs. Paged to the end, a settled run therefore yields at least `eventsNew` events — one page is capped and need not, so follow `nextCursor` before comparing to that counter. Before it settles the same filter returns what the run has written so far; poll `GET /v1/discoveries/{runId}` for the rest. `candidatesScreened` and `eventsNew` remain the execution's frozen counters, not the size of this page.","operationId":"listEvents","parameters":[{"description":"Restrict to events that stand for one discovery run. That is the union of two sets: every event the run itself has written — all of them, whatever their `eventDate`, because a job change is dated by the month the job STARTED and can predate the lookback — and the canonical events that match its accounts, its signals and the event-date window from `startedAt - lookbackDays` through `settledAt`, including ones an earlier run wrote. So the page can be non-empty when the run reports `eventsNew: 0`, and a settled run paged to the end — follow `nextCursor` until `hasMore` is false — yields at least `eventsNew` events, which one page of at most 100 need not; the run counters remain about that execution. Before the run settles this returns what it has written so far — poll for the rest. Additional account, signal, or date filters only narrow this scope. Use the `id` from `POST`/`GET /v1/discoveries`; a run that does not resolve in your workspace is a 404 (`discovery_run_not_found`). One limit worth knowing: the out-of-window half covers what THIS run wrote. An event an earlier run wrote outside this run's window, and that this run merely re-detected, is matched to that earlier row and stays outside — read it by `accountId` and `signalKey` instead.","required":false,"name":"discoveryRunId","in":"query","schema":{"format":"uuid","pattern":"^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$","type":"string"}},{"description":"Restrict to events on one account.","required":false,"name":"accountId","in":"query","schema":{"format":"uuid","pattern":"^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$","type":"string"}},{"description":"Restrict to events matched to this signal.","required":false,"name":"signalKey","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"description":"Restrict to events matched to ANY of these signals — the union, not the intersection. A check of several signals needs one call rather than one per key. Pair it with `discoveredSince` to read events found after your previous check. Send this or `signalKey`, not both.","required":false,"name":"signalKeys","in":"query","schema":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},{"description":"Send a plain date — `2026-06-07`, read as midnight UTC — or a full ISO-8601 timestamp — `2026-06-07T14:30:00Z` — when you need the time of day. **Relative words are not accepted:** `yesterday`, `last-quarter`, `7d` and anything else that has to be resolved against \"now\" is rejected with a 400 (`invalid_date`). Compute the date yourself and send it. Only events that HAPPENED at or after this value — `eventDate`, the date carried by the event itself. Ask it when the age of what happened is what matters to you.\n\n**For events found after your previous check, use `discoveredSince` instead.** An article published last month can reach your workspace today, and this filter will not show it to you.","required":false,"name":"since","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"description":"Send a plain date — `2026-06-07`, read as midnight UTC — or a full ISO-8601 timestamp — `2026-06-07T14:30:00Z` — when you need the time of day. **Relative words are not accepted:** `yesterday`, `last-quarter`, `7d` and anything else that has to be resolved against \"now\" is rejected with a 400 (`invalid_date`). Compute the date yourself and send it. Only events Trayo FOUND at or after this value — `createdAt` on every row, and the order this list already comes back in.\n\n**Use this to read events found since your previous check.** Send the moment you last looked and you get everything new since then, whatever date the events themselves carry — news that happened before the previous check included. `since` answers the other question, when the event happened; send both and an event has to satisfy both.","required":false,"name":"discoveredSince","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"description":"Defaults to `live` — dismissed events are excluded unless you ask for them.\n\n**`dismissed` is Trayo's own verdict,** not yours: an event discovery produced and then withdrew. Nothing a caller does moves an event into it, so it is normally empty for a workspace whose events all come from this API. It stays readable with `?state=dismissed`.\n\n**To dismiss an event yourself, send `DELETE /v1/events/{id}`** — the same action as the dismiss button in the Trayo app. Nothing a discovery run wrote is permanent. An event dismissed that way does **not** turn up under `?state=dismissed`: it leaves both states, its id 404s afterwards, and it stays gone, because discovery deduplicates against every event in the workspace, the ones you dismissed included, so no later run recreates it.\n\nSo the two readable states answer different questions: `live` is what stands, `dismissed` is what Trayo withdrew, and what you dismissed is in neither.","required":false,"name":"state","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"description":"Send `expand=people,signals` to add the `people` and `signals` arrays to every item in `data`. Despite the comma-separated syntax, expansion is currently ALL-OR-NOTHING: any non-empty value — `people` alone, `signals` alone, even `expand=bogus` — expands both fields together. There is no way to request only one. Omit the parameter entirely for the compact form.","required":false,"name":"expand","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"description":"Opaque pagination cursor from a previous page's `nextCursor`. Omit for the first page. Do not construct or parse this value — it is a base64url-encoded implementation detail and may change shape without notice.","required":false,"name":"cursor","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"description":"Page size, default 25. Values above 100 are silently CAPPED to 100, not rejected. Note the deliberate contrast with the two other bounds in this API: `POST /v1/find`'s `limit` is rejected above 100 (and a sentence search returns at most 50), and a `/v1/…/batch` array of more than 200 items is an ERROR rather than a clamp — silently dropping rows would lose records the caller believes it created. A `limit` that is zero, negative or not an integer is rejected here too; only the upper bound clamps.","required":false,"name":"limit","in":"query","schema":{"minimum":1,"maximum":9007199254740991,"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/EventListDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.\n\n`malformed_cursor` (`retry: fix_input`) — `cursor` was not a value this API issued. Send a previous page's `nextCursor` verbatim, or omit it to start over.\n\n`invalid_date` (`retry: fix_input`) — A date filter (`updatedSince`, `since`, `detectedSince`) did not parse. Send a plain date (`2026-06-07`, read as midnight UTC) or a full ISO-8601 timestamp (`2026-06-07T14:30:00Z`). Relative words such as `yesterday` or `last-quarter` are not accepted. `param` names the field.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`discoveryRunId` does not resolve in your workspace.\n\n`discovery_run_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such run in your workspace.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"List events","tags":["Events"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["events:read"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/events\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/v1/events\", headers=HEADERS)\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/events/{id}":{"get":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `events:read`.\n\nAlways returns `people` and `signals` expanded — unlike the list route, there is no `expand` parameter here because it is not needed.","operationId":"getEvent","parameters":[{"name":"id","required":true,"in":"path","schema":{"format":"uuid","type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The event, always expanded.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/EventDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`id` is not a UUID.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"No such event, it belongs to another workspace, or it exists but has not become available yet. All three are indistinguishable.\n\n`event_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such event in your workspace, or it has not finished processing and is not addressable yet.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Get an event","tags":["Events"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["events:read"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"# Replace {id} with the real value.\ncurl \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/events/{id}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nid = \"...\"  # the {id} in the path\nr = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/v1/events/{id}\", headers=HEADERS)\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]},"delete":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `events:write`.\n\nSoft delete — the same action as dismissing the event in the Trayo app. Returns 200, not 204, with the event as it was, exactly like the other delete routes here; the proof is behavioral: this id now 404s and the event no longer appears in `GET /v1/events` under any `state`.\n\n**It stays deleted.** Discovery deduplicates against every event in the workspace, deleted ones included, so a later run does not recreate it. Use this to tell Trayo an event was wrong or irrelevant; an event you merely ignore keeps counting toward the account's `scores`.\n\n**Not the same as `state: dismissed`.** That state means Trayo withdrew the event. It is still readable with `?state=dismissed`. A delete is yours, and is not readable afterwards.","operationId":"deleteEvent","parameters":[{"name":"id","required":true,"in":"path","schema":{"format":"uuid","type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The event as it existed immediately before deletion.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/EventDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`id` is not a UUID.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"No such event, it belongs to another workspace, it was already deleted, or it has not reached a public state yet. All four are indistinguishable.\n\n`event_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such event in your workspace, or it has not finished processing and is not addressable yet.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Delete (dismiss) an event","tags":["Events"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["events:write"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"# Replace {id} with the real value.\ncurl -X DELETE \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/events/{id}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nid = \"...\"  # the {id} in the path\nr = requests.delete(f\"{BASE}/v1/events/{id}\", headers=HEADERS)\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/people":{"get":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `people:read`.\n\nA page of people, most recently created first. PAGINATES: follow `nextCursor` until `hasMore` is false.\n\n**Why each person matters is behind `?expand=`.** Send `?expand=stakeholderReport,events` to add both `stakeholderReport` — the generated report on the person, the same one the Trayo app shows — and `events`, the events they are attached to with the per-event reasoning. Without the parameter neither KEY is present (absent, not `null` and not `[]`), because a page of 50 reports is a large response for a call that only wanted names. `GET /v1/people/{id}` always includes both.","operationId":"listPeople","parameters":[{"description":"Restrict to people linked to this account. An `accountId` that does not exist, or belongs to another workspace, is not an error — it simply matches no rows.","required":false,"name":"accountId","in":"query","schema":{"format":"uuid","pattern":"^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$","type":"string"}},{"description":"Case-insensitive substring match against `fullName` only — does not search `title`, `email`, or anything else.","required":false,"name":"q","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"description":"Send the literal string `true` or `false`. `true` returns only people whose `email` comes back non-null, `false` only those whose does not. Omit the parameter to return people regardless. Any other value is rejected rather than guessed at.\n\nIt filters on the SAME `email` the response publishes, from either source: an address you wrote (`emailSource: \"manual\"`) or one a lookup found and still considers deliverable (`emailSource: \"enrichment\"`). So `POST /v1/people/{id}/enrich` finding an address moves that person from `?hasEmail=false` to `?hasEmail=true`. A found address that later bounced, or a lookup that is still running, found nothing, or went stale, leaves `email` null and the person on the `false` side — the two sides always partition the workspace, never overlap.","required":false,"name":"hasEmail","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"description":"Filter on the derived `isRepVisible` flag. Same parsing as `hasEmail`, but NOT the same idea — the two sit next to each other and are unrelated.\n\n**Omit it to list both values.** `?isRepVisible=true` lists people somebody added or Trayo attached to an event. `?isRepVisible=false` lists profiles Trayo collected while searching but never surfaced. Adding one of those with `POST /v1/people` moves it to the `true` side. See the field's own description on `PersonDto`.","required":false,"name":"isRepVisible","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"description":"Send a plain date — `2026-06-07`, read as midnight UTC — or a full ISO-8601 timestamp — `2026-06-07T14:30:00Z` — when you need the time of day. **Relative words are not accepted:** `yesterday`, `last-quarter`, `7d` and anything else that has to be resolved against \"now\" is rejected with a 400 (`invalid_date`). Compute the date yourself and send it. Returns people with `updatedAt >=` this value.\n\nA contact lookup counts as an update: when a lookup finishes for a person — whether it found an `email` or `phone`, found nothing, or a previously found address bounced — that person's `updatedAt` moves. A sweep that polls this parameter on a schedule therefore sees contact details that arrived since its last run, not only edits made through the API.","required":false,"name":"updatedSince","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"description":"Send `expand=stakeholderReport,events` to add the `stakeholderReport` and `events` fields to every item in `data`. Despite the comma-separated syntax, expansion is ALL-OR-NOTHING: any non-empty value — `events` alone, even `expand=bogus` — expands both fields together. There is no way to request only one. Omit the parameter entirely for the compact form, which omits both KEYS rather than sending them empty.\n\nBoth are heavy — a whole markdown report and a join across every event a person is attached to — which is why they are behind this parameter here and unconditional on `GET /v1/people/{id}`.","required":false,"name":"expand","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"description":"Only people who say on their LinkedIn profile that they are in this city, e.g. `San Diego`. Case-insensitive, whole name. A person whose profile names only a metro area (`Greater San Diego Area`) also matches when that text contains the city. This is where the person is, not where their account is headquartered; see the person's `location`.","required":false,"name":"residenceCity","in":"query","schema":{"minLength":1,"maxLength":100,"type":"string"}},{"description":"Only people whose stated LinkedIn location is in this state, province or region, e.g. `California`. Case-insensitive, whole name.","required":false,"name":"residenceState","in":"query","schema":{"minLength":1,"maxLength":100,"type":"string"}},{"description":"Only people whose stated LinkedIn location is in this country: an ISO-2 code (`US`) or a country name (`United States`), any case. A name is read as its ISO-2 code.","required":false,"name":"residenceCountry","in":"query","schema":{"minLength":2,"maxLength":80,"type":"string"}},{"description":"Opaque pagination cursor from a previous page's `nextCursor`. Omit for the first page. Do not construct or parse this value — it is a base64url-encoded implementation detail and may change shape without notice.","required":false,"name":"cursor","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"description":"Page size, default 25. Values above 100 are silently CAPPED to 100, not rejected. Note the deliberate contrast with the two other bounds in this API: `POST /v1/find`'s `limit` is rejected above 100 (and a sentence search returns at most 50), and a `/v1/…/batch` array of more than 200 items is an ERROR rather than a clamp — silently dropping rows would lose records the caller believes it created. A `limit` that is zero, negative or not an integer is rejected here too; only the upper bound clamps.","required":false,"name":"limit","in":"query","schema":{"minimum":1,"maximum":9007199254740991,"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PersonListDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.\n\n`malformed_cursor` (`retry: fix_input`) — `cursor` was not a value this API issued. Send a previous page's `nextCursor` verbatim, or omit it to start over.\n\n`invalid_date` (`retry: fix_input`) — A date filter (`updatedSince`, `since`, `detectedSince`) did not parse. Send a plain date (`2026-06-07`, read as midnight UTC) or a full ISO-8601 timestamp (`2026-06-07T14:30:00Z`). Relative words such as `yesterday` or `last-quarter` are not accepted. `param` names the field.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"List people","tags":["People"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["people:read"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/people\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/v1/people\", headers=HEADERS)\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]},"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `people:write`.\n\n**A person is a name, a title, a note, an email, a LinkedIn username and a photo URL. That is the whole record you can WRITE.** Phone numbers are only ever found: `POST /v1/people/{id}/enrich` looks up an email and/or a phone and the results appear on the person as `email` (with `emailSource: \"enrichment\"`) and `phone`.\n\n**`note` is where sourcing and confidence go.** It is free text you own — up to 1000 characters, no structure imposed, stored and returned verbatim and NEVER interpreted by Trayo: not parsed, not indexed, not searchable, not shown in the Trayo UI, and nothing in the product branches on it. `\"sourced from LinkedIn, unverified, 2026-09-02\"` is exactly the intended use. Set it here, change or clear it with `PATCH /v1/people/{id}`, read it back on every people route.\n\n**Do not put any of that in `title`.** `title` is the job title, it is published, and humans and downstream systems read it as a job title — so a value like `\"VP Sales (UNVERIFIED, sourced from LinkedIn)\"` is a wrong job title for every reader of it, not an annotated one. That workaround is why `note` exists.\n\n**LinkedIn and email are upsert keys.** A create that matches an existing person on either key updates that row with the fields you sent, makes it rep-visible, returns its existing `id`, and answers `200`. A new person answers `201`. WHERE Trayo looks depends on what you sent: with an `accountId` or a `company`, within THAT account only — the same human under two accounts (an advisor, a dual role) is two records and both are created. With neither, across your whole workspace, because you asked \"do you have this person\" and the answer must not depend on which account Trayo happens to attach them to. A person with neither key can never upsert. If LinkedIn and email point at two different people, the request is a `409` rather than merging those identities.\n\n**`linkedinUrl` is a source for `linkedinUsername`, not a decoration.** Send either. With no `linkedinUsername`, the username is taken from the URL and stored, so a `POST /v1/find` contacts row keeps its LinkedIn identity when posted verbatim. A `linkedinUsername` you send always wins over the URL.\n\n**For a new person, a LinkedIn identity also FILLS the fields you left empty.** A new row carrying one is looked up in Trayo's own profile mirror, and whatever it finds is used for `title` and `photoUrl` when you sent neither, and for the account link when you sent neither `accountId` nor `company` — so the response can carry a `title`, a `profileImageUrl` and an `accountId` you never supplied, and a company Trayo does not already have becomes a NEW account under the same name-only rule below. It never overwrites a value you DID send, and it is best-effort: a lookup that misses or takes too long creates the row exactly as you sent it rather than failing it. Supply the fields yourself to keep control of them; there is no other way to opt out. A strong-key upsert writes only fields you sent; it never copies these profile values onto the match.\n\nNote `isRepVisible` on the response: it comes back `true`. Creating a person here counts as a deliberate human add, the same as adding one by hand in the app, so the record surfaces to reps. You cannot send the field and you cannot turn it off.\n\n`accountId` and `company` are mutually exclusive ways to link the new person to an account — send at most one, or neither to create an unlinked person.\n\n**Company auto-link.** `company: { name }` finds-or-creates the linked account by `name`, case-insensitive, within your workspace. A match reuses the existing account and `company.domain` is ignored. `company.domain` takes a bare host or a full website URL; the account is created at `https://<host>` either way, and a value that is not a usable hostname is refused — `validation_failed`, `param: \"company.domain\"`.\n\nA company that does NOT already exist is created anyway — with an empty `url` when you sent no `company.domain`, so a name-only row still gets an account rather than being refused. Supply `company.domain` when you have one so the new account gets a real url. Look up whether an account already exists, and get its `id` for the `accountId` route, with `GET /v1/accounts?q=<company name>`.","operationId":"createPerson","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/CreatePersonDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Existing person updated.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PersonDto"}}}},"201":{"description":"Person created.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PersonDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`validation_failed` covers a malformed body and `accountId` and `company` both present (`param: \"company\"`). `unknown_account` (`param: \"accountId\"`) means the `accountId` does not resolve — another workspace's account is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.\n\n`unknown_account` (`retry: fix_input`) — One or more `accountIds` do not exist in your workspace. `message` lists them. Create them first or drop them from the request.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"409":{"description":"The LinkedIn identity and email match different existing people. Send one identity, or PATCH the intended record explicitly.\n\n`conflict` (`retry: fix_input`) — The generic 409: the request collides with existing state, and none of the specific codes covers it. `message` says what.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Create a person","tags":["People"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["people:write"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/people\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"fullName\":\"<fullName>\"}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/people\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"fullName\":\"<fullName>\"})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/people/batch":{"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `people:write`.\n\nCreate up to 200 people in one call — the import path for bulk results (e.g. from `POST /v1/find`). A row is the same body as `POST /v1/people`, `note` included, so per-row sourcing (\"found by search X, unverified\") travels with the import instead of being flattened into `title`. Each row supports the same `accountId`/`company` auto-link as `POST /v1/people`, INCLUDING minting an account from a company name with no `domain`. That is the common case when piping the find contacts lane straight in here: those rows carry a company name and no domain, and each one now lands in an account rather than in `skipped`.\n\n**Every new row is enriched from its LinkedIn identity**, exactly as on `POST /v1/people`: a new row that carries a `linkedinUrl` or `linkedinUsername` and leaves `title`, `photoUrl` or the account link empty has them filled from the profile Trayo has on file, and can land in an account it never named. Values you send are never overwritten, and a lookup that misses or runs long costs the row nothing. Strong-key upserts write only fields the row sent; they never copy these profile values onto the match.\n\n**Partial success is the contract.** A malformed row, a row whose `accountId`/`company` cannot be resolved, or a name-only row that collides with another row in the SAME batch or with a person you already have, is reported in `skipped` by its 0-based index and a reason — never as a request error. This response is always `200`, even if every row was skipped. An array over the 200-item cap ERRORS rather than clamping.\n\n**Sending the same batch twice creates nothing the second time.** The same `linkedinUsername` or `email` (case-insensitive) updates the existing row with the fields this row sent. Those rows are returned in `updated`, with their submitted `index`; `created` contains new records only. Inside an account, a match on `fullName` alone is not safe enough to merge, so it stays in `skipped` as a duplicate and nothing is changed. The scope is the same rule as `POST /v1/people`: within the account the row NAMED (`accountId` or `company`), or across the whole workspace for a row that named neither. Name-only duplicates carry `reasonCode: \"duplicate\"` and `existingId`. Strong-key updates work for visible and hidden profiles alike and make the record rep-visible. If LinkedIn and email point at different existing people, the row is skipped with `reasonCode: \"identity_conflict\"` instead of fusing those identities. Send one identity, or PATCH the intended record explicitly. The same person under two DIFFERENT accounts you named is two records and both are created; a row with no account and neither a LinkedIn nor an email has nothing to match on and is always created.\n\n**`fullName` is the third key, and it is BATCH-ONLY.** It applies only to a row that resolves to an account — an `accountId`, or a `company` that matched one you already have. Two people at ONE company sharing a full name is rare enough to be worth catching, whereas a bare name across a whole workspace collides too often to dedup on, so a row with no account is still matched on `linkedinUsername`/`email` alone and is created when it has neither. `fullName` is required, so a row that DOES name an account always carries this key: such a row can come back as a duplicate even when its `email` or `linkedinUsername` is one you have never seen. Read `existingId` before assuming the two rows are the same person. A single `POST /v1/people` never applies this key and still `201`s on a name that already exists.\n\n**`linkedinUrl` carries identity here too.** A row with no `linkedinUsername` takes one from `linkedinUrl`, and that derived username is both what is stored and what the row is deduplicated on — so a `POST /v1/find` contacts import is idempotent on replay rather than landing a fresh copy of every contact.\n\n**It is still best-effort, and here is the edge.** The check happens in APPLICATION CODE, the same posture as `POST /v1/accounts/batch` and for the same reason: no unique database index backs it. Two batches running CONCURRENTLY can both pass the check for the same person before either has committed, and both create one. Serialize your batch calls if you cannot tolerate that.","operationId":"batchCreatePeople","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BatchCreatePeopleDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The request was processed. Check `skipped` — a `200` does not mean every row was created or updated; it means the call itself succeeded. Read `created` for new records and `updated` for strong-key upserts. Then check `degraded`: those rows WERE created, but without an account (`no_account`) and/or without a LinkedIn/email identity (`no_identity`), and a row with no identity is one a replay of this batch will create again.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BatchCreatePeopleResultDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"The request itself is malformed: `people` is missing, not an array, or has more than 200 items (`param: \"people\"`). A malformed INDIVIDUAL row, or one whose `accountId`/`company` cannot be resolved, never produces this status — it is reported in the `200` response's `skipped` instead.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Batch create people","tags":["People"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["people:write"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/people/batch\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"people\":[\"<people>\"]}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/people/batch\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"people\":[\"<people>\"]})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/people/{id}":{"get":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `people:read`.\n\nAlways returns `stakeholderReport` and `events` — unlike the list route, there is no `expand` parameter here because it is not needed.\n\nThose two are where \"why does this person matter?\" is answered. `stakeholderReport` is the generated report on the person, the same one the Trayo app shows, and is `null` until stakeholder research has run for them. `events` lists what they were attached to and, per event, why they were named on it.","operationId":"getPerson","parameters":[{"name":"id","required":true,"in":"path","schema":{"format":"uuid","type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The person, always expanded.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PersonDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`id` is not a UUID.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"No such person, OR it belongs to another workspace — the two are indistinguishable on purpose.\n\n`person_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such person in your workspace. Another workspace's person is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Get a person","tags":["People"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["people:read"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"# Replace {id} with the real value.\ncurl \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/people/{id}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nid = \"...\"  # the {id} in the path\nr = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/v1/people/{id}\", headers=HEADERS)\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]},"patch":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `people:write`.\n\nOnly the fields present in the body change; everything else is left alone.\n\n**`note` is yours to rewrite.** Send a string to replace it (there is no append), send `null` to clear it, omit it to leave it untouched. It is stored and returned verbatim and never interpreted by Trayo, which is what makes it the right home for sourcing, confidence and \"unverified\" — `title` is the published job title and is the wrong place for any of that.","operationId":"updatePerson","parameters":[{"name":"id","required":true,"in":"path","schema":{"format":"uuid","type":"string"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/UpdatePersonDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The person after the update.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PersonDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"Malformed body, e.g. `email` not a valid address.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`person_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such person in your workspace. Another workspace's person is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Update a person","tags":["People"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["people:write"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"# Replace {id} with the real value.\ncurl -X PATCH \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/people/{id}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"fullName\":\"<fullName>\"}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nid = \"...\"  # the {id} in the path\nr = requests.patch(f\"{BASE}/v1/people/{id}\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"fullName\":\"<fullName>\"})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]},"delete":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `people:delete`.\n\nSoft delete. Returns 200, not 204, with the person as it was — nothing in the response body distinguishes it from a normal GET, and there is no `deletedAt` field in this API's Person shape. The proof of deletion is behavioral: this id now 404s on every route and no longer appears in `GET /v1/people`.","operationId":"deletePerson","parameters":[{"name":"id","required":true,"in":"path","schema":{"format":"uuid","type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The person as it existed immediately before deletion.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PersonDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`id` is not a UUID.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`person_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such person in your workspace. Another workspace's person is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Delete a person","tags":["People"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["people:delete"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"# Replace {id} with the real value.\ncurl -X DELETE \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/people/{id}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nid = \"...\"  # the {id} in the path\nr = requests.delete(f\"{BASE}/v1/people/{id}\", headers=HEADERS)\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/people/enrich/batch":{"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `body.fields` includes `email`: `people:enrich_email`; `body.fields` includes `phone`: `people:enrich_phone`. All scopes for the selected fields are required. Omitting `body.fields` uses `[\"email\",\"phone\"]` and requires `people:enrich_email` and `people:enrich_phone`. Malformed values: no additional scopes; unknown fields add no scopes. Request validation still applies.\n\nStart lookups for up to 200 people in one call, with the same rules as the single route applied per person. Partial success is the contract: a person who exists gets an outcome in `accepted` even if every field was skipped; an id that is unknown, another workspace's, or a duplicate earlier in the batch lands in `skipped` by index.\n\n**This route always answers `200`, never `202` or `402`.** A workspace allowance stop — the plan lookup limit, the workspace quota, or the daily usage limit — is reported per person rather than raised: people reached before the stop are looked up and charged, and the person that hit it and every person after it are reported in `skipped` with the limit as the reason. Nothing after the limit is partially run. `stoppedBy` says so as data: which allowance, how many people were processed and how many were not looked up.\n\n**The batch has a 45s budget for starting lookups.** The whole batch starts together and normally takes a few seconds. The budget is checked once, before anything is reserved: if it has run out, the first person who needed a lookup and every person after are reported in `skipped` with a reason saying the call ran out of time. Nothing was started for them and nothing was spent, so send those ids again in smaller batches. Retain this request's `personIds` array and map `skipped[].index` back to it. Only re-send time-skipped rows this way: other rows in `skipped` may be duplicates, invalid ids, or allowance refusals that need a different remedy. Poll already-started lookups with `GET /v1/people/{id}/enrich`. If a retry makes no progress, stop and keep the unresolved ids for later.\n\n**A lookup is explicit, asynchronous, idempotent, and governed by your plan.** Nothing is looked up on create or on read; this call is the only trigger, and it reports what it started and what it SKIPPED — a field already in progress, already found, blocked by a written email, or inside its retry cooldown is skipped with the reason, never an error — so sending it twice never double-runs or is charged twice. Poll `GET /v1/people/{id}/enrich` (or read the person) for the result; a lookup takes seconds to a minute.\n\n**Provenance is kept.** A found value carries `source`, `status` and `foundAt`; a value you wrote is `source: \"manual\"` and is never overwritten by a found one — the email lookup is not even attempted while one is present.\n\n**Plan limits are checked BEFORE anything runs.** Each lookup that starts counts once against a lifetime plan limit. Every response carries `quota` — `limit`, `used` and `remaining` per field, as they stand after the call, the same numbers `GET /v1/whoami` reports — so size each request by `quota.<field>.remaining` rather than learning the limit from a refusal.","operationId":"batchEnrichPeople","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BatchEnrichBodyDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The batch was processed. Check `skipped` — a `200` does not mean a lookup started for every person.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BatchEnrichResultDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"The ENVELOPE was wrong: `personIds` missing, empty, over 200, not UUIDs, or an unknown `fields` entry. A problem with one PERSON never produces this status — it is reported in the `200` response's `skipped`.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Look up emails and phones for many people","tags":["People"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"contact-fields","parameter":"body.fields","combine":"union","cases":{"email":["people:enrich_email"],"phone":["people:enrich_phone"]},"defaultFields":["email","phone"],"omitted":["people:enrich_email","people:enrich_phone"],"malformed":[]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/people/enrich/batch\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"personIds\":[\"11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111\"]}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/people/enrich/batch\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"personIds\":[\"11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111\"]})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/people/{id}/enrich":{"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `body.fields` includes `email`: `people:enrich_email`; `body.fields` includes `phone`: `people:enrich_phone`. All scopes for the selected fields are required. Omitting `body.fields` uses `[\"email\",\"phone\"]` and requires `people:enrich_email` and `people:enrich_phone`. Malformed values: no additional scopes; unknown fields add no scopes. Request validation still applies.\n\nFind this person's email and/or phone the same way the Trayo app's own \"Find email\" does. Omit `fields` for both.\n\n**It returns `202` at once** with what it started and what it skipped. Over the plan limit, or on a plan with no such lookups, the call is `402 lookup_limit_reached`: nothing was started and nothing was charged.\n\n**A lookup is explicit, asynchronous, idempotent, and governed by your plan.** Nothing is looked up on create or on read; this call is the only trigger, and it reports what it started and what it SKIPPED — a field already in progress, already found, blocked by a written email, or inside its retry cooldown is skipped with the reason, never an error — so sending it twice never double-runs or is charged twice. Poll `GET /v1/people/{id}/enrich` (or read the person) for the result; a lookup takes seconds to a minute.\n\n**Provenance is kept.** A found value carries `source`, `status` and `foundAt`; a value you wrote is `source: \"manual\"` and is never overwritten by a found one — the email lookup is not even attempted while one is present.\n\n**Plan limits are checked BEFORE anything runs.** Each lookup that starts counts once against a lifetime plan limit. Every response carries `quota` — `limit`, `used` and `remaining` per field, as they stand after the call, the same numbers `GET /v1/whoami` reports — so size each request by `quota.<field>.remaining` rather than learning the limit from a refusal.","operationId":"enrichPerson","parameters":[{"name":"id","required":true,"in":"path","schema":{"format":"uuid","type":"string"}}],"requestBody":{"required":false,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/EnrichPersonBodyDto"}}}},"responses":{"202":{"description":"Accepted. `started` lists the lookups this call started; `skipped` lists the ones it did not and why; `contact` is the state right now; `quota` is the lookup allowance left after this call.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/EnrichPersonResultDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`id` is not a UUID, or `fields` names something other than `email`/`phone`.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"402":{"description":"`lookup_limit_reached` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — This workspace cannot run this contact lookup: the plan's email or phone lookup limit is reached, or the plan does not include that kind of lookup. `message` says which and quotes the limit. Retrying never helps and neither does changing the request — the plan has to change. Nothing was started and nothing was charged.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`person_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such person in your workspace. Another workspace's person is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"503":{"description":"`lookup_start_failed` (`retry: retry_later`) — The contact lookup passed every check but could not be started. No lookup is running for it, and a retry of the same request is not charged twice. Send it again shortly.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Look up an email and/or phone","tags":["People"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"contact-fields","parameter":"body.fields","combine":"union","cases":{"email":["people:enrich_email"],"phone":["people:enrich_phone"]},"defaultFields":["email","phone"],"omitted":["people:enrich_email","people:enrich_phone"],"malformed":[]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"# Replace {id} with the real value.\ncurl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/people/{id}/enrich\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"fields\":[\"email\"]}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nid = \"...\"  # the {id} in the path\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/people/{id}/enrich\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"fields\":[\"email\"]})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]},"get":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `people:read`.\n\nThe full contact picture for a person: the email and phone to use, where each came from, and the state of the lookup behind each. This is the poll target after `POST /v1/people/{id}/enrich`: a field reads `in_progress` until its lookup finishes, then `found` or `not_found` (with `retryAvailableAt`). Free; nothing is started by reading.","operationId":"getPersonContact","parameters":[{"name":"id","required":true,"in":"path","schema":{"format":"uuid","type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ContactStatusDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`id` is not a UUID.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`person_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such person in your workspace. Another workspace's person is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Read the contact lookup state","tags":["People"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["people:read"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"# Replace {id} with the real value.\ncurl \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/people/{id}/enrich\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nid = \"...\"  # the {id} in the path\nr = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/v1/people/{id}/enrich\", headers=HEADERS)\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/people/{id}/ask":{"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `people:read`.\n\n**Derived-context capability: people:read includes derived briefing context.** For this operation, that scope permits the person record, stored contacts, notes, list membership, synthesis and stakeholder reports, the linked account and its stored research, attached events and rationale, sequences and outcomes, sent emails, composed messages, the LinkedIn profile and posts, and workspace solution and stakeholder criteria. Answers may include facts from this derived context. No additional source scopes are required here, including when the owner role grants only people:read. The key and its owner's current workspace role must both allow people:read. Losing unrelated owner permissions does not block this operation. GET /v1/whoami reports the key's current effective scopes in key.effectiveScopes. Direct account and workspace reads still require accounts:read, and direct event reads events:read. This capability grants no writes or new research. Sources remain limited to the existing person dossier and workspace context; the receipt describes which records informed the answer, subject to existing limits.\n\nAsk anything about one person and get an answer grounded in everything Trayo holds on them. **Synchronous and read-only**: the answer comes back in one response, typically in 5–15 seconds (the server gives up at 25 with `503 person_ask_failed`, so set your client timeout above that and retry once on `retry_later`). The answer is not saved. Public REST and MCP usage is recorded without daily usage caps, workspace quota cutoffs or lookup quotas for now. Workspace request pacing still applies. **What goes into the answer.** Two kinds of source, rendered into one dossier with sane limits: the person's **Trayo record** — the contact details on record, the account and its research, the signals (events) the person is attached to and Trayo's reason for each, every sequence composed for them with each step's send/open/reply outcome, emails sent, messages composed, lists, any stored synthesis or stakeholder report, and the `note` you wrote — plus the **LinkedIn profile** from Trayo's own data: headline, about, work history with dates, and the person's recent posts.\n\n**`intent` steers the answer.** Say what you will do with it — \"qualifying whether to sequence them, I need a verdict and the reason\", \"drafting a first email, I need hooks I can cite\", \"briefing a rep before a call\" — and the focus, depth and form follow. Without it you get a direct, concise answer.\n\n**No confidence score is returned — read `sources` to see what the answer is grounded in.** It is a receipt of the records used: how many signals, whether any outreach exists, whether the LinkedIn profile was found. `sources.linkedin.status` is `not_linked` when the person has no LinkedIn identity in Trayo (set `linkedinUsername` with `PATCH /v1/people/{id}` and ask again), `not_found` when Trayo has no record for that profile, and `unavailable` when that data could not be reached this time — the answer then rests on the Trayo record alone. `gaps` names what was missing.\n\n**Grounded, not researched.** Trayo answers from these records only: no web search, no guessing. A fact that is not on record is named as unknown. To put more on record first: `POST /v1/people/{id}/enrich` finds an email or phone, and `POST /v1/discoveries` puts events and the people attached to them on the account's record.","operationId":"askPerson","parameters":[{"name":"id","required":true,"in":"path","schema":{"format":"uuid","type":"string"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AskPersonBodyDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The answer, what was missing from the record (`gaps`), and a receipt of the records used (`sources`).","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AskPersonResponseDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`id` is not a UUID; `question` missing, blank, or over 2000 characters; `intent` blank or over 2000 characters; or an unknown field. `param` names it.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"402":{"description":"`quota_exceeded` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — This workspace has insufficient quota for this operation. Retrying or changing the request does not help; raise the quota or wait for it to renew.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`person_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such person in your workspace. Another workspace's person is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.\n\n`quota_daily_limit` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace daily usage limit blocks new work. Wait for recent usage to leave the 24-hour window, or contact support; changing scopes does not help.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"503":{"description":"`person_ask_not_configured` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Questions about a person are unavailable. Retrying will not help. Contact support. To read the saved person record, use `GET /v1/people/{id}`.\n\n`person_ask_failed` (`retry: retry_later`) — The answer failed, came back unusable, or ran past the time budget. Nothing was written. Send the same request again shortly. A LinkedIn-profile failure is NOT this error: the answer proceeds on the Trayo record and `sources.linkedin.status` says `unavailable`.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Ask a question about a person","tags":["People"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["people:read"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"# Replace {id} with the real value.\ncurl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/people/{id}/ask\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"question\":\"<question>\"}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nid = \"...\"  # the {id} in the path\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/people/{id}/ask\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"question\":\"<question>\"})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/find":{"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `body.target` equals `people`: `people:read`; `body.target` equals `companies`: `accounts:read`. Other or missing values: no additional scopes; request validation still applies.\n\nSearch for companies and people you do not already have. It never writes: you get candidates, and you import the ones you want.\n\n**For explicit criteria, use `mode: direct` with `filters`.** Reads stored company and people records with no sentence interpretation or external search. `query` is rejected. Each call returns one page of at most 100 records; follow `nextCursor` to continue. Company records without websites are kept and can be read again by `filters.companyIds`. A direct companies search can combine company criteria with `filters.title` to return companies with a matching current employee, once per company. People results include their matching current company. A company reaching `perCompany` sets `truncated: true` with a note because additional matching people may exist. Omitting mode preserves the usual search behavior below.\n\n**Say what you want in one of two ways, or both.**\n\n- `query` — a sentence. Trayo interprets it and ranks results by relevance. `interpreted` in the response tells you what it read out of the sentence, in the same `filters` shape you can send back. One ranked page of at most 50; no cursor.\n- `filters` — exact attributes: industry, headcount, headquarters, funding stage, founded year, technologies, legal form, and for people a title. Applied exactly as sent, never interpreted, never fail-open: a company with no value for a filtered attribute is excluded. Paginated. A companies search without a title can use only country, founded year, technology or company type: it checks a bounded set of the largest companies and reports `led_by_headcount`, so its matches are not exhaustive. A people search or a company search with a title needs named companies or `industries`, `hq.cities`, `hq.states` or a `headcount` band. Funding stage alone also needs one of those indexed filters. Read `GET /v1/find/industries` before your first industry filter, because the values are a closed taxonomy.\n- both — the sentence ranks, the filters decide. Rows Trayo cannot check are dropped.\n\n**`target: people` returns people with their current company.** `\"founders at seed-stage software companies\"` is `{\"target\": \"people\", \"filters\": {\"industries\": [\"software development\"], \"fundingStages\": [\"seed\"], \"title\": {\"any\": [\"founder\"]}}}`. Company filters describe the employer; `title` describes the person. With a `query`, a people search takes `title` only.\n\n**Searching inside companies you already know.** Name them instead of describing them: `filters.companyWebsites` takes their websites (`[\"stripe.com\", \"https://www.acme.example\"]`), the form you already have without asking this API for anything. It replaces every other company filter, and takes no `query` beside it. (`filters.companyIds`, which takes an `id` a previous search returned, is the older form of the same thing and replaces it in turn; websites are what to reach for.) Each website resolves to at most one company, and `resolvedWebsites` in the response says which: several company profiles can share a domain, so a website resolves only to a profile whose name matches the domain; check it before trusting the page. A website that does not resolve is left out of the search and listed in `unresolvedWebsites`, never dropped without saying so: the page covers only the websites in `resolvedWebsites`. `reason: \"not_found\"` means no company on that domain: fix the spelling, send the company's own domain, or describe that company with filters in a separate search. `reason: \"uncertain\"` means the domain carries several possible companies and none clearly owns it; its `alternatives` list them (id, name, headcount). Show them to the user, or search again with `filters.companyIds` set to the right alternative's id. When no website resolves at all, the answer is a `404 company_not_found` naming them.\n\n**Reading the response.** `data` holds one row shape per target. `hasMore`/`nextCursor` page a filters-only search. `truncated` means more matched than this search can show — narrow, do not page deeper. `known: false` on a company means the sentence search found something Trayo does not hold. `state: alreadyAdded` means it is in your workspace; for \"find N new companies\", send `filters.excludeWorkspace: true` and those rows are left out, so the page fills with companies you do not have.\n\n**Before re-running a thin search, read `interpreted`, `truncated` and `degraded`.** They say whether your criteria were enforced, whether the set is larger than reachable, and whether the search was incomplete — and a search that ran counts against the quota whether or not it was useful. Outside direct mode, every company row carries a `url`: rows with no website are dropped before the page is filled and counted in `droppedUnaddressable`, because `POST /v1/accounts` could not import them.\n\n**Importing.** Companies: `POST /v1/accounts/batch` with `{name, url}` from each row (`url` is ready to send). People: `POST /v1/people/batch` with `{fullName, title, linkedinUrl}`; the company links by website when known. Contact details are a separate step: `POST /v1/contacts/lookup` with the `linkedinUrl`.\n\n`target: companies` needs the `accounts:read` scope, `target: people` needs `people:read`. A search with a `query` draws on the workspace's search quota when it runs; a filters-only search does not.","operationId":"find","parameters":[{"name":"idempotency-key","required":false,"in":"header","description":"For searches with a query, replay the saved response without repeating the search. Reuse only with the same request body. Filters-only searches do not use this key.","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FindRequestDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The search ran. An empty `data` array is a successful search that matched nothing — check `truncated`, `degraded` and `interpreted` before retrying.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FindResponseDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"Neither `query` nor `filters` was sent, a field is malformed or outside its closed set, a band is inverted, a people-only field was sent for companies, a cursor was sent with a query, or a filters-only search named no usable company filter, or requested a title or funding stage without an indexed company lead.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.\n\n`find_needs_indexed_filter` (`retry: fix_input`) — This filters-only search needs an indexed company lead. A people search or company search with a title cannot use country, founded year, technologies or company type alone; funding stage also needs an indexed lead. A company search without a title can use those filters alone, but checks only a bounded set of the largest companies (`led_by_headcount`). Add at least one of `filters.industries` (see `GET /v1/find/industries`), `filters.hq.cities`, `filters.hq.states` or a `filters.headcount` band, or send a `query` and let the sentence select the set. With no company criteria in the request, do not ask the user: read `buyerProfile` from `GET /v1/workspace`, map its industries to exact `GET /v1/find/industries` values for `filters.industries`, and send its `sizeBand` (max capped at 50,000) as `filters.headcount` when `buyerProfileSource` is `saved`. With a partial profile, no mapped industry or no profile, send `{\"min\": 1, \"max\": 10000}`, never `{\"min\": 1}` alone.\n\n`malformed_cursor` (`retry: fix_input`) — `cursor` was not a value this API issued. Send a previous page's `nextCursor` verbatim, or omit it to start over.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"402":{"description":"`quota_exceeded` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — This workspace has insufficient quota for this operation. Retrying or changing the request does not help; raise the quota or wait for it to renew.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"Trayo could not identify a company for any `filters.companyWebsites` value, so there was nothing to search. The message names the websites; for an ambiguous one it also names the candidate companies with their ids, to send back as `filters.companyIds`. When only SOME websites fail to resolve, the search runs over the rest and the ones left out are listed in `unresolvedWebsites` instead.\n\n`company_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — We could not identify this company — not from the account's own record, nor from a LinkedIn page, website (including its redirect), or name — so there are no people to search. Retrying will not help. Send the company's own website if you did not; for any company, `POST /v1/find` on the contacts lane searches the web instead. From `POST /v1/find` with `filters.companyWebsites`, this means NO website resolved and nothing was searched; the message names every website. For one that is ambiguous (several possible companies on the domain) it also names the candidates and their ids: send the right id as `filters.companyIds`. When only some websites fail, the search runs over the rest and lists the others in `unresolvedWebsites`.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"409":{"description":"TWO DIFFERENT FAILURES AT ONE STATUS, and `retry` is what tells them apart — they demand OPPOSITE responses. Never branch on the 409 alone.\n\n`idempotency_key_reused` (`retry: fix_input`) — This `Idempotency-Key` was already used with a different request body. Repeating this request unchanged will keep failing; use a new key.\n\n`idempotency_in_progress` (`retry: retry_later`) — This operation is still in progress. Retry the same request with the same Idempotency-Key.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.\n\n`quota_daily_limit` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace daily usage limit blocks new work. Wait for recent usage to leave the 24-hour window, or contact support; changing scopes does not help.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"`find_response_failed` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — The search completed and was charged, but its response could not be produced. The same Idempotency-Key preserves this outcome; a new key starts another paid search. Contact support.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"503":{"description":"Read `code` and `retry` to choose the next action. `find_unavailable` (`retry_later`): the search service failed. Wait, then send the same request again. `find_timeout` (`fix_input`): the search exceeded its time limit. Narrow the query or filters before trying again. `find_not_configured` (`do_not_retry`): this search is unavailable. No charge applies. `data_search_busy`: direct search is at capacity or briefly unavailable; wait `details.retryAfterSeconds` before retrying. `data_search_timeout` (`fix_input`): a search by filters, with or without `mode`, reached its time limit. Change what `message` names before retrying; the same search runs out of time again. It is not an empty result.\n\n`find_unavailable` (`retry: retry_later`) — The search service failed. Wait, then send the same request again. A successful search with incomplete data returns 200 with `degraded: true`.\n\n`find_timeout` (`retry: fix_input`) — The search exceeded its time limit. Narrow the query or filters before trying again. A search that already started can still finish. Do not repeat the identical request.\n\n`find_not_configured` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — This type of search is unavailable. Nothing was charged. Retrying or rewording the request will not help. Contact support. The `message` lists any available alternatives, such as an exact company-name lookup or a filters-only search.\n\n`data_search_busy` (`retry: retry_later`) — Hosted search capacity (direct Find, post keyword search, job-change search) is in use: your workspace already has as many of these searches running as it may, or the service is at capacity. Nothing ran. Wait for details.retryAfterSeconds, then retry, and send fewer at once.\n\n`data_search_timeout` (`retry: fix_input`) — A hosted search (Find by filters, with or without `mode: direct`; post keyword search; job-change search) ran out of time. Change what `message` names and retry; resending the same search runs out of time again, and a timeout is not an empty result.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Find companies or people not yet in your workspace","tags":["Find"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"find-anchor","parameter":"body.target","cases":{"people":["people:read"],"companies":["accounts:read"]},"otherwise":[]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/find\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"target\":\"people\",\"filters\":{\"industries\":[\"software development\"],\"hq\":{\"regions\":[\"europe\"]},\"headcount\":{\"min\":10,\"max\":200},\"fundingStages\":[\"seed\",\"series_a\"],\"foundedYear\":{\"min\":2019},\"title\":{\"any\":[\"founder\",\"cto\"],\"exclude\":[\"assistant\"]}},\"perCompany\":2,\"limit\":25}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/find\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"target\":\"people\",\"filters\":{\"industries\":[\"software development\"],\"hq\":{\"regions\":[\"europe\"]},\"headcount\":{\"min\":10,\"max\":200},\"fundingStages\":[\"seed\",\"series_a\"],\"foundedYear\":{\"min\":2019},\"title\":{\"any\":[\"founder\",\"cto\"],\"exclude\":[\"assistant\"]}},\"perCompany\":2,\"limit\":25})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/find/industries":{"get":{"description":"**Required permissions:** None beyond a valid API key.\n\nEvery value `filters.industries` accepts, lowercase, exactly as the Trayo holds it (a few hundred). Read this before your first industry filter: a value that is not on this list matches nothing, and the search will not guess a nearby one. `contains` narrows the list by substring. Free; any key may call it.","operationId":"listFindIndustries","parameters":[{"description":"Case-insensitive substring to narrow the list, e.g. `software`.","required":false,"name":"contains","in":"query","schema":{"minLength":1,"maxLength":60,"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/IndustriesResponseDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"503":{"description":"`find_not_configured` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — This type of search is unavailable. Nothing was charged. Retrying or rewording the request will not help. Contact support. The `message` lists any available alternatives, such as an exact company-name lookup or a filters-only search.\n\n`find_unavailable` (`retry: retry_later`) — The search service failed. Wait, then send the same request again. A successful search with incomplete data returns 200 with `degraded: true`.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"The industry taxonomy `filters.industries` accepts","tags":["Find"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":[]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/find/industries\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/v1/find/industries\", headers=HEADERS)\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/job-changes/search":{"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `people:read`.\n\nStateless search over our people data. Send `source` (the company left), `destination` (the company joined), or both. Or search without a company by `title`, the new role (same terms as `/v1/find` `filters.title`), narrowed by `destinationFilters` (`hq.countries`, `headcount` of the company joined); those two go only with a title search. Inclusive `startedSince` and exclusive `startedBefore` (the month the new role started, month precision) narrows any of these searches, with or without a company. One of source, destination or title is required. Returns moves observed in the last 90 days and writes nothing. One row per person per destination — we hold a row per source record, and those are collapsed; a title search returns one row per person. `limit` sets the page size: 25 by default, 100 at most, capped rather than rejected. `hasMore` says more matches may remain behind this page; send `nextCursor` back as `cursor`, verbatim and with the same search, to walk them. The walk resumes where the page stopped, so a later page neither repeats nor skips what an earlier one returned. `hasMore` reads the row count before duplicate records are collapsed, so a page can come back short and still be `true` — follow `hasMore` and `nextCursor`, never the row count. A source-only search may read a fixed sample rather than an ordered walk and cannot be paged; indexed source-only searches can page. Sending `cursor` on a sampled source-only search is rejected, `nextCursor` is null, and `hasMore: true` there means narrow the search. Report truncation for the requested period. Each row carries `detectedAt` (when we saw the move), `startedAt` (when the role began, to the month, often null) and `startedAtPrecision` (`month` or `year`). `detectedSince` filters detection recency: it keeps only moves with `detectedAt >=` the value you send — the DETECTION date, not the start date; `startedSince` filters the start, and both can be sent. It only narrows the 90-day window, starting at midnight UTC 90 days ago: an earlier value is clamped to that start and a future value matches nothing. Destination searches already return the newest moves first: narrowing the window does not recover omitted matches; it returns the same rows or a subset. This is a recency filter, not pagination. `seniority` is the second filter: it keeps only moves INTO a role at that level or above, read from the title of the role they joined — not the one they left, and not a title list you supply. The four seniority levels widen in order: `cxo` (the C-suite), `vp` (adds VP, SVP, EVP, Vice President and President), `director` (adds Director), `head` (adds Partner, Principal and Head of). With `destination`, it WIDENS the search rather than trimming the page — the search reads further through recent moves looking for matches instead of filtering the slice it would have read without it — and that wider read is still bounded, so a short or empty answer does not prove nobody senior joined. Source-only searches that report `sampled: true` filter the same fixed sample; they do not read further. Title matching is heuristic and excludes assistant/support roles. `sampled: true` means a source-only search read a small fixed sample of recent moves; an empty answer does not mean nobody left, and retrying gives the same answer while the underlying data is unchanged. A source-only search with `sampled: false` walked the newest moves out of that company instead of sampling them. With `destination`, `sampled` is false: the search reads a bounded slice of the newest moves into that company before filtering by source. `hasMore: false` does not prove completeness with either value of `sampled`. A title search reads the title index up to a cap and says `sampled: true` when the title is held by more people than that; each page reads a bounded number of moves, so it can come back short, even empty, with `hasMore: true` — follow the cursor. A company search with `startedSince` or `startedBefore` checks the start after reading each move, so it also reads a bounded number per page and pages the same way. Every row is a move between two companies; promotions and same-company title changes never appear here. For hires and promotions at a watched company, use the workspace `job_change` signal (`create_signal`, then `run_discovery`). That signal is not a departure search and does not provide a complete list of who left. A workspace can run only a few job-change searches at once. A search sent while that many are running comes back as `503 data_search_busy` before anything is read: wait `details.retryAfterSeconds`, send it again, and send fewer at the same time.","operationId":"searchJobChanges","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/JobChangeSearchBodyDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/JobChangeSearchResponseDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"None of source, destination or title was sent, `title` or `destinationFilters` was combined with a company, title had no any or all terms, `startedSince` or `startedBefore` was not a valid calendar month/date in YYYY-MM or YYYY-MM-DD form, either company is malformed, both resolve to the same company, `detectedSince` did not parse, `seniority` was not one of cxo, vp, director, head, `cursor` was sent to a sampled source-only backend, the start-month range was empty or reversed, or `cursor` did not decode.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.\n\n`invalid_date` (`retry: fix_input`) — A date filter (`updatedSince`, `since`, `detectedSince`) did not parse. Send a plain date (`2026-06-07`, read as midnight UTC) or a full ISO-8601 timestamp (`2026-06-07T14:30:00Z`). Relative words such as `yesterday` or `last-quarter` are not accepted. `param` names the field.\n\n`malformed_cursor` (`retry: fix_input`) — `cursor` was not a value this API issued. Send a previous page's `nextCursor` verbatim, or omit it to start over.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`account_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such account in your workspace. Another workspace's account is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.\n\n`company_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — We could not identify this company — not from the account's own record, nor from a LinkedIn page, website (including its redirect), or name — so there are no people to search. Retrying will not help. Send the company's own website if you did not; for any company, `POST /v1/find` on the contacts lane searches the web instead. From `POST /v1/find` with `filters.companyWebsites`, this means NO website resolved and nothing was searched; the message names every website. For one that is ambiguous (several possible companies on the domain) it also names the candidates and their ids: send the right id as `filters.companyIds`. When only some websites fail, the search runs over the rest and lists the others in `unresolvedWebsites`.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"503":{"description":"Our people data is unavailable, the bounded query failed or ran past the request budget, the search read ran out of time (`data_search_timeout`: narrow what `message` names; a timeout is not an empty result), or the workspace already has as many job-change searches running as it may (`data_search_busy`; wait `details.retryAfterSeconds`).\n\n`job_change_search_not_configured` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Job-change search is unavailable. Retrying will not help. Contact support.\n\n`job_change_search_failed` (`retry: retry_later`) — The bounded lookup failed or ran past its time budget. Nothing was written. Send the same job-change request again shortly.\n\n`data_search_busy` (`retry: retry_later`) — Hosted search capacity (direct Find, post keyword search, job-change search) is in use: your workspace already has as many of these searches running as it may, or the service is at capacity. Nothing ran. Wait for details.retryAfterSeconds, then retry, and send fewer at once.\n\n`data_search_timeout` (`retry: fix_input`) — A hosted search (Find by filters, with or without `mode: direct`; post keyword search; job-change search) ran out of time. Change what `message` names and retry; resending the same search runs out of time again, and a timeout is not an empty result.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Find recent company moves","tags":["People"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["people:read"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/job-changes/search\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"source\":{\"companyId\":1}}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/job-changes/search\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"source\":{\"companyId\":1}})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/posts/search":{"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `people:read`.\n\nSearches public LinkedIn posts from the last `windowDays` (default 30, maximum 30), or between inclusive `publishedFrom` and `publishedTo` dates within the last 365 days, for a `topic` by meaning and keyword, or by LinkedIn profile `author`. Omit topic to list an author's posts. Results are limited to posts Trayo holds, which go back 365 days; an earlier `publishedFrom` is refused with `validation_failed`. An empty result does not prove none were published. Posts arrive with a delay of about 10 days, so the most recent days may be incomplete. Returns up to `limit` posts per page (default 25, maximum 50), each with `postId`, `url`, the author, the author's company where known, and `commentCount`. Send a post's `url` or `postId` to POST /v1/posts/engagers to see who commented.\n\nFollow `nextCursor` as `cursor` with identical search filters until `hasMore` is false. Dates stay fixed across pages. Author-only pages traverse current stored posts newest first; edits or inserts can change a traversal. Topic pages freeze a bounded ranked candidate pool in private temporary storage. Check `coverage`: exhausting that pool does not prove all stored matches were found. An expired or unavailable snapshot never silently restarts a search. Nothing is added to your workspace. Allow at least 35 seconds for the client timeout.","operationId":"searchPosts","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PostSearchBodyDto"},"examples":{"topic":{"value":{"topic":"evaluating a new intent data vendor","windowDays":30,"limit":25}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PostSearchResponseDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.\n\n`malformed_cursor` (`retry: fix_input`) — `cursor` was not a value this API issued. Send a previous page's `nextCursor` verbatim, or omit it to start over.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"503":{"description":"`post_search_not_configured` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Post search is unavailable. Retrying will not help. Contact support.\n\n`post_search_failed` (`retry: retry_later`) — The post search or engager read failed or exceeded its time budget. Nothing was saved; retry the same request shortly.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Find LinkedIn posts by topic or author","tags":["People"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["people:read"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/posts/search\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"topic\":\"<topic>\"}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/posts/search\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"topic\":\"<topic>\"})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/posts/engagers":{"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `people:read`.\n\nSend `post`, a LinkedIn post URL or the `postId` from POST /v1/posts/search. Returns the post author, then up to 500 commenters in comment order, each with their current title and company where we know them. A person who commented more than once appears once, with their first comment and `commentCount`. `indexed: false` means we did not find the post; it does not mean nobody commented. `reason` says why: `outside_coverage` when the post predates `coverageFrom`, the first day of the 365 days Trayo keeps, else `not_held`. `commentsChecked: false` means we hold the post but not its comments, so the author comes back without commenters. `commentsLoadedAt` is the latest Trayo load time among returned stored comments, or null if none are stored. Stored comments can be stale or incomplete, and `truncated: false` only means the stored rows fit within the read limit. LinkedIn share URLs are resolved to activity ids when the post is held.\n\nSynchronous and read-only; nothing is added to your workspace. To keep people, send them to POST /v1/people/batch.","operationId":"getPostEngagers","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PostEngagersBodyDto"},"examples":{"url":{"value":{"post":"https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7350000000000000000/"}},"postId":{"value":{"post":"7350000000000000000"}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PostEngagersResponseDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"503":{"description":"`post_search_not_configured` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Post search is unavailable. Retrying will not help. Contact support.\n\n`post_search_failed` (`retry: retry_later`) — The post search or engager read failed or exceeded its time budget. Nothing was saved; retry the same request shortly.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"List the author and commenters of a LinkedIn post","tags":["People"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["people:read"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/posts/engagers\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"post\":\"<post>\"}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/posts/engagers\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"post\":\"<post>\"})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/posts/search/keywords":{"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `people:read`.\n\nDirect search with no generated query or semantic fallback. Split a request into concepts; put spelling variants or synonyms inside the same group. Groups are AND, alternatives are OR, and each alternative matches a normalized whole-token phrase. The response returns the executed `applied` groups. Optional authorIds constrain the authors.\n\nVerifies at most 200 ranked candidates from the recent-post index and returns at most 50 matches, ranked by keyword relevance within that sample. This bounded direct search accepts at most seven days and omits bodies shorter than 120 characters. Coverage is always non-exhaustive; an empty sample cannot prove absence. Read coverage.candidateCapReached and coverage.resultsTruncated, including on empty responses. There is no global match count or continuation cursor. Narrow criteria for a more complete answer. The requested date window is not a guarantee that every recent post has arrived. Nothing is saved. The server has an eight-second request budget; busy and timeout responses are failures, not empty matches.","operationId":"searchPostsByKeywords","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PostKeywordSearchBodyDto"},"examples":{"expanded":{"value":{"concepts":[["CRM","customer relationship management"],["migration","switching"]],"windowDays":7,"limit":25}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PostKeywordSearchResponseDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"503":{"description":"`post_search_not_configured` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Post search is unavailable. Retrying will not help. Contact support.\n\n`post_search_failed` (`retry: retry_later`) — The post search or engager read failed or exceeded its time budget. Nothing was saved; retry the same request shortly.\n\n`data_search_busy` (`retry: retry_later`) — Hosted search capacity (direct Find, post keyword search, job-change search) is in use: your workspace already has as many of these searches running as it may, or the service is at capacity. Nothing ran. Wait for details.retryAfterSeconds, then retry, and send fewer at once.\n\n`data_search_timeout` (`retry: fix_input`) — A hosted search (Find by filters, with or without `mode: direct`; post keyword search; job-change search) ran out of time. Change what `message` names and retry; resending the same search runs out of time again, and a timeout is not an empty result.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Search stored LinkedIn posts with explicit keyword groups","tags":["People"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["people:read"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/posts/search/keywords\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"concepts\":[[\"<concepts>\"]]}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/posts/search/keywords\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"concepts\":[[\"<concepts>\"]]})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/lists":{"get":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `people:read`.\n\nA page of your lists, most recently created first. PAGINATES: follow `nextCursor` until `hasMore` is false.\n\nLists are scoped to the USER your key acts as, matching the app: you see the lists this key created, and they appear in the Trayo app under that user. Another user's list in the same workspace is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.","operationId":"listLists","parameters":[{"description":"Case-insensitive substring match against `name` only.","required":false,"name":"q","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"description":"Send a plain date — `2026-06-07`, read as midnight UTC — or a full ISO-8601 timestamp — `2026-06-07T14:30:00Z` — when you need the time of day. **Relative words are not accepted:** `yesterday`, `last-quarter`, `7d` and anything else that has to be resolved against \"now\" is rejected with a 400 (`invalid_date`). Compute the date yourself and send it. Only lists whose `updatedAt` is at or after this value. Renaming a list moves `updatedAt`; adding or removing members does not.","required":false,"name":"updatedSince","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"description":"Page size, default 25, max 100.","required":false,"name":"limit","in":"query","schema":{"minimum":1,"maximum":9007199254740991,"type":"integer"}},{"description":"A previous page's `nextCursor`, verbatim.","required":false,"name":"cursor","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ListListDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.\n\n`malformed_cursor` (`retry: fix_input`) — `cursor` was not a value this API issued. Send a previous page's `nextCursor` verbatim, or omit it to start over.\n\n`invalid_date` (`retry: fix_input`) — A date filter (`updatedSince`, `since`, `detectedSince`) did not parse. Send a plain date (`2026-06-07`, read as midnight UTC) or a full ISO-8601 timestamp (`2026-06-07T14:30:00Z`). Relative words such as `yesterday` or `last-quarter` are not accepted. `param` names the field.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"List lists","tags":["Lists"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["people:read"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/lists\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/v1/lists\", headers=HEADERS)\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]},"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `people:write`.\n\n**A list is where the set you are working lives between calls.** Everything else in this API is a record the workspace holds; a list is YOUR grouping of those records — the 25 accounts for this week, the 40 people going to a campaign. Create it, add members with `POST /v1/lists/{id}/members`, and hand the list (not your session) to whatever acts on it.\n\n**Do not mark a working set any other way.** Overloading `starred`, writing a marker into a person's `title`, or keeping the set only in your own context are all things previous callers did before this resource existed, and all three lose the set or corrupt a record. This is the intended place.\n\nThe response has `memberCount: 0` — members are a second call. Lists are scoped to the USER your key acts as, matching the app: you see the lists this key created, and they appear in the Trayo app under that user. Another user's list in the same workspace is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.","operationId":"createList","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/CreateListDto"}}}},"responses":{"201":{"description":"List created, empty.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ListDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Create a list","tags":["Lists"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["people:write"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/lists\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"name\":\"<name>\"}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/lists\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"name\":\"<name>\"})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/lists/{id}":{"get":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `people:read`.\n\nThe list with its live counts. Members themselves are on `GET /v1/lists/{id}/members`, paginated.","operationId":"getList","parameters":[{"name":"id","required":true,"in":"path","schema":{"format":"uuid","type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ListDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`id` is not a UUID.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`list_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such list for this key. Lists are scoped to the user your key acts as, so a list another user created in the same workspace is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Get a list","tags":["Lists"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["people:read"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"# Replace {id} with the real value.\ncurl \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/lists/{id}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nid = \"...\"  # the {id} in the path\nr = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/v1/lists/{id}\", headers=HEADERS)\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]},"patch":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `people:write`.\n\n`name` is the only mutable field. Membership changes go through the `/members` routes, which is what keeps them append-only and safe to retry.","operationId":"updateList","parameters":[{"name":"id","required":true,"in":"path","schema":{"format":"uuid","type":"string"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/UpdateListDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ListDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`list_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such list for this key. Lists are scoped to the user your key acts as, so a list another user created in the same workspace is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Rename a list","tags":["Lists"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["people:write"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"# Replace {id} with the real value.\ncurl -X PATCH \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/lists/{id}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"name\":\"<name>\"}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nid = \"...\"  # the {id} in the path\nr = requests.patch(f\"{BASE}/v1/lists/{id}\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"name\":\"<name>\"})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]},"delete":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `people:write`.\n\nHard delete: the list and its membership rows are removed. The people and accounts it pointed at are untouched — membership is a reference, not ownership. Returns 200 with the list as it was.\n\nRefused with `list_in_use` while an outreach play in the Trayo app references the list; that reference is not addressable here.","operationId":"deleteList","parameters":[{"name":"id","required":true,"in":"path","schema":{"format":"uuid","type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The list as it existed immediately before deletion.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ListDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`id` is not a UUID.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`list_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such list for this key. Lists are scoped to the user your key acts as, so a list another user created in the same workspace is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"409":{"description":"`list_in_use` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — An outreach play still references this list, so it cannot be deleted. Plays are managed in the Trayo app, not here — remove the reference there, then delete. Repeating this call unchanged will keep failing.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Delete a list","tags":["Lists"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["people:write"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"# Replace {id} with the real value.\ncurl -X DELETE \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/lists/{id}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nid = \"...\"  # the {id} in the path\nr = requests.delete(f\"{BASE}/v1/lists/{id}\", headers=HEADERS)\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/lists/{id}/members":{"get":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `people:read`.\n\nA page of the list's live members, most recently added first. PAGINATES: follow `nextCursor` until `hasMore` is false.\n\nEach row is a MEMBERSHIP: its `id` is what `DELETE …/members/{memberId}` takes, and `personId` / `accountId` say what it points at. Fetch the person or account itself from its own route.\n\nRows whose person or account has since been deleted, and rows the app has marked `excluded`, are omitted.","operationId":"listListMembers","parameters":[{"name":"id","required":true,"in":"path","schema":{"format":"uuid","type":"string"}},{"description":"Only members of this kind. Omit for both.","required":false,"name":"kind","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"description":"Page size, default 25, max 100.","required":false,"name":"limit","in":"query","schema":{"minimum":1,"maximum":9007199254740991,"type":"integer"}},{"description":"A previous page's `nextCursor`, verbatim.","required":false,"name":"cursor","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ListMemberListDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.\n\n`malformed_cursor` (`retry: fix_input`) — `cursor` was not a value this API issued. Send a previous page's `nextCursor` verbatim, or omit it to start over.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`list_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such list for this key. Lists are scoped to the user your key acts as, so a list another user created in the same workspace is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"List members","tags":["Lists"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["people:read"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"# Replace {id} with the real value.\ncurl \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/lists/{id}/members\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nid = \"...\"  # the {id} in the path\nr = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/v1/lists/{id}/members\", headers=HEADERS)\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]},"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `people:write`.\n\nAdd people and/or whole accounts, up to 200 per call. Each row is either `{ personId }` (pin a person) or `{ accountId }` (add the whole account as a dynamic entry) — the kind is derived from which id you send. Set `via` to say how they got here: `find` for a `POST /v1/find` result, `signal` when an event suggested them, `import` for a bulk load, `manual` (default) otherwise.\n\n**Partial success, and duplicates are skips.** A row that is already on the list — from this call or an earlier one — lands in `skipped` with a reason, not in an error, so the same batch can be sent twice without doubling anything. Read `skipped` every time; `200` means the call ran, not that every row was added.\n\nThe typical shape: `POST /v1/find` → `POST /v1/accounts/batch` (or `/v1/people/batch`) → this route with the ids that came back and `via: \"find\"`.","operationId":"addListMembers","parameters":[{"name":"id","required":true,"in":"path","schema":{"format":"uuid","type":"string"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AddListMembersDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The request was processed. Check `skipped` — a `200` does not mean every row landed.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AddListMembersResultDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"The ENVELOPE was wrong: `members` missing, not an array, empty, or over 200 items. A bad ROW never produces this status — it is reported in the `200` response's `skipped` instead.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`list_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such list for this key. Lists are scoped to the user your key acts as, so a list another user created in the same workspace is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Add members","tags":["Lists"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["people:write"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"# Replace {id} with the real value.\ncurl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/lists/{id}/members\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"members\":[{\"personId\":\"11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111\"}]}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nid = \"...\"  # the {id} in the path\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/lists/{id}/members\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"members\":[{\"personId\":\"11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111\"}]})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/lists/{id}/members/{memberId}":{"delete":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `people:write`.\n\nRemoves the membership row. The person or account is untouched. `memberId` is the row's `id` from `GET /v1/lists/{id}/members`, not the person's or account's id. Returns 200 with the row as it was.","operationId":"removeListMember","parameters":[{"name":"id","required":true,"in":"path","schema":{"format":"uuid","type":"string"}},{"name":"memberId","required":true,"in":"path","schema":{"format":"uuid","type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The membership as it existed before removal.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ListMemberDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"A path parameter is not a UUID.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`list_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such list for this key. Lists are scoped to the user your key acts as, so a list another user created in the same workspace is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.\n\n`list_member_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such member on this list. `memberId` is the MEMBERSHIP row's `id` from `GET /v1/lists/{id}/members` — not the person's or account's id.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Remove a member","tags":["Lists"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["people:write"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"# Replace {id}, {memberId} with the real value.\ncurl -X DELETE \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/lists/{id}/members/{memberId}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nid = \"...\"  # the {id} in the path\nmember_id = \"...\"  # the {memberId} in the path\nr = requests.delete(f\"{BASE}/v1/lists/{id}/members/{member_id}\", headers=HEADERS)\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/workspace":{"get":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `accounts:read`.\n\nThe workspace your key acts in, including generated solution cards, buyer personas, the ICP buyer profile, and their prose projections. Review generated assumptions with the user before acting on them. One workspace per key; there is nothing to select.\n\n**The stakeholder definition is what makes stakeholder search yours.** Two stages read it. The account-level search that runs when a company is added to the workspace turns it into search keywords and selects people at the company against it; without a definition that search seeds on seniority alone (chiefs, VPs, directors of any function). The per-event stage that a discovery run started with `people: \"add\"` runs attaches people, with a per-person `reasoning`, to each event; without a definition that stage does not run at all and `expand=people` is `[]` on every event.\n\n**Set it FIRST — before you add accounts, and before you run discovery.** It steers work that starts after it is set and is never applied retroactively, and the account-level search for a company starts the moment that company is added. An account added before the definition existed keeps the people that search found for it then; the way to search it against the new definition is `POST /v1/stakeholders/search`.","operationId":"getWorkspace","parameters":[],"responses":{"200":{"description":"","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/WorkspaceDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Read workspace onboarding assumptions and settings","tags":["Workspace"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["accounts:read"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/workspace\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/v1/workspace\", headers=HEADERS)\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]},"patch":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `settings:write`.\n\nPartial update: send only the fields you are changing. `solutionItems` and `stakeholderPersonas` replace complete structured lists and regenerate their prose projections atomically. Pass the latest `revision` as `expectedRevision` for list edits, and re-read and merge on a 409 conflict. Changing solutions clears an omitted `solutionsBrief` rather than leaving an outdated summary. `buyerProfile` patches only supplied ICP assumptions, including nested geography and sizeBand. Legacy prose fields accept `null` to clear, but a direct prose edit discards the matching structured cards. Do not send both forms of the same setting. Discovery uses the saved values on future work.\n\n**Write the definition as prose, the way you would brief a new researcher**: the roles that own or buy what you sell, the roles that influence the decision, and the roles to skip. Example: \"Heads of platform, infrastructure, DevOps or SRE, and the VP or Director of Engineering they report to. Not recruiters, not IT, not security, not individual engineers.\"\n\n**The stakeholder definition is what makes stakeholder search yours.** Two stages read it. The account-level search that runs when a company is added to the workspace turns it into search keywords and selects people at the company against it; without a definition that search seeds on seniority alone (chiefs, VPs, directors of any function). The per-event stage that a discovery run started with `people: \"add\"` runs attaches people, with a per-person `reasoning`, to each event; without a definition that stage does not run at all and `expand=people` is `[]` on every event.\n\n**Set it FIRST — before you add accounts, and before you run discovery.** It steers work that starts after it is set and is never applied retroactively, and the account-level search for a company starts the moment that company is added. An account added before the definition existed keeps the people that search found for it then; the way to search it against the new definition is `POST /v1/stakeholders/search`.","operationId":"updateWorkspace","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/UpdateWorkspaceBodyDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The settings as they now stand.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/WorkspaceDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"An empty body, an unknown field, a blank or oversized value, conflicting structured/prose forms, a list edit without expectedRevision, or a buyer-profile edit without a saved profile. `param` names the field.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"409":{"description":"The workspace changed since expectedRevision. Re-read and merge the correction.\n\n`conflict` (`retry: fix_input`) — The generic 409: the request collides with existing state, and none of the specific codes covers it. `message` says what.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Correct workspace onboarding assumptions and settings","tags":["Workspace"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["settings:write"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl -X PATCH \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/workspace\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"expectedRevision\":\"<expectedRevision>\"}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.patch(f\"{BASE}/v1/workspace\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"expectedRevision\":\"<expectedRevision>\"})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/whoami":{"get":{"description":"**Required permissions:** None beyond a valid API key.\n\n**Make this your first call.** It confirms the key works and returns the workspace and user, granted and effective key scopes, key expiry, data-access restrictions, workspace request budgets and lookup capabilities. Compare `key.effectiveScopes` with each operation’s `x-trayo-scope-requirements`.\n\nRead-only and free. This call starts no searches and changes no records. A 401 here is the key itself — no other route will accept it either.\n\n`canInitiate` describes workspace lifecycle only; it does not authorize this key. Lookup `available` combines scope, lifecycle, plan and current quota checks for new lookups. `blockedBy` explains missing authority or limits. These are snapshots: workspace request pacing, concurrent work and request-specific checks still apply.","operationId":"whoami","parameters":[],"responses":{"200":{"description":"","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/WhoamiDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Who this key is: permissions, workspace and limits","tags":["Workspace"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":[]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/whoami\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/v1/whoami\", headers=HEADERS)\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/stakeholders/search":{"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `research:trigger`.\n\nGiven a company — any company, by its website (or LinkedIn page or name), or an account in your workspace — and a stakeholder definition, return the people at it who fit, best first, each with a reason. **Synchronous and read-only**: the answer comes back in one response, typically in 5–20 seconds (the server gives up at 25 with `503 stakeholder_search_failed`, so set your client timeout above that and retry once on `retry_later`), and nothing is written to your workspace. Import the ones you want with `POST /v1/people/batch`.\n\n**Company identity.** Trayo identifies the company from its LinkedIn page first, then its website, then its name. The response includes people who fit your definition and explains each result in `whyThisPerson`. `company.resolvedBy` says which identity was used. Before importing anyone, make sure that `company.name` and `company.website` identify the intended company. A guessed handle or a common name can identify a different company.\n\nPublic REST and MCP usage is recorded without daily usage caps, workspace quota cutoffs or lookup quotas for now. Workspace request pacing still applies. **The definition.** Send one per call, in plain prose — the roles that own or buy what you sell, the roles that influence, the roles to skip. Omit it to use the workspace's own definition; if that is unset too, a search for senior roles applies and `definition.source` says `default` so you know the result is senior people of any function rather than your buying committee. A definition sent here changes nothing on the workspace.\n\n**Read `candidates` with `people`.** `candidates: 0` means Trayo found no people with the requested keywords at this company. `candidates > 0` with `people: []` means the selection judged none of them to fit — a real answer, not an error. Fewer than `limit` come back when fewer fit.\n\n**Near-misses.** When nobody fits, `nearMisses` holds up to 3 of the closest candidates, each with `belowThreshold: true` and a reason saying what their role lacks, and `next` names their titles. They did not fit: offer them as alternatives rather than importing them as the buying committee.\n\n**Personas.** Each person carries `matchedPersona`, and `coverage` lists every persona with whether anyone in `people` matched it — so a persona with no match (no champion, say) is stated, not guessed from titles, and `next` says what to do about it. The names come from `personas` in the request, or from the workspace's saved personas when its definition applies. Each label is checked after selection against the job's function and seniority (a saved persona's seniority and rationale are read too) and replaced or cleared when it does not hold; the person stays. One person can cover several personas: a CTO also covers \"VP Eng\".\n\n**Repeatable.** Repeating a search within a week normally returns the same people.\n\n**Many companies.** For up to 50 companies at once, use `POST /v1/stakeholders/search/batch` rather than one call per company.\n\n**Compared with `POST /v1/find`.** Find's contacts lane searches the web and identifies people from any source; this searches Trayo's data for people who fit your definition. Use find when the company is not in our data (`company_not_found`) or when you want breadth over fit.","operationId":"searchStakeholders","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/StakeholderSearchBodyDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The selected people, with the company as resolved and the definition as applied. `people` may be empty — read `candidates`.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/StakeholderSearchResponseDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`company` with neither an `accountId` nor any of `website` / `linkedinUrl` / `name`, or with `accountId` alongside them; a `linkedinUrl` that is a LinkedIn URL but not a company page; a blank definition; a `limit` outside 1–10; or an unknown field. `param` names it.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"402":{"description":"`quota_exceeded` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — This workspace has insufficient quota for this operation. Retrying or changing the request does not help; raise the quota or wait for it to renew.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`account_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such account in your workspace. Another workspace's account is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.\n\n`company_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — We could not identify this company — not from the account's own record, nor from a LinkedIn page, website (including its redirect), or name — so there are no people to search. Retrying will not help. Send the company's own website if you did not; for any company, `POST /v1/find` on the contacts lane searches the web instead. From `POST /v1/find` with `filters.companyWebsites`, this means NO website resolved and nothing was searched; the message names every website. For one that is ambiguous (several possible companies on the domain) it also names the candidates and their ids: send the right id as `filters.companyIds`. When only some websites fail, the search runs over the rest and lists the others in `unresolvedWebsites`.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.\n\n`quota_daily_limit` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace daily usage limit blocks new work. Wait for recent usage to leave the 24-hour window, or contact support; changing scopes does not help.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"503":{"description":"`stakeholder_search_not_configured` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Stakeholder search is unavailable. Retrying will not help. Contact support. For another way to find people, use `POST /v1/find` on the contacts lane.\n\n`stakeholder_search_failed` (`retry: retry_later`) — Stakeholder search failed or timed out. Nothing was saved. Send the same request again shortly.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Find the stakeholders at a company that fit a definition","tags":["People"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["research:trigger"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/stakeholders/search\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"company\":{\"companyId\":1}}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/stakeholders/search\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"company\":{\"companyId\":1}})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/stakeholders/search/batch":{"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `research:trigger`.\n\nThe same search as `POST /v1/stakeholders/search`, for every company in `companies` (1 to 50), under one `definition`, `personas` and `limit`. The companies are searched ten at a time: 50 typically answer in about a minute, against 8–14 seconds each one after another. Each company still has its own 25-second limit, so set your client timeout to at least 180 seconds. **Synchronous and read-only**: nothing is written to your workspace.\n\n**One outcome per company.** Every company ends in exactly one of `results` or `errors`, matched by `index`. A company that cannot be found (`company_not_found`) or whose search fails (`stakeholder_search_failed`, `retry_later`) is an `errors` entry and never fails the rest; send just those companies again. Each `results` entry has the single route's shape without `definition`, which is stated once at the top.\n\nPublic REST and MCP usage is recorded without daily usage caps, workspace quota cutoffs or lookup quotas for now. Workspace request pacing still applies. ","operationId":"searchStakeholdersBatch","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/StakeholderBatchSearchBodyDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"One outcome per submitted company, in `results` or `errors`.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/StakeholderBatchSearchResponseDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`companies` empty or over 50, a company named neither by `accountId` nor by any of `website` / `linkedinUrl` / `name`, a blank definition, a `limit` outside 1–10, or an unknown field. `param` names it.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"402":{"description":"`quota_exceeded` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — This workspace has insufficient quota for this operation. Retrying or changing the request does not help; raise the quota or wait for it to renew.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.\n\n`quota_daily_limit` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace daily usage limit blocks new work. Wait for recent usage to leave the 24-hour window, or contact support; changing scopes does not help.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"503":{"description":"`stakeholder_search_not_configured` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Stakeholder search is unavailable. Retrying will not help. Contact support. For another way to find people, use `POST /v1/find` on the contacts lane.\n\n`stakeholder_search_failed` (`retry: retry_later`) — Stakeholder search failed or timed out. Nothing was saved. Send the same request again shortly.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Find the stakeholders at up to 50 companies in one call","tags":["People"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["research:trigger"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/stakeholders/search/batch\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"companies\":[{\"companyId\":1}]}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/stakeholders/search/batch\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"companies\":[{\"companyId\":1}]})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/research/company":{"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `research:trigger`.\n\nGiven a company — any company, by its website (or LinkedIn page or name), or an account in your workspace — return a short overview: the firmographic facts, `whyNow` hooks drawn from its recent LinkedIn updates, and `fit` against what your workspace sells.\n\nReturns an overview in the same response, typically within 2–3 seconds. The server stops after 45 seconds with `503 research_failed`. Set your client timeout above 45 seconds and retry once on `retry_later`. Each call generates a new answer. It saves nothing to your workspace. The company or person does not need to be in your workspace. This is the same quick overview the Trayo app shows. Public REST and MCP usage is recorded without daily usage caps, workspace quota cutoffs or lookup quotas for now. Workspace request pacing still applies. \n\n**How it works.** The company is identified exactly as the Trayo app identifies one — LinkedIn page, then website (following its redirect), then name, against the same data; `company.resolvedBy` says which key matched. **Read `company.name` and `company.website` back before you act on the overview** — a guessed handle or a common name can match a different company, and the overview will faithfully describe that one. The record Trayo holds — description, industry, size, tech stack and its recent company updates — informs the overview together with your workspace's `solutions` and stakeholder definition (`GET /v1/workspace`), which is where `fit` comes from. No web search: the \"why now\" signal is our own recent updates, so `whyNow` is empty when the company has posted nothing substantive.\n\n**Nothing is written.** Adding a company as an account is what puts it on record — background work that persists the company, its people and its events. This is a read: seconds, nothing stored, any company, whether or not you hold it.","operationId":"researchCompany","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/CompanyResearchBodyDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The overview, with the company as resolved.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/CompanyResearchResponseDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`company` with neither an `accountId` nor any of `website` / `linkedinUrl` / `name`, or with `accountId` alongside them; a `linkedinUrl` that is a LinkedIn URL but not a company page; or an unknown field. `param` names it.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"402":{"description":"`quota_exceeded` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — This workspace has insufficient quota for this operation. Retrying or changing the request does not help; raise the quota or wait for it to renew.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`account_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such account in your workspace. Another workspace's account is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.\n\n`company_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — We could not identify this company — not from the account's own record, nor from a LinkedIn page, website (including its redirect), or name — so there are no people to search. Retrying will not help. Send the company's own website if you did not; for any company, `POST /v1/find` on the contacts lane searches the web instead. From `POST /v1/find` with `filters.companyWebsites`, this means NO website resolved and nothing was searched; the message names every website. For one that is ambiguous (several possible companies on the domain) it also names the candidates and their ids: send the right id as `filters.companyIds`. When only some websites fail, the search runs over the rest and lists the others in `unresolvedWebsites`.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.\n\n`quota_daily_limit` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace daily usage limit blocks new work. Wait for recent usage to leave the 24-hour window, or contact support; changing scopes does not help.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"503":{"description":"`research_not_configured` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Company and person research are unavailable. Retrying will not help. Contact support.\n\n`research_failed` (`retry: retry_later`) — A research route failed or ran past the time budget. Nothing was written. Send the same request again shortly.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"A quick overview of a company: what it does, why now, and fit","tags":["Research"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["research:trigger"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/research/company\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"company\":{\"companyId\":1}}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/research/company\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"company\":{\"companyId\":1}})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/research/person":{"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `research:trigger`.\n\nGiven a person — any person, by their LinkedIn profile, or a person in your workspace — return a short stakeholder overview: their career progression, `professionalInsights` tied to what your workspace sells, and the `challenges` they are likely up against.\n\nReturns an overview in the same response, typically within 2–3 seconds. The server stops after 45 seconds with `503 research_failed`. Set your client timeout above 45 seconds and retry once on `retry_later`. Each call generates a new answer. It saves nothing to your workspace. The company or person does not need to be in your workspace. This is the same quick overview the Trayo app shows. Public REST and MCP usage is recorded without daily usage caps, workspace quota cutoffs or lookup quotas for now. Workspace request pacing still applies. \n\n**How it works.** A workspace person's existing match is read; without one, their LinkedIn username is looked up, which is also what a profile sent as `linkedinUrl` does. `person.resolvedBy` says which. The profile Trayo holds — headline and work history — informs the overview together with your workspace's `solutions` and stakeholder definition (`GET /v1/workspace`).\n\n**`grounded`.** Ungrounded, the default: no web search, and the overview is built from the profile Trayo holds alone, so `personalInsights`, `companyIntel`, `location` and `education` are empty and `challenges` are inferences. Grounded, Trayo searches the web for timely company intel and personal facts — slower (5–15 seconds rather than 2–3), and it occasionally fails to answer (`503 research_failed`; retry once). Both modes draw on the quota the same way. A web fact Trayo could not source is withheld rather than stated, so an empty `location` means \"could not be sourced\", not \"unknown\". **Source links are not published** — the requirement to have one gates what is said, and the link itself is not returned, in `research` or in `reportMarkdown`. Treat a grounded overview as a lead to check, not as sourced evidence.\n\n**Compared with `POST /v1/stakeholders/search`.** That finds WHO at a company fits a definition; this says what to know about ONE person you already have in hand — a stakeholder-search result's `linkedinUrl` goes straight into `person.linkedinUrl` here.","operationId":"researchPerson","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PersonResearchBodyDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The overview, with the person as resolved.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PersonResearchResponseDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`person` with neither or both of `personId` / `linkedinUrl`; a `linkedinUrl` that is a LinkedIn URL but not a profile; `grounded` not a boolean; or an unknown field. `param` names it.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"402":{"description":"`quota_exceeded` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — This workspace has insufficient quota for this operation. Retrying or changing the request does not help; raise the quota or wait for it to renew.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`person_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such person in your workspace. Another workspace's person is indistinguishable from a non-existent one.\n\n`person_profile_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — We hold no public profile for this person — the LinkedIn profile is not in our data, or the person in your workspace carries neither a match to it nor a LinkedIn username. Retrying will not help. Send the person's LinkedIn profile URL if you sent a `personId`. Distinct from `person_not_found`, which means there is no such person in your workspace at all.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.\n\n`quota_daily_limit` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace daily usage limit blocks new work. Wait for recent usage to leave the 24-hour window, or contact support; changing scopes does not help.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"503":{"description":"`research_not_configured` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Company and person research are unavailable. Retrying will not help. Contact support.\n\n`research_failed` (`retry: retry_later`) — A research route failed or ran past the time budget. Nothing was written. Send the same request again shortly.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"A quick overview of a person: career, likely challenges, and angles","tags":["Research"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["research:trigger"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/research/person\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"person\":{\"personId\":\"11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111\"}}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/research/person\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"person\":{\"personId\":\"11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111\"}})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/research/person/batch":{"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `research:trigger`.\n\nReturns every overview in the same response. One person typically takes 2–3 seconds, and people are synthesized several at a time, so a full 10-person call takes a small multiple of that rather than 10 times it. The server stops after 45 seconds with `503 research_failed`. Set your client timeout above 45 seconds and retry once on `retry_later`. Each call generates a new answer. It saves nothing to your workspace. The company or person does not need to be in your workspace. This is the same quick overview the Trayo app shows. Public REST and MCP usage is recorded without daily usage caps, workspace quota cutoffs or lookup quotas for now. Workspace request pacing still applies. \n\nSame as `POST /v1/research/person`, once per person in `people` (1 to 10), reading the workspace seller context once for the whole batch. Always ungrounded — `grounded` is not accepted here. A person that cannot be resolved, or whose overview comes back empty (`person_profile_too_thin`), lands in `errors` by `index` with a `code` and a `retry` class, and never fails the rest of the batch. Only the overviews in `results` draw on the quota — a person in `errors` does not.","operationId":"researchPersonBatch","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PersonBatchResearchBodyDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"One outcome per submitted person, in `results` or `errors`.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PersonBatchResearchResponseDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`people` empty, over 10, containing an item with neither or both of `personId` / `linkedinUrl`, or a top-level `grounded` field.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"402":{"description":"`quota_exceeded` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — This workspace has insufficient quota for this operation. Retrying or changing the request does not help; raise the quota or wait for it to renew.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.\n\n`quota_daily_limit` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace daily usage limit blocks new work. Wait for recent usage to leave the 24-hour window, or contact support; changing scopes does not help.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"503":{"description":"`research_not_configured` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Company and person research are unavailable. Retrying will not help. Contact support.\n\n`research_failed` (`retry: retry_later`) — A research route failed or ran past the time budget. Nothing was written. Send the same request again shortly.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"A quick overview for up to 10 people in one call","tags":["Research"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["research:trigger"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/research/person/batch\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"people\":[{\"personId\":\"11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111\"}]}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/research/person/batch\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"people\":[{\"personId\":\"11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111\"}]})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/contacts/lookup":{"post":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `body.fields` includes `email`: `people:enrich_email`; `body.fields` includes `phone`: `people:enrich_phone`. All scopes for the selected fields are required. Omitting `body.fields` uses `[\"email\"]` and requires `people:enrich_email`. Malformed values: no additional scopes; unknown fields add no scopes. Request validation still applies.\n\nGive a person — their name, and their LinkedIn profile or where they work — and get their email back in the same response, and their phone as a lookup to poll. The person does not have to exist in your workspace, and this call does not create them: it is `POST /v1/people/{id}/enrich` with the person row taken out of the middle, for the case where you are still deciding whether someone is worth keeping.\n\n**Email is synchronous.** Typically a few seconds, and the server gives up at 30 with `503 contact_lookup_failed`, so set your client timeout above that. Import the people you want afterwards with `POST /v1/people` (send the `email` you got back as the person's email).\n\n**Phone is asynchronous.** Ask for it with `fields: [\"phone\"]` and the response is `202` with `phone.status: \"pending\"` and a `phone.lookupId`; collect it from `GET /v1/contacts/lookups/{lookupId}`. Phone lookups typically take one to two minutes, but can take up to four minutes. Email asked for in the same call is still answered inline, in the same response.\n\n**What it costs.** One lookup per field when a search starts (a phone counts when it starts, so polling is free), counted against your plan's allowance for that field — email and phone have separate limits. A lookup here and a lookup on a person draw on the same allowance for the same field. Over the limit is `402 lookup_limit_reached` before any search starts. The response carries `quota`: the allowance left per field after this call, the same numbers `GET /v1/whoami` reports.\n\n**Asking twice is free.** The workspace's answer for one identity is remembered — a month for a found address, a week for `not_found` — and a repeat request reads it: `source: \"saved\"`, no new lookup, and nothing counted against your allowance. So a retry after `not_found` costs nothing.\n\n**A found address is not a verified owner.** `status: \"found\"` means a search returned the address and nothing suggests it belongs to someone else. `status: \"unconfirmed\"` means a search returned it but `email.identityConfidence` is `conflict`: the address is still in `value`, and a human should look before anyone sends to it. `email.identityConfidence` (`match`, `conflict` or `unknown`) says why. It compares the address against the `fullName` you sent, always, and against the `company.website` you sent, when you sent one. Include the known employer website even with a LinkedIn profile; without it, a matching name can produce `match` at the wrong employer. `match` does not prove mailbox ownership or current employment, and this field does not block sending.\n\n**`not_found` is an answer.** The lookup finished without a value and returns `200`. A `503` means the question was never answered — nothing charged, nothing stored.\n\n**Partial success is the contract.** When you ask for both fields and one fails because of a plan limit or a lookup error, the call still answers. That field reads `status: \"failed\"` with `error.code`, `error.retry` and `error.message`, exactly what an error response would have carried. The other field keeps its answer and its `lookupId`. Nothing is charged for a field that failed. The call itself fails only when every field you asked for did.\n\n**What to send.** Include the LinkedIn profile when known to improve the chance of finding contact details. Otherwise, send the company website. A name alone returns `400`.","operationId":"lookupContact","parameters":[],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ContactLookupBodyDto"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The lookup ran, a stored answer was returned, or nothing could run (`not_attempted`). Read `email.status` for the outcome (`unconfirmed` for a found address that may be someone else's), `email.identityConfidence` for whether the address looks like the person you described, and `email.source` for whether this call paid for it.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ContactLookupResultDto"}}}},"202":{"description":"A phone lookup was started. Same body as `200`; `phone.status` is `pending` and `phone.lookupId` is the id to poll. An email asked for in the same call is answered in this response.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ContactLookupResultDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"Neither `linkedinUrl` nor `company.website`; a `linkedinUrl` that is not a personal profile URL; a missing or empty `fullName`; or an unknown field. `param` names it.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"402":{"description":"`lookup_limit_reached` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — This workspace cannot run this contact lookup: the plan's email or phone lookup limit is reached, or the plan does not include that kind of lookup. `message` says which and quotes the limit. Retrying never helps and neither does changing the request — the plan has to change. Nothing was started and nothing was charged.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"503":{"description":"`contact_lookup_failed` (`retry: retry_later`) — The email lookup could not be completed: it failed or ran past its time budget. Nothing was charged, nothing was stored, and no allowance was consumed. Send the same request again shortly. A lookup that RAN and found nothing is a `200` with `status: \"not_found\"`, not this.\n\n`lookup_start_failed` (`retry: retry_later`) — The contact lookup passed every check but could not be started. No lookup is running for it, and a retry of the same request is not charged twice. Send it again shortly.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Find an email or phone for a person you describe","tags":["People"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"contact-fields","parameter":"body.fields","combine":"union","cases":{"email":["people:enrich_email"],"phone":["people:enrich_phone"]},"defaultFields":["email"],"omitted":["people:enrich_email"],"malformed":[]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl -X POST \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/contacts/lookup\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"fullName\":\"<fullName>\"}'"},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nr = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/v1/contacts/lookup\", headers=HEADERS, json={\"fullName\":\"<fullName>\"})\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/contacts/lookups/{lookupId}":{"get":{"description":"**Required permissions:** `people:enrich_phone`.\n\nThe state of one lookup started by `POST /v1/contacts/lookup` — in practice a phone. `status` is `pending` until the lookup finishes, then `found`, `not_found`, or `failed` and it stays that way. Poll every 10 to 15 seconds. A phone lookup typically finishes within two minutes, but can take up to four. Attempts expire two hours after acceptance. On `failed`, stop polling this ID; the nested error explains why. A new `POST /v1/contacts/lookup` may be tried later, with normal charges and no automatic refund. Polling is free.\n\nThis response does not include the person. Keep a note of who each `lookupId` refers to.\n\nTrayo saves a `found` or `not_found` answer for repeat requests, so re-sending the original `POST` after it settles returns it with `source: \"saved\"` and no charge — either way of collecting it works.","operationId":"getContactLookup","parameters":[{"name":"lookupId","required":true,"in":"path","description":"From a `POST /v1/contacts/lookup` response.","schema":{"format":"uuid","type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The lookup, pending or final.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ContactLookupStatusDto"}}}},"400":{"description":"`lookupId` is not a UUID.\n\n`validation_failed` (`retry: fix_input`) — The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"401":{"description":"Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Every way authentication can fail returns the identical body, so do not try to infer which one it was, and do not repeat the call with the same key.\n\n`unauthorized` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"403":{"description":"The key grant and its owner's current workspace role must both include every scope required by the operation.\n\n`insufficient_scope` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"},{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"details":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ScopeDenialDetailsDto"}}}}}]}}}},"404":{"description":"`contact_lookup_not_found` (`retry: do_not_retry`) — No such `lookupId` in your workspace. Another workspace's lookup is indistinguishable from one that never existed. The id comes from a `POST /v1/contacts/lookup` response.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"429":{"description":"Every route is rate limited per workspace across REST, MCP, all keys and OAuth users, `GET /v1/whoami` included, so a balance poll competes with the work it is watching. For `rate_limited`, wait `Retry-After` seconds (also `details.retryAfterSeconds`), then send the same request once; do not retry sooner. `RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` describe the workspace's bucket, and they come back on successful responses too: read them and slow down BEFORE you are refused. A burst from one network can also be refused before the key is checked; that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*` headers.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"RateLimit-Limit":{"description":"Maximum requests permitted in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"RateLimit-Remaining":{"description":"Requests remaining in the active rolling window.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"RateLimit-Reset":{"description":"Seconds until the oldest request in the window expires.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}},"500":{"description":"Something failed on our side. Nothing about the request needs changing.\n\n`internal_error` (`retry: retry_later`) — Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"summary":"Collect a lookup that was still running","tags":["People"],"x-trayo-scope-requirements":{"version":1,"requirement":{"kind":"static","scopes":["people:enrich_phone"]}},"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"# Replace {lookupId} with the real value.\ncurl \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/contacts/lookups/{lookupId}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TRAYO_API_KEY\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\nHEADERS = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {os.environ['TRAYO_API_KEY']}\"}\n\nlookup_id = \"...\"  # the {lookupId} in the path\nr = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/v1/contacts/lookups/{lookup_id}\", headers=HEADERS)\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/":{"get":{"description":"An unauthenticated JSON index: the URL of the OpenAPI document, the auth scheme, and every route this API serves with its method and summary. Derived from the same generated document the `openapi` URLs return, so it cannot list a route that does not exist.\n\nServed at both `/` and `/v1`.","operationId":"getApiIndex","parameters":[],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The index."}},"security":[],"summary":"Where the documentation is and how to authenticate","tags":["Meta"],"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl \"$TRAYO_API_URL/\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\n\nr = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/\")\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/recipes":{"get":{"description":"Unauthenticated. Each recipe is an ordered list of operations from this document — by `operationId`, `method` and `path` — with what each step does in that sequence and, for a poll step, the condition that ends the loop (`until`). `when` says which recipe fits a task; `spends` says what it costs before you start.\n\nThe same list is carried in the OpenAPI document as `x-recipes` and rendered in `/llms.txt`. A recipe can only name an operation this document describes: the list is resolved against the document, not maintained beside it.","operationId":"listRecipes","parameters":[],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The recipes."},"429":{"description":"Unauthenticated, so this route is limited per source network rather than per workspace and carries `Retry-After` alone — there is no workspace bucket to report, and no `RateLimit-*` headers. Fetch this document once and reuse it rather than re-reading it per call.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"security":[],"summary":"The call sequences that make up a task","tags":["Meta"],"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/recipes\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\n\nr = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/v1/recipes\")\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/v1/openapi.yaml":{"get":{"description":"Unauthenticated, so that a caller can fetch this document before it has a key configured. Generated from the running server's own routes, so it cannot drift from the API it describes.\n\nThe same document is served at `GET /openapi.json` and `GET /.well-known/openapi`. The extension chooses the default serialization — YAML here, JSON there — and an explicit `Accept` of `application/json` or `application/yaml` overrides it either way.","operationId":"getOpenApiDocument","parameters":[],"responses":{"200":{"description":"This OpenAPI document.","content":{"application/yaml":{"schema":{"type":"string"}},"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object"}}}},"429":{"description":"Unauthenticated, so this route is limited per source network rather than per workspace and carries `Retry-After` alone — there is no workspace bucket to report, and no `RateLimit-*` headers. Fetch this document once and reuse it rather than re-reading it per call.\n\n`rate_limited` (`retry: retry_later`) — The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying the request.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorDto"}}}}},"security":[],"summary":"This document","tags":["Meta"],"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl \"$TRAYO_API_URL/v1/openapi.yaml\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\n\nr = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/v1/openapi.yaml\")\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/openapi.json":{"get":{"description":"The same document as `GET /v1/openapi.yaml`, serialized as JSON. Send `Accept: application/yaml` to get YAML from this URL instead.","operationId":"getOpenApiDocumentJson","parameters":[],"responses":{"200":{"description":"This OpenAPI document.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object"}},"application/yaml":{"schema":{"type":"string"}}}}},"security":[],"summary":"This document, as JSON","tags":["Meta"],"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl \"$TRAYO_API_URL/openapi.json\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\n\nr = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/openapi.json\")\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}},"/.well-known/openapi":{"get":{"description":"Identical to `GET /openapi.json`.","operationId":"getWellKnownOpenApiDocument","parameters":[],"responses":{"200":{"description":"This OpenAPI document.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object"}},"application/yaml":{"schema":{"type":"string"}}}}},"security":[],"summary":"This document, at its well-known URI","tags":["Meta"],"x-codeSamples":[{"lang":"shell","label":"curl","source":"curl \"$TRAYO_API_URL/.well-known/openapi\""},{"lang":"python","label":"Python (requests)","source":"import os\nimport requests\n\nBASE = os.environ.get(\"TRAYO_API_URL\", \"https://api.trayo.ai\")\n\nr = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/.well-known/openapi\")\nbody = r.json()\nif not r.ok:\n    err = body[\"error\"]\n    raise SystemExit(f\"{r.status_code} {err['code']} ({err['retry']}): {err['message']}\")\nprint(body)"}]}}},"info":{"title":"Trayo API","description":"**Permissions:** each authenticated REST operation publishes `x-trayo-scope-requirements`\nand a readable summary of its required permissions. MCP checks permissions per tool;\nread each tool’s `_meta[\"trayo/scopeRequirements\"]`. Read `GET /v1/whoami` for your\nkey’s configured scopes, current effective permissions and restrictions.\nRequest validation, workspace access rules and plan eligibility still apply.\n\nDefine accounts (companies) and signals (what you want to detect), run\ndiscovery on demand, read the events discovery produces.\n\n**Start with `GET /v1/whoami`.** It confirms the key and returns the\nworkspace, the plan, `canInitiate` and the lookup\nlimits — the numbers to plan against before you start. Then pick\na **recipe**: the call sequences that make up a task (track companies and\nread events; find lookalike companies; find and keep prospects; stakeholders at a company with\ncontact details; a brief before outreach; recent movers) are published at\n`GET /v1/recipes`, carried in this document as `x-recipes`, and rendered\nin `/llms.txt`. Each step names the operation, what it does in that\nsequence, and for a poll step the condition that ends the loop. Every\noperation below also carries `x-codeSamples` — a `curl` and a Python\nsample generated from its own parameters and request schema.\n\nCreate or reuse accounts and signals. Then call `POST /v1/discoveries` with the account IDs, signal keys, and lookback window.\nAdd `people: \"add\"` when you want the people who matter to each event added and listed on it; by default a run adds no people.\n\n**Give a new account the strongest identity you have.** Send its bare\n`linkedinHandle` whenever you know the LinkedIn company page; it is checked\nbefore the website `url`, then the name. A correct handle at create time\nmakes a `company_not_found` result less likely.\n\n**Discovery is ASYNCHRONOUS.** The POST returns 202 immediately with a run\nwhose `status` is `running` — it has not searched anything yet. Poll\n`GET /v1/discoveries/{runId}` until `settledAt` is non-null, then read\nthe events standing for its scope with `GET /v1/events?discoveryRunId={runId}`.\nThat scope is everything the run wrote — at any event date, because a job\nchange is dated by the month the job STARTED and can predate the lookback —\nplus the canonical events matching the run's accounts, signals and lookback\nwindow, including ones earlier runs wrote. Paged to the end, a settled run\ntherefore yields at least `eventsNew` events — one page is capped and need\nnot, so follow `nextCursor` before comparing anything to that counter.\nReading it before `settledAt` returns what the run has written so far.\n\n**Run your signals together, not one at a time.** Every event carries\n`signalKeys`, the keys of the signals that matched it, so a single run over\nmany signals stays attributable event by event. Do not split a run per\nsignal to find out which one fired. `signalType` will not tell you — it is\nthe kind of source a signal reads (`news`, `jobs`, `job_change`) and your\nsignals share a handful of those between them.\n\n**`settledAt` is the finish line.** A run has two halves — searching your\naccounts, then writing what the search found as events — and it is final\nonly when both are done. `settledAt` is set at that instant, `status` reads\n`completed` or `failed` at the same instant, and from then on the candidate\nand event counts are frozen: they are the run's receipt and stay what they\nwere even if you later delete some of the events it created.\n\n`completedAt` marks only the first half, the search. It can be set while\n`status` is still `running`, because the events from that search are still\nbeing written. **Do not poll on `completedAt`, and do not try to detect the\nend by watching `eventsNew` stop changing** — a pause between two writes\nlooks exactly like the end of a run and is not one. Wait for `settledAt`.\n\n`status` is the POLLING signal: it tells you when to stop calling, nothing\nmore. `candidatesScreened`, `candidatesMatched` and `eventsNew` are the RUN\nRECEIPT — what this execution screened, what matched a signal, and what it\nwrote — not the size of the scoped events page. Candidates are not events:\n`candidatesScreened: 12` with `candidatesMatched: 0` means nothing matched,\nand `bySignal` gives both counts per signal, so a signal that matched nothing\nshows 0. `eventsFound` is the deprecated name for `candidatesScreened`. Read the page,\n`error`, and `blockedSignals`; even a `completed` run with a non-null `error`\nended without doing everything it was asked to.\n\n**A run also says what it could NOT search.** `blockedSignals`, on the 202\nand on every poll, names each ready signal that cannot produce results for\npart of the run, why, and — in `accountIds` — WHICH accounts. Read it before\nconcluding from `eventsNew: 0` that there was nothing to find: an account\nthat was not searched is indistinguishable from a real empty result on the\ncounts alone.\n\nYou can use a new signal key in discovery immediately.\nThese outcomes apply to every signal type, including `news`. While a run is active, keep polling the same run. `account_not_ready` means Trayo could not search the account this time. After the run settles, retry the affected account IDs. `company_not_found` means Trayo could not identify the company from the supplied details. For `company_not_found`, check the named accounts before starting another discovery. If an identity is wrong, send the correct `linkedinHandle` with `trayo_update_account` over MCP, or with `PATCH /v1/accounts/{id}` and a workspace API key over REST. When no handle is known, send a corrected website `url` instead. Both need `accounts:write`. `trayo_update_account` also reports whether Trayo can now identify the company. Importing the same hostname again skips the existing account and does not update it. After the current run settles, start a new discovery for the corrected account IDs.\n\n**Re-running an identical discovery is safe.** Results are deduplicated\nagainst everything already in the workspace, so calling the same\naccounts/signals/lookback again typically returns `eventsNew: 0` and creates\nno duplicate events. The `discoveryRunId` event read still returns the\nmatching events that already stand for that scope. Zero is SUCCESS, not\nfailure, and not a reason to retry. A retry loop that treats `eventsNew: 0`\nas an error will never terminate.\n\n**Errors** are always `{ \"error\": { type, code, retry, message, param,\nrequestId } }`. `code` identifies the reason from the documented set.\nEvery failure includes a code, including request validation failures.\n`retry` tells you what to DO about it without parsing the message:\n`fix_input` (change the request), `retry_later` (send the same request again\nshortly, with backoff and a FINITE number of attempts), `do_not_retry` (it\nwill never work). Branch on `code`; fall back to `retry` when you only need\nto decide whether to send the request again, or when you meet a `code` you\ndo not recognise — that fallback is what lets a client written today keep\nworking against an error added tomorrow. The full table, with every code's\nstatus and retry class, is in the `Error` schema.\n\nTwo 409s make the point: `idempotency_in_progress` and\n`idempotency_key_reused` share a status and demand OPPOSITE responses —\nrepeat the identical request with the same key, versus never send that\nrequest again unchanged. Never infer recovery from the HTTP status.\n\n**Rate limits.** Every route shares the workspace budget, in two buckets, each a\nrolling 60-second window. A workspace starts with 120\nrequests per minute for the API and a separate\n7 per minute for the routes\nthat do the most work per call, `POST /v1/discoveries`, `POST /v1/find`, `POST /v1/accounts/lookalikes`, `POST /v1/companies/competitors`, `POST /v1/posts/search`, `POST /v1/posts/search/keywords`, `POST /v1/research/person/batch`, `POST /v1/stakeholders/search/batch` and `POST /v1/people/enrich/batch`; a call spends one\nbucket or the other, never both, and each MCP tool names the bucket it spends in its description and\n`_meta[\"trayo/rateLimitBucket\"]`. REST, MCP, all API keys and OAuth users share\nthe same workspace buckets; adding credentials does not increase throughput.\nSupport can adjust these defaults for a workspace, so read your budget rather than\nhardcoding these numbers: EVERY authenticated response, successful ones included, carries\n`RateLimit-Limit`, `RateLimit-Remaining` and `RateLimit-Reset` (seconds\nuntil the window frees up) for the bucket that request was counted in. That\nis how you slow down BEFORE being refused. Over the limit is\n`429 rate_limited` with `Retry-After` in seconds: wait that long, then send\nthe same request again.\n\n**Fanning out is what actually hits this** — a hundred concurrent\ncalls to any route are a hundred requests in one window, not one — and\n**`GET /v1/whoami` is limited like everything else**, so a\nbalance poll on a timer spends the same budget as the work it is watching.\nBack the poll off with the rest of your client, or drop it: the\n`RateLimit-*` headers on the responses you are already getting say more,\nsooner, for nothing. A per-network limit also sits in front of every `/v1`\nroute, before the key is read: a burst from one network can be refused\nthere, and that 429 carries `Retry-After` and no `RateLimit-*`. It is the\nonly limit on the unauthenticated document routes under `/v1` — fetch the\ndocument once and reuse it.\n\n**Usage limits.** Public REST and MCP usage quotas and daily usage caps are\ndisabled for now. Lookup allowances report `null` in `GET /v1/whoami`\n(MCP: `trayo_whoami`). Usage is still recorded; workspace request pacing still applies.\nAuthentication, permissions, workspace lifecycle and request validation still apply.\n\n**Pagination.** Six list routes — `GET /v1/accounts`, `GET /v1/people`,\n`GET /v1/events`, `GET /v1/discoveries`, `GET /v1/lists`,\n`GET /v1/lists/{id}/members` — return `{ data, hasMore,\nnextCursor }`; follow `nextCursor` until `hasMore` is false.\n`POST /v1/find` also paginates when you send only `filters`: repeat the\nsame request with `nextCursor` as `cursor`, preserving the filters, until\n`hasMore` is false. Any search with a `query`, including one that also\nsends `filters`, returns one ranked page and rejects a `cursor`.\n`GET /v1/signals`, `POST /v1/stakeholders/search` and the research routes\ndo not paginate. `GET /v1/signals` carries the list envelope with\n`hasMore` always false. `POST /v1/job-changes/search` pages with its own\n`limit`/`cursor`/`nextCursor` on the body, not on the query string, and\nonly when you send `destination`.\n\n**Naming across routes:** two things go by different names depending on\nthe route, and nothing is renamed for you — map them at your boundary.\nThe **company website** is `url` on an account, `domain` on the `company`\nblock of `POST /v1/people`, and `website` on the routes that take a company\nreference (`POST /v1/research/company`, `POST /v1/stakeholders/search`,\n`POST /v1/job-changes/search`, `POST /v1/contacts/lookup`); a\n`POST /v1/find` accounts row carries both `domain` and `url`. The\n**LinkedIn page** is a bare handle in an account's `linkedinHandle` and in\na person's own `linkedinUsername`, and a full URL in `linkedinUrl` on the\ncompany references and on find results. Different names, the same company\nwebsite and the same LinkedIn page.\n\n**Prospecting:** `POST /v1/find` searches for companies and people.\nFor direct stored-data search, send `mode: \"direct\"` with exact `filters`\nand a limit up to 100. For people, company filters select their current\nemployer and `filters.title` selects the person; each row includes both.\nDirect mode does not accept a sentence query or automatically expand criteria.\nA company without a website is still returned; use its ID for follow-up searches.\nCheck `truncated` and `notes`; per-company limits can leave additional people unseen.\n`POST /v1/posts/search/keywords` directly searches stored LinkedIn posts:\n`concepts` is an AND of groups, each containing OR phrase alternatives.\nThis supports explicit query decomposition and synonym expansion in one call.\nIts results rank keyword relevance within a bounded sample of 200 ranked candidates, with coverage even when empty.\nIt searches at most seven days of the recent-post index (bodies of at least 120 characters).\nRetrieval is always non-exhaustive; an empty result cannot prove absence.\nDirect searches use an eight-second request budget and shared capacity limits.\nOn `data_search_busy`, wait for `details.retryAfterSeconds`; on\n`data_search_timeout`, narrow the criteria. Neither error means no matches.\n`POST /v1/accounts/lookalikes` finds companies similar to supplied seeds.\nBoth return candidates without saving them — you post selected results\nback to `/v1/accounts/batch` or `/v1/people/batch` to bring them in.\n`POST /v1/companies/competitors` ranks the competitors of one company.\nFind with a sentence query draws on your search quota per search that runs; contact lookups (below)\ndraw on your plan's lookup allowance. Research, stakeholder search and\nasking about a person draw on the same usage quota per answer returned.\nNothing else in this API is metered.\n\n**Working sets:** `/v1/lists` is where the set of people or accounts you\nare acting on lives between calls. Create one, add members by `personId`\nor `accountId` with a `via` that records how they got there (`find`,\n`signal`, `import`, `manual`), then hand the LIST — not your session — to\nwhatever acts on it: a CRM push, a campaign, a human. Adding a member who is\nalready there is a skip, not an error, so the same batch is safe to send\ntwice. Lists are scoped to the user your key acts as, and show up in the\nTrayo app under that user. Do not mark a working set with `starred`, a\nperson's `note`, or a marker in `title` — that is what lists are for.\n\n**Ranking:** every account carries `scores` — Trayo's own view of how\nmuch is happening there — so you do not have to rebuild a ranking by\ncounting events. `scores.timing.score` (0–100, normalized against your\nworkspace's hottest account, as the product defines it) is the number for\n\"who is worth working this week\"; `scores.timing.raw` is the un-normalized\nvalue that holds still for absolute thresholds;\n`scores.activity` adds the event count, average significance and relevance,\nand a generated prose `summary` of what the events add up to. Both are\nnull until Trayo has scored the account, and nothing in this API\ntriggers scoring. `GET /v1/accounts` does not sort by them yet: page\nthrough and sort client-side.\n\n**Contact enrichment:** `POST /v1/people/{id}/enrich` finds a person's\nemail and/or phone the same way the Trayo app's own \"Find email\" does,\nand `POST /v1/people/enrich/batch` accepts up to 200 ids per call. Its\n45-second budget for starting lookups is checked once, before anything is\nreserved; the whole batch starts together in a few seconds. The batch answers `200`\nwith partial results. Retain the submitted ids: `skipped[].index` maps to\nthat request. Re-send rows skipped because time ran out in smaller batches;\nnothing was started or charged for them. Other skip reasons, including\nallowance refusals and invalid ids, require their own remedy. Single-person\nlookup requests answer `202`; both routes use `GET /v1/people/{id}/enrich` to poll.\nThese lookups are\nexplicit (nothing is looked up on create or read), asynchronous, idempotent\n(re-sending never double-runs or is charged twice — a field already\nrunning, already found, blocked by an email you wrote, or inside its retry\ncooldown is reported in `skipped`, not raised), and governed by your plan:\neach lookup counts against the\nplan's lookup limit (`402 lookup_limit_reached` before anything runs).\nEvery found value carries\n`source`, `status` and `foundAt`; a value you wrote is `source: \"manual\"`\nand is never overwritten by a found one.\n\n**Workspace settings:** `PATCH /v1/workspace` sets your stakeholder\ndefinition — plain prose describing who buys and owns what you sell, and\nwho to skip — plus `solutions` and `solutionsBrief`, what you sell. The\ndefinition steers stakeholder search and the per-event people (with\n`reasoning`) that a discovery run started with `people: \"add\"` attaches;\nthe default, `people: \"none\"`, attaches none. Without it stakeholder search seeds\non seniority alone and no people are attached to events. **Set it FIRST,\nbefore you run discovery** — it applies to work\nthat starts after it is set, not retroactively. The definition is carried as\n`stakeholderCriteria` on the workspace and as `definition` on stakeholder\nsearch.\n\n**Stakeholders:** `POST /v1/stakeholders/search` takes a company — any\ncompany by its website, or an account of yours — and a stakeholder definition,\nand returns the people at it who fit, best first, each with a reason.\nSynchronous, seconds, read-only: nothing is written, import the ones you\nwant with `POST /v1/people/batch`. It is the product's own stakeholder\nfinding (definition → keywords → candidate search → selection) without the\npersistence, so it works for a company you have never touched. Omit the\ndefinition to use the workspace's; the response says which applied.\nEach person carries `matchedPersona` and each company `coverage` (every\npersona, and whether anyone matched it); each label is checked against the\njob's function and seniority. When nobody fits, `nearMisses` holds the\nclosest candidates flagged `belowThreshold: true`. Repeating a search\nwithin a week normally returns the same people. For many companies,\n`POST /v1/stakeholders/search/batch` takes up to 50 in one call and searches\nthem ten at a time, reporting each in `results` or `errors` by `index`.\n\n**Recent moves:** `POST /v1/job-changes/search` finds people who changed\ncompany. Send `source` (the company left), `destination` (the company\njoined), or both. Without a company, send `title` (the new role, same\nterms as `/v1/find` `filters.title`), optionally with `destinationFilters`\n(`hq.countries`, `headcount` of the company joined). Inclusive `startedSince` and\nexclusive `startedBefore` bound the start month for either kind of search. `startedSince` (the\nmonth the new role started) narrows either kind of search: \"who became\nCISO since August at US companies over 500 people\" is one call, and so is\n\"who joined Stripe as an executive since September\". It returns moves\nobserved in the last 90 days — the person, the two companies, the title on\neach side, when the move was detected, and when the new role started to the\nmonth — and writes nothing. One row per person per destination.\n`limit` sets the page size: 25 by default, 100 at most, capped rather than\nrejected. `hasMore` says more matches may remain behind this page; send\n`nextCursor` back as `cursor`, verbatim and with the same search, to walk\nthem. The walk resumes where the page stopped, so a later page neither\nrepeats nor skips what an earlier one returned. `hasMore` reads the row\ncount before duplicate records are collapsed, so a page can come back\nshort and still be `true` — follow `hasMore` and `nextCursor`, never the\nrow count. A source-only search may read a fixed sample rather than an ordered\nwalk: only that sampled search cannot page, and sending a cursor is rejected.\nIndexed source-only searches accept cursors. For a sampled source-only search,\n`nextCursor` is null, and `hasMore: true` means narrow the\nsearch. Report truncation\nfor the requested period. `detectedSince` filters detection recency: only moves with\n`detectedAt >=` the value you send — the date the move was DETECTED, not the\ndate the role started, which startedSince and startedBefore filter. It only narrows the 90-day\nwindow, starting at midnight UTC 90 days ago: an earlier value is clamped to\nthat start and a future value matches nothing. Destination searches already return\nthe newest moves first: narrowing the window does not recover omitted matches;\nit returns the same rows or a subset. This is a recency filter, not pagination.\n`seniority` is the second filter: it keeps only moves INTO a role at that\nlevel or above, read from the title of the role they joined — not the one\nthey left, and not a title list you supply. The four seniority levels widen\nin order: `cxo` (the C-suite), `vp` (adds VP, SVP, EVP, Vice President and\nPresident), `director` (adds Director), `head` (adds Partner, Principal and\nHead of). With `destination`, it WIDENS the search rather than trimming the page — the search\nreads further through recent moves looking for matches instead of filtering\nthe slice it would have read without it — and that wider read is still\nbounded, so a short or empty answer does not prove nobody senior joined.\nSource-only searches that report `sampled: true` filter the same fixed sample; they do not read further. Title matching is heuristic and excludes assistant/support roles.\n`sampled: true` means a source-only search read a small\nfixed sample of recent moves: an empty answer does not mean nobody left,\nand retrying gives the same answer while the underlying data is unchanged.\nA source-only search with `sampled: false` walked the newest moves out of\nthat company instead of sampling them.\nWith `destination`, `sampled` is false: the search reads a bounded slice of\nthe newest moves into that company before filtering by source.\n`hasMore: false` does not prove completeness with either value of `sampled`.\nEvery row is a move between two companies; promotions and same-company\ntitle changes never appear here. For hires and promotions at a watched\ncompany, use the workspace `job_change` signal (`create_signal`, then\n`run_discovery`). That signal is not a departure search and does not provide\na complete list of who left. Import the people you want with\n`POST /v1/people/batch`.\n\n**Research:** `POST /v1/research/company` and `POST /v1/research/person`\nreturn the quick overview the Trayo app opens its drawer with — for a\ncompany: what it does, `whyNow` hooks from its recent updates, and `fit`\nagainst what you sell; for a person: career, likely challenges, and the\nangles that tie their role to what you sell. Synchronous, stateless,\nread-only: one read of Trayo's own data, one generated answer, nothing stored,\nnothing written, any company or person we hold — not only the ones in your\nworkspace. Both read your `solutions` and stakeholder definition from the\nworkspace for the seller side of the answer.\n\n`POST /v1/research/person/batch` is the person route for up to\n10 people in one call, always ungrounded, reading your seller\ncontext once for the whole batch. A person it cannot resolve or answer for\nis reported in `errors` by its `index`, with the same `code` and `retry` an\nerror response carries, so one bad profile never costs you the rest of the\nbatch. An overview that came back empty is one of those errors\n(`person_profile_too_thin`), never a blank result.\n\n**Contact lookup without a person:** `POST /v1/contacts/lookup` takes a name\nplus a LinkedIn profile or a company website and returns that person's email\nin the same response, for somebody who is not in your workspace and does not\nhave to be. Ask for `fields: [\"phone\"]` and it answers `202` with a\n`lookupId` to collect from `GET /v1/contacts/lookups/{lookupId}` — the phone\nlookup can take several minutes. One lookup per\nfield, against your plan's allowance for that field — email and phone have\nseparate limits, and a lookup here draws on the same allowance as a lookup\non a person. Asking again for the same person reads the stored answer for\nnothing.\n\n**Ask about a person:** `POST /v1/people/{id}/ask` answers one question\nabout one person in your workspace from everything on record — the Trayo\nrecord (contact details, the account and its research, the signals the\nperson is attached to and why, the sequences and emails sent with their\noutcomes, lists, notes) plus the LinkedIn profile Trayo holds for them\n(work history, recent posts). Send an `intent` — what you will do with the\nanswer — to steer focus and form. Synchronous, seconds, read-only,\ngrounded in that dossier only: nothing is searched, nothing is guessed,\nand `sources` is a receipt of what Trayo read. Each answer draws on\nyour usage quota.\n\n**Which of the two to ask.** `POST /v1/research/person` is a FIXED overview\nof ANY person Trayo holds, built from their public profile — use it for\nsomeone you have just found and do not have. `POST /v1/people/{id}/ask`\ntakes YOUR question about a person you already hold, and is the only route\nthat can see your own history with them: what discovery attached to them,\nwhat you sent, whether they replied. \"Who is this person\" is research;\n\"did we ever email her, and is she worth a sequence\" is ask.\n\n**Limits go two ways, on purpose.** `POST /v1/find`'s `limit` CLAMPS at 50.\nA `/v1/…/batch` array over its cap is an ERROR — 200 items on the write\nbatches, 10 on `POST /v1/research/person/batch`. Silently dropping\nbatch rows would lose records you believe you created; rejecting an over-large\nfind `limit` would draw on your search quota for a number you could have read\nhere.\n\n**Auth:** every route below requires `Authorization: Bearer <key>` except\na few unauthenticated discovery routes, so a caller can find and read\nthis document before it has a key configured: `GET /` and `GET /v1` return\na small JSON index naming the document and how to authenticate, and this\ndocument itself is served at `GET /openapi.json`,\n`GET /.well-known/openapi` and `GET /v1/openapi.yaml`. All three are the\nSAME document; the extension picks the default serialization and an\n`Accept` header of `application/json` or `application/yaml` overrides it.\nThe same reference as Markdown is at `GET /llms.txt` (a short index) and\n`GET /llms-full.txt` (everything, in one file); `GET /v1/recipes` is\nunauthenticated too.","version":"1.0.0","contact":{}},"tags":[{"name":"Accounts","description":"Companies you track. Discovery runs against accounts, and each one carries `scores` — Trayo's ranking of how much is happening there."},{"name":"Signals","description":"Named definitions of what counts as a noteworthy event. A discovery run scans for events matching your ready signals."},{"name":"Discoveries","description":"On-demand runs that scan accounts for signal matches and produce events. Asynchronous: start one, then poll it until `settledAt` is set."},{"name":"Events","description":"What discovery found. Every event names the signals it matched in `signalKeys`, so one run over many signals is attributable event by event. Delete one to dismiss it; it will not come back."},{"name":"People","description":"Contacts at accounts you track — and the lookups that find their emails and phones, with provenance."},{"name":"Lists","description":"Working sets you curate — pinned people and whole-account entries, each with provenance. The bridge from what you found to what you act on, and the only way a set outlives the session that built it."},{"name":"Find","description":"Search for companies and people that are NOT yet in your workspace — by a sentence, by exact filters, or both. Every other resource here operates on records you already have; this is the only entry point that brings new ones in. It never writes — results are shaped to be posted to `POST /v1/accounts/batch` and `POST /v1/people/batch`."},{"name":"Workspace","description":"Who your key is (`GET /v1/whoami`: workspace, user, plan, limits) and the settings that steer discovery and stakeholder search: your stakeholder definition and what you sell. One workspace per key."},{"name":"Research","description":"Quick overviews of a company or a person — the app's own drawer synthesis, as stateless calls: one generated answer over the record Trayo holds, nothing stored, nothing written."},{"name":"Meta","description":"Machine-readable API description: this document, the index, and the recipes. Unauthenticated."}],"servers":[{"url":"https://api.trayo.ai"}],"components":{"securitySchemes":{"bearerAuth":{"scheme":"bearer","bearerFormat":"JWT","type":"http","description":"A single static key, e.g. `Authorization: Bearer sk_live_...`. The key implicitly identifies your workspace and an owning user — there is no separate workspace id to pass anywhere."}},"schemas":{"ErrorDto":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"type":{"type":"string","enum":["invalid_request_error","authentication_error","authorization_error","not_found_error","conflict_error","api_error"],"description":"Coarse class, derived directly from the HTTP status (400 -> invalid_request_error, 401 -> authentication_error, 403 -> authorization_error, 404 -> not_found_error, 409 -> conflict_error, anything else including a 500 -> api_error). The HTTP status is in turn fixed by `code`, per the table below — status, `type`, `code` and `retry` are always mutually consistent, so no response can pair a 404 with advice to retry it."},"code":{"type":"string","enum":["data_search_busy","data_search_timeout","validation_failed","malformed_cursor","invalid_date","unknown_account","unknown_signal","unauthorized","insufficient_scope","forbidden","not_found","account_not_found","signal_not_found","event_not_found","discovery_run_not_found","person_not_found","list_not_found","list_member_not_found","method_not_allowed","idempotency_in_progress","conflict","signal_key_conflict","idempotency_key_reused","list_in_use","quota_daily_limit","quota_exceeded","lookup_limit_reached","lookup_start_failed","contact_lookup_not_found","phone_lookup_failed","phone_lookup_expired","contact_lookup_failed","company_not_found","company_resolution_timed_out","job_change_search_not_configured","job_change_search_failed","lookalike_search_not_configured","lookalike_search_failed","competitor_roster_not_configured","competitor_roster_failed","post_search_not_configured","post_search_failed","stakeholder_search_not_configured","stakeholder_search_failed","stakeholder_search_not_found","person_ask_not_configured","person_ask_failed","person_profile_not_found","person_profile_too_thin","research_not_configured","research_failed","find_needs_indexed_filter","rate_limited","internal_error","find_not_configured","find_response_failed","discovery_run_too_large","mcp_result_delivery_failed","mcp_result_not_found","mcp_result_expired","mcp_tool_removed","find_unavailable","find_timeout"],"description":"Why the request failed. This enum lists the codes that the API currently returns.\nEvery `/v1` failure includes a code and retry instructions.\n\nUse `code` to identify the failure and `retry` to decide what to do next.\nIf you do not recognize a code, follow its `retry` value.\n\nThe status and recovery class each code is served with:\n\n| code | status | retry | what it means / what to do |\n\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n\n| `data_search_busy` | 503 | `retry_later` | Hosted search capacity (direct Find, post keyword search, job-change search) is in use: your workspace already has as many of these searches running as it may, or the service is at capacity. Nothing ran. Wait for details.retryAfterSeconds, then retry, and send fewer at once. |\n\n| `data_search_timeout` | 503 | `fix_input` | A hosted search (Find by filters, with or without `mode: direct`; post keyword search; job-change search) ran out of time. Change what `message` names and retry; resending the same search runs out of time again, and a timeout is not an empty result. |\n\n| `validation_failed` | 400 | `fix_input` | The request did not pass input validation: a missing or malformed body field, a bad `limit`, a path parameter that is not a UUID, a `signalKey` that already exists or is reserved. `message` lists every failed constraint; `param` names the first offending field when one can be identified. |\n\n| `malformed_cursor` | 400 | `fix_input` | `cursor` was not a value this API issued. Send a previous page's `nextCursor` verbatim, or omit it to start over. |\n\n| `invalid_date` | 400 | `fix_input` | A date filter (`updatedSince`, `since`, `detectedSince`) did not parse. Send a plain date (`2026-06-07`, read as midnight UTC) or a full ISO-8601 timestamp (`2026-06-07T14:30:00Z`). Relative words such as `yesterday` or `last-quarter` are not accepted. `param` names the field. |\n\n| `unknown_account` | 400 | `fix_input` | One or more `accountIds` do not exist in your workspace. `message` lists them. Create them first or drop them from the request. |\n\n| `unknown_signal` | 400 | `fix_input` | One or more `signalKeys` do not exist in your workspace. `message` lists them. |\n\n| `unauthorized` | 401 | `do_not_retry` | Missing, malformed, or incorrect bearer token. Identical body for every cause. |\n\n| `insufficient_scope` | 403 | `do_not_retry` | Scope denial details distinguish missing_key_scope (use a key granting every missing scope), owner_permission_limit (the owner needs the missing workspace permissions), and invalid_key_scope (replace the key with supported scopes). Membership and undeclared-route denials remain generic. |\n\n| `forbidden` | 403 | `do_not_retry` | The API key is valid but lacks a required scope. `message` identifies the missing scope to request; retrying with the same key will not help. |\n\n| `not_found` | 404 | `do_not_retry` | The generic 404: a resource that does not exist and that none of the specific codes covers. `message` says which. |\n\n| `account_not_found` | 404 | `do_not_retry` | No such account in your workspace. Another workspace's account is indistinguishable from a non-existent one. |\n\n| `signal_not_found` | 404 | `do_not_retry` | No such signal key, or it is product-managed/person-entity and not addressable here. |\n\n| `event_not_found` | 404 | `do_not_retry` | No such event in your workspace, or it has not finished processing and is not addressable yet. |\n\n| `discovery_run_not_found` | 404 | `do_not_retry` | No such run in your workspace. |\n\n| `person_not_found` | 404 | `do_not_retry` | No such person in your workspace. Another workspace's person is indistinguishable from a non-existent one. |\n\n| `list_not_found` | 404 | `do_not_retry` | No such list for this key. Lists are scoped to the user your key acts as, so a list another user created in the same workspace is indistinguishable from a non-existent one. |\n\n| `list_member_not_found` | 404 | `do_not_retry` | No such member on this list. `memberId` is the MEMBERSHIP row's `id` from `GET /v1/lists/{id}/members` — not the person's or account's id. |\n\n| `method_not_allowed` | 405 | `fix_input` | This path exists but does not accept the method you used. The `Allow` RESPONSE HEADER lists the methods it does accept and `message` names the call to make instead. THE RESOURCE IS REAL — do not treat this like a 404 and give up on it. |\n\n| `idempotency_in_progress` | 409 | `retry_later` | This operation is still in progress. Retry the same request with the same Idempotency-Key. |\n\n| `conflict` | 409 | `fix_input` | The generic 409: the request collides with existing state, and none of the specific codes covers it. `message` says what. |\n\n| `signal_key_conflict` | 409 | `fix_input` | A signal with this `signalKey` already exists with a different definition. Choose another key, `PATCH` the existing one, or delete it first. Repeating a create with the same definition is not a conflict: it returns the saved signal. |\n\n| `idempotency_key_reused` | 409 | `fix_input` | This `Idempotency-Key` was already used with a different request body. Repeating this request unchanged will keep failing; use a new key. |\n\n| `list_in_use` | 409 | `do_not_retry` | An outreach play still references this list, so it cannot be deleted. Plays are managed in the Trayo app, not here — remove the reference there, then delete. Repeating this call unchanged will keep failing. |\n\n| `quota_daily_limit` | 429 | `retry_later` | The workspace daily usage limit blocks new work. Wait for recent usage to leave the 24-hour window, or contact support; changing scopes does not help. |\n\n| `quota_exceeded` | 402 | `do_not_retry` | This workspace has insufficient quota for this operation. Retrying or changing the request does not help; raise the quota or wait for it to renew. |\n\n| `lookup_limit_reached` | 402 | `do_not_retry` | This workspace cannot run this contact lookup: the plan's email or phone lookup limit is reached, or the plan does not include that kind of lookup. `message` says which and quotes the limit. Retrying never helps and neither does changing the request — the plan has to change. Nothing was started and nothing was charged. |\n\n| `lookup_start_failed` | 503 | `retry_later` | The contact lookup passed every check but could not be started. No lookup is running for it, and a retry of the same request is not charged twice. Send it again shortly. |\n\n| `contact_lookup_not_found` | 404 | `do_not_retry` | No such `lookupId` in your workspace. Another workspace's lookup is indistinguishable from one that never existed. The id comes from a `POST /v1/contacts/lookup` response. |\n\n| `phone_lookup_failed` | 503 | `retry_later` | Accepted phone work failed. GET polling returns HTTP 200 with status failed and this nested reason. Stop polling this ID; retry a new POST later. No automatic refund. |\n\n| `phone_lookup_expired` | 503 | `retry_later` | Accepted phone work exceeded its supported lifetime. GET polling returns HTTP 200 with status failed and this nested reason. Stop polling this ID; retry a new POST later. No automatic refund. |\n\n| `contact_lookup_failed` | 503 | `retry_later` | The email lookup could not be completed: it failed or ran past its time budget. Nothing was charged, nothing was stored, and no allowance was consumed. Send the same request again shortly. A lookup that RAN and found nothing is a `200` with `status: \"not_found\"`, not this. |\n\n| `company_not_found` | 404 | `do_not_retry` | We could not identify this company — not from the account's own record, nor from a LinkedIn page, website (including its redirect), or name — so there are no people to search. Retrying will not help. Send the company's own website if you did not; for any company, `POST /v1/find` on the contacts lane searches the web instead. From `POST /v1/find` with `filters.companyWebsites`, this means NO website resolved and nothing was searched; the message names every website. For one that is ambiguous (several possible companies on the domain) it also names the candidates and their ids: send the right id as `filters.companyIds`. When only some websites fail, the search runs over the rest and lists the others in `unresolvedWebsites`. |\n\n| `company_resolution_timed_out` | 503 | `retry_later` | Resolving the company by name timed out under load before we could answer. This is NOT a \"we do not have it\" result: nothing was recorded, and the same request sent again shortly will usually resolve. Companies sent by website or LinkedIn page do not take this path. |\n\n| `job_change_search_not_configured` | 503 | `do_not_retry` | Job-change search is unavailable. Retrying will not help. Contact support. |\n\n| `job_change_search_failed` | 503 | `retry_later` | The bounded lookup failed or ran past its time budget. Nothing was written. Send the same job-change request again shortly. |\n\n| `lookalike_search_not_configured` | 503 | `do_not_retry` | Lookalike search is unavailable. Retrying will not help. Contact support. |\n\n| `lookalike_search_failed` | 503 | `retry_later` | Lookalike search failed or exceeded its time budget. Nothing was saved; retry the same request shortly. |\n\n| `competitor_roster_not_configured` | 503 | `do_not_retry` | Competitor rosters are unavailable in this environment. Retrying will not help. Contact support. |\n\n| `competitor_roster_failed` | 503 | `retry_later` | Competitor roster generation failed or exceeded its 45 second budget. Nothing was saved; the previous roster, if any, is unchanged. Retry the same request shortly. |\n\n| `post_search_not_configured` | 503 | `do_not_retry` | Post search is unavailable. Retrying will not help. Contact support. |\n\n| `post_search_failed` | 503 | `retry_later` | The post search or engager read failed or exceeded its time budget. Nothing was saved; retry the same request shortly. |\n\n| `stakeholder_search_not_configured` | 503 | `do_not_retry` | Stakeholder search is unavailable. Retrying will not help. Contact support. For another way to find people, use `POST /v1/find` on the contacts lane. |\n\n| `stakeholder_search_failed` | 503 | `retry_later` | Stakeholder search failed or timed out. Nothing was saved. Send the same request again shortly. |\n\n| `stakeholder_search_not_found` | 404 | `do_not_retry` | No stakeholder search with this `searchId` for your credential. A batch search can be read for an hour after it starts, only with the credential that started it. Start the search again. |\n\n| `person_ask_not_configured` | 503 | `do_not_retry` | Questions about a person are unavailable. Retrying will not help. Contact support. To read the saved person record, use `GET /v1/people/{id}`. |\n\n| `person_ask_failed` | 503 | `retry_later` | The answer failed, came back unusable, or ran past the time budget. Nothing was written. Send the same request again shortly. A LinkedIn-profile failure is NOT this error: the answer proceeds on the Trayo record and `sources.linkedin.status` says `unavailable`. |\n\n| `person_profile_not_found` | 404 | `do_not_retry` | We hold no public profile for this person — the LinkedIn profile is not in our data, or the person in your workspace carries neither a match to it nor a LinkedIn username. Retrying will not help. Send the person's LinkedIn profile URL if you sent a `personId`. Distinct from `person_not_found`, which means there is no such person in your workspace at all. |\n\n| `person_profile_too_thin` | 404 | `fix_input` | The profile we hold for this person has too little in it for an overview built from it alone, so the overview came back empty. Sending the same request again gives the same result. Research this person on their own with `grounded: true`, which also searches the web. |\n\n| `research_not_configured` | 503 | `do_not_retry` | Company and person research are unavailable. Retrying will not help. Contact support. |\n\n| `research_failed` | 503 | `retry_later` | A research route failed or ran past the time budget. Nothing was written. Send the same request again shortly. |\n\n| `find_needs_indexed_filter` | 400 | `fix_input` | This filters-only search needs an indexed company lead. A people search or company search with a title cannot use country, founded year, technologies or company type alone; funding stage also needs an indexed lead. A company search without a title can use those filters alone, but checks only a bounded set of the largest companies (`led_by_headcount`). Add at least one of `filters.industries` (see `GET /v1/find/industries`), `filters.hq.cities`, `filters.hq.states` or a `filters.headcount` band, or send a `query` and let the sentence select the set. With no company criteria in the request, do not ask the user: read `buyerProfile` from `GET /v1/workspace`, map its industries to exact `GET /v1/find/industries` values for `filters.industries`, and send its `sizeBand` (max capped at 50,000) as `filters.headcount` when `buyerProfileSource` is `saved`. With a partial profile, no mapped industry or no profile, send `{\"min\": 1, \"max\": 10000}`, never `{\"min\": 1}` alone. |\n\n| `rate_limited` | 429 | `retry_later` | The workspace or source network exhausted its request budget for one bucket. `details.retryAfterSeconds` (and `Retry-After` on REST) is the wait: wait that long, then retry the same request once. Do not poll or retry sooner; an early retry is refused again. If you cannot wait, stop and tell the user when to retry; do not fill the wait with other calls. `details.limit` and `details.bucket` name the exhausted budget. When present, RateLimit-* headers describe the active budget and reset. |\n\n| `internal_error` | 500 | `retry_later` | Something failed on our side. `message` never describes it — quote `requestId` when reporting. Retry with exponential backoff and GIVE UP after a few attempts: `retry_later` here does not mean the failure is known to be transient, only that nothing about your request needs changing. A request that fails this way repeatedly will not start working. |\n\n| `find_not_configured` | 503 | `do_not_retry` | This type of search is unavailable. Nothing was charged. Retrying or rewording the request will not help. Contact support. The `message` lists any available alternatives, such as an exact company-name lookup or a filters-only search. |\n\n| `find_response_failed` | 500 | `do_not_retry` | The search completed and was charged, but its response could not be produced. The same Idempotency-Key preserves this outcome; a new key starts another paid search. Contact support. |\n\n| `discovery_run_too_large` | 400 | `fix_input` | The run asked for more accounts or signals than a run started through MCP covers. `details.requested` and `details.limits` carry the numbers. Split it into smaller runs, or start one larger run with `POST /v1/discoveries`, which accepts the bounds in `details.rest`. |\n\n| `mcp_result_delivery_failed` | 503 | `do_not_retry` | An MCP operation completed but its result file could not be saved. Do not automatically repeat a search: it may incur another charge. Read-only listings can be requested again with a smaller page and inline output. |\n\n| `mcp_result_not_found` | 404 | `do_not_retry` | No stored MCP result with this `resultId` is available to your credential. A result can be read only by the API key or OAuth user that created it, in the same workspace. Results are also removed some time after they expire. |\n\n| `mcp_result_expired` | 404 | `do_not_retry` | The stored MCP result has expired. Results can be read for four hours, or until the API key expires if that is sooner. Do not automatically repeat the original operation: a new search may incur another charge. Ask the user before running it again. |\n\n| `mcp_tool_removed` | 404 | `do_not_retry` | MCP only. The tool you called was removed from the MCP server. `message` names the tool that replaces it and how to move your arguments to it. Calling the removed name again, with any arguments, gives the same error; refresh your tool list. |\n\n| `find_unavailable` | 503 | `retry_later` | The search service failed. Wait, then send the same request again. A successful search with incomplete data returns 200 with `degraded: true`. |\n\n| `find_timeout` | 503 | `fix_input` | The search exceeded its time limit. Narrow the query or filters before trying again. A search that already started can still finish. Do not repeat the identical request. |\n\nNote the two 409s — `idempotency_in_progress` and\n`idempotency_key_reused`: they share a status and carry\nOPPOSITE instructions. The first is `retry_later` — send the identical\nrequest again with the same key. The second is `fix_input` — that exact\nrequest will never succeed, send a new key. This is precisely why `retry`\nexists as a field. Never infer recovery from the status."},"retry":{"type":"string","enum":["fix_input","retry_later","do_not_retry"],"description":"What to do about the failure, and the only field you need in order to decide\nwhether to send the request again.\n\n`fix_input` — the request is wrong; change it and retry.\n\n`retry_later` — the request is right, the system is not ready; retry it\nunchanged, with backoff and a FINITE number of attempts. On a 500\n(`internal_error`) this especially does not mean retry indefinitely: the\nfailure is not known to be transient, only that nothing about your request\nneeds changing, so give up after a few attempts rather than looping.\n\n`do_not_retry` — retrying will never help.\n\nFixed per `code`; see the table above. Always present, on every error,\nincluding any code added after this document — so a client that does not\nrecognise a `code` can still act correctly by reading this field alone."},"message":{"type":"string","description":"Human-readable, English, not guaranteed stable wording. Says what to do as well as what went wrong. Never parsed for control flow — that is what `code` and `retry` are for."},"param":{"description":"The request field this error is about, when there is a single identifiable one. Omitted (not `null`) otherwise — including when a validation failure names a field this API cannot extract unambiguously, in which case `message` still names it.","type":"string"},"details":{"description":"Scope denial details for insufficient_scope; retryAfterSeconds, limit and bucket for rate_limited; retryAfterSeconds for data_search_busy.","anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"reason":{"type":"string","enum":["missing_key_scope","owner_permission_limit","invalid_key_scope"]},"requiredScopes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"missingScopes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["reason","requiredScopes","missingScopes"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"retryAfterSeconds":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":9007199254740991},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":9007199254740991},"bucket":{"type":"string","enum":["default","expensive","handshake","transport"]}},"required":["retryAfterSeconds","limit","bucket"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"retryAfterSeconds":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":60}},"required":["retryAfterSeconds"],"additionalProperties":false}]},"requestId":{"type":"string","description":"Unique per error response. Not correlated with any other id in this API."}},"required":["type","code","retry","message","requestId"],"additionalProperties":false}},"required":["error"],"additionalProperties":false},"ScopeDenialDetailsDto":{"type":"object","properties":{"reason":{"type":"string","enum":["missing_key_scope","owner_permission_limit","invalid_key_scope"]},"requiredScopes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"missingScopes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["reason","requiredScopes","missingScopes"],"additionalProperties":false},"LookalikeSearchBodyDto":{"type":"object","properties":{"companies":{"minItems":1,"maxItems":50,"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"companyId":{"description":"Exact company dataset ID, as a number or numeric string. Reuse companyId from a lookalike result or id from a known company find result. This is not a workspace account UUID. When supplied, it takes precedence; a missing ID is reported as not_found without trying other fields.","anyOf":[{"type":"integer","exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991},{"type":"string","pattern":"^[1-9]\\d*$"}]},"linkedinUrl":{"description":"The company's LinkedIn page — the `linkedinUrl` a find result or a person row carries, copied through (`https://www.linkedin.com/company/zapier`); the bare handle (`zapier`) is accepted too. Tried first when present, and the most precise key there is. Showcase pages are not company pages: send the company's own. Copy the handle from a Trayo result or the company's own site rather than guessing it from the name — a slug that belongs to a different company resolves to that company.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048},"website":{"description":"The company's own website, as a URL or a domain (`https://zapier.com`, `zapier.com`). The strongest key after the LinkedIn page: it is matched against our data, then, on a miss, followed through a cross-domain redirect, so a legacy or vanity domain that forwards to the current site still resolves. Sent on its own as the bare site (no path or subdomain), a data or social platform's domain names the platform itself (`zoominfo.com` is ZoomInfo); a page on such a site (`linkedin.com/company/acme`) is not a company website. When our data files the company under a different website, a website sent on its own is also tried as the LinkedIn page it spells (`gong.io` as `gong-io`), accepted only for an established company whose name matches the domain. An alias that does not forward to the company's current site is a miss: send the current website, the LinkedIn page or the name. Does not have to be in your workspace.","type":"string","minLength":3,"maxLength":2048},"name":{"description":"The company name. Tried last and the weakest key, since a common name can match the wrong company — send the website when you have it. A name-only lookup finds only companies Trayo holds under that name; an employer that a Trayo person row names with `companyId: null` has no company record, and its name will usually miss.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Seed companies. Use companyId as an exact reference when supplied. Otherwise, try LinkedIn first, then its marketing website (including redirects), then its name. Stop at the first match."},"limit":{"default":100,"description":"Maximum number of candidates to return. Fewer may be available; there is no pagination.","type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":500},"matchSize":{"default":true,"description":"Keep results within the employee range of the seeds. On by default: when the seeds are your accounts or target accounts, size is part of a good match. Set false to find companies that do what the seeds do at any size, for example when the seeds are competitors in one niche.","type":"boolean"},"useWorkspaceAccounts":{"default":true,"description":"Rank results partly by where people at your workspace's accounts used to work: among companies similar to the seeds, the ones your accounts hire from rank higher. On by default. Set false to rank on the seeds alone.","type":"boolean"},"minEmployees":{"description":"Hard filter: keep only companies with at least this many employees. A company with an unknown employee count is left out unless includeUnknown is set. Either employee bound replaces the seed size range.","type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":9007199254740991},"maxEmployees":{"description":"Hard filter: keep only companies with at most this many employees. A company with an unknown employee count is left out unless includeUnknown is set. Either employee bound replaces the seed size range.","type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":9007199254740991},"countries":{"description":"Hard filter: the headquarters country, as ISO-2 codes (`[\"US\", \"DE\"]`) or country names (`[\"United States\", \"Germany\"]`), any case. A name is read as its ISO-2 code. A company with an unknown country is left out unless includeUnknown is set. Merged with regions.","minItems":1,"maxItems":250,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":2,"maxLength":80}},"regions":{"description":"Hard filter: shorthand for a block of countries (north_america, europe, asia_pacific, latin_america, middle_east, africa). Merged with countries.","minItems":1,"maxItems":6,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","enum":["north_america","europe","asia_pacific","latin_america","middle_east","africa"]}},"industries":{"description":"Hard filter: exact industry values, the same taxonomy as find (list them with trayo_list_industries or GET /v1/find/industries), case-insensitive. Several values are a union. An unrecognised value is a 400 that names it.","minItems":1,"maxItems":100,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"includeUnknown":{"default":false,"description":"Keep companies whose value for a filtered field is unknown instead of leaving them out. About 9.5% of companies have no known headquarters country and 3.5% no industry; employee counts are nearly always known. Kept rows show the unknown field as null.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["companies"],"additionalProperties":false},"LookalikeSearchResponseDto":{"type":"object","properties":{"seeds":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"input":{"type":"object","properties":{"companyId":{"description":"Exact company dataset ID, as a number or numeric string. Reuse companyId from a lookalike result or id from a known company find result. This is not a workspace account UUID. When supplied, it takes precedence; a missing ID is reported as not_found without trying other fields.","anyOf":[{"type":"integer","exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991},{"type":"string","pattern":"^[1-9]\\d*$"}]},"linkedinUrl":{"description":"The company's LinkedIn page — the `linkedinUrl` a find result or a person row carries, copied through (`https://www.linkedin.com/company/zapier`); the bare handle (`zapier`) is accepted too. Tried first when present, and the most precise key there is. Showcase pages are not company pages: send the company's own. Copy the handle from a Trayo result or the company's own site rather than guessing it from the name — a slug that belongs to a different company resolves to that company.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048},"website":{"description":"The company's own website, as a URL or a domain (`https://zapier.com`, `zapier.com`). The strongest key after the LinkedIn page: it is matched against our data, then, on a miss, followed through a cross-domain redirect, so a legacy or vanity domain that forwards to the current site still resolves. Sent on its own as the bare site (no path or subdomain), a data or social platform's domain names the platform itself (`zoominfo.com` is ZoomInfo); a page on such a site (`linkedin.com/company/acme`) is not a company website. When our data files the company under a different website, a website sent on its own is also tried as the LinkedIn page it spells (`gong.io` as `gong-io`), accepted only for an established company whose name matches the domain. An alias that does not forward to the company's current site is a miss: send the current website, the LinkedIn page or the name. Does not have to be in your workspace.","type":"string","minLength":3,"maxLength":2048},"name":{"description":"The company name. Tried last and the weakest key, since a common name can match the wrong company — send the website when you have it. A name-only lookup finds only companies Trayo holds under that name; an employer that a Trayo person row names with `companyId: null` has no company record, and its name will usually miss.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"additionalProperties":false},"company":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"companyId":{"type":"integer","exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"Company dataset ID. Reuse as companyId in a subsequent search."},"name":{"type":"string","description":"The company as Trayo records it."},"website":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The company's website domain as Trayo files it."},"linkedinUrl":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The company's LinkedIn page, when Trayo has it."},"resolvedBy":{"type":"string","enum":["account_match","company_id","linkedin","website","redirect","name"],"description":"Which supplied key identified this company. company_id is an exact lookup."},"nameMatch":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["exact","approximate"]},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Set only when `resolvedBy` is `name`, null otherwise. `exact`: the company's name equals the name looked up once legal suffixes (Inc, GmbH, Ltd) are dropped. `approximate`: the closest name Trayo holds, which can be a different company (\"CR Management Consulting\" answered with \"m3 management consulting\"). Check an `approximate` match against what you know of the company before using it, and leave it out when it does not fit."}},"required":["companyId","name","website","linkedinUrl","resolvedBy","nameMatch"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"null"}]},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["resolved","not_found","not_indexed"],"description":"resolved: contributed to the search. not_found: no company matched the input. not_indexed: the company matched but similarity data is unavailable for it."}},"required":["input","company","status"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"One entry per input, in the same order. Check the matched identity, especially for a name-only input."},"companies":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"companyId":{"type":"integer","exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"Company dataset ID. Reuse as companyId in a subsequent search."},"name":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"website":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"linkedinUrl":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"industry":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"sizeRange":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"sizeEmployees":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}]},"country":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"city":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"similarity":{"type":"string","enum":["high","medium","low"],"description":"Heuristic bands: high >= 0.85, medium >= 0.7, low below that. These are preliminary similarity bands, not probabilities."},"similarityScore":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":1,"description":"Similarity to the closest seed, from 0 to 1. Higher is closer."},"closestSeedIndex":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"Zero-based index into seeds for the closest contributing input. Duplicate identities use the first input."},"seedsMatched":{"type":"integer","exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"Number of distinct seed companies that retrieved this candidate."}},"required":["companyId","name","website","linkedinUrl","industry","sizeRange","sizeEmployees","country","city","similarity","similarityScore","closestSeedIndex","seedsMatched"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Candidates ranked best match first: a company close to several seeds ranks above one close to a single seed. Seed companies, their subsidiaries and sister brands, and repeat listings of one company are left out; see filtered. Other companies already in your workspace may appear. Nothing is saved."},"filtered":{"type":"object","properties":{"seedAffiliates":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"Candidates left out as a subsidiary, sister brand or another listing of a seed company."},"duplicates":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"Candidates left out as another listing of a company already in the results."},"outsideSeedSize":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"Candidates left out because their employee count is outside seedSizeRange."},"outsideFilters":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"Candidates retrieved and then left out by minEmployees, maxEmployees, countries, regions or industries. Most filtering happens inside the search, and companies it never retrieved are not counted, so this is usually 0 and is not the number of companies the filters excluded."},"seedSizeRange":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"minEmployees":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991},"maxEmployees":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991}},"required":["minEmployees","maxEmployees"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The employee range results were kept w