ou named it. nomination: named while the roster was generated, then matched to a company."},"rankReason":{"type":"string","enum":["pinned","incumbent","alignment"]},"similarity":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}]},"seedsMatched":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991},{"type":"null"}]},"customers":{"type":"object","properties":{"status":{"type":"string","enum":["not_scanned","pending","running","completed","failed"],"description":"Each roster call starts a background scan when the scan is missing or more than 30 days old. It takes a few minutes; call again to see it fill in. An entry with no website stays not_scanned."},"scrapedAt":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"ISO 8601; when the competitor's site was last read."},"pagesScraped":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991},"customersFound":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991},"customersResolved":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991},"error":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["no_pages_fetched","queue_unavailable","scan_failed"]},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Why the last scan failed, or null. no_pages_fetched: none of the competitor's pages could be read. queue_unavailable: the scan could not be started. scan_failed: any other failure. A failed scan is tried again on a roster request made at least 24 hours later."},"customers":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"domain":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"companyId":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer","exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Set when the name or domain matched a company in our data."},"evidenceKind":{"type":"string","enum":["logo","case_study","testimonial","review","customer_list"],"description":"Where on the competitor's site the customer appeared."},"sourceUrl":{"type":"string"},"quote":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The sentence or heading that named the customer, at most 240 characters."},"confidence":{"type":"string","enum":["high","medium","low"]},"flag":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["self","tenant"]},{"type":"null"}],"description":"self: the competitor named itself. tenant: it named the company this roster is for."}},"required":["name","domain","companyId","evidenceKind","sourceUrl","quote","confidence","flag"],"additionalProperties":false}}},"required":["status","scrapedAt","pagesScraped","customersFound","customersResolved","error","customers"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"The customers this competitor shows on its own website."}},"required":["rank","companyId","name","website","linkedinUrl","industry","sizeRange","verdict","productAlignment","icpAlignment","reason","source","rankReason","similarity","seedsMatched","customers"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"The roster, rank 1 first."},"unresolvedNominations":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"website":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]}},"required":["name","website"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Companies named while the roster was generated that matched nothing in our data. Not in the roster."},"cap":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991},"generatedAt":{"type":"string","description":"ISO 8601."},"reused":{"type":"boolean","description":"true when the stored roster was returned without generating a new one."},"stats":{"type":"object","propertyNames":{"type":"string"},"additionalProperties":{}}},"required":["subject","pins","entries","unresolvedNominations","cap","generatedAt","reused","stats"],"additionalProperties":false},"AccountListDto":{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"name":{"type":"string"},"url":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","format":"uri"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The company's website as an absolute HTTP or HTTPS URL, or `null` when this workspace does not know one. `null` is expected rather than exceptional: an account created from a company NAME alone — by `POST /v1/people` with a `company` carrying no `domain`, or by a Trayo import — has no website until one is supplied. Set it with `PATCH /v1/accounts/{id}` (`trayo_update_account` over MCP). `logoUrl` is `null` for exactly these accounts, because it is derived from this field."},"logoUrl":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The account's logo URL. Derived from `url`, so it is present for every account whose `url` is a usable domain and `null` otherwise. Cannot be set through this API. The URL returns image bytes (200) or redirects to them (302), so it is usable directly as an `<img src>`; it answers 404 when no logo resolves for the domain. Fetching it needs no API key."},"linkedinHandle":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"starred":{"type":"boolean"},"scores":{"type":"object","properties":{"timing":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"score":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"0–100, NORMALIZED: this account's `raw` as a share of the highest `raw` in your workspace, rounded — the definition the product uses for its timing score. 100 is your hottest account right now, which means it moves when OTHER accounts move. Rank on this; threshold on `raw`."},"raw":{"type":"number","description":"The un-normalized score. How much your signals have fired at this account RECENTLY: each matched signal contributes its weight (1–3), decayed with a 30-day half-life, over a 90-day window, stacked and capped at 100. Stable for this account regardless of the rest of the workspace, so an absolute threshold on it holds still."},"calculatedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"}},"required":["score","raw","calculatedAt"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Null until Trayo has computed it. `calculatedAt` records when this score was last updated."},"activity":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"total":{"type":"number","description":"Weighted sum of event significance and relevance with recency decay and a diversity bonus, over `lookbackDays`. Scale depends on the workspace's scoring configuration — compare accounts within a workspace, not across workspaces."},"eventCount":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"Events that contributed."},"avgSignificance":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}]},"avgRelevance":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}]},"recencyBonus":{"type":"number"},"signalDiversityBonus":{"type":"number"},"lookbackDays":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991},"summary":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"A generated prose summary of what the contributing events add up to for this account — the \"why\", not just the number. Null until generated; regenerated when new events arrive."},"summaryGeneratedAt":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},{"type":"null"}]},"calculatedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"}},"required":["total","eventCount","avgSignificance","avgRelevance","recencyBonus","signalDiversityBonus","lookbackDays","summary","summaryGeneratedAt","calculatedAt"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Null until Trayo has computed it. Recomputed after discovery runs; nothing in this API triggers it."}},"required":["timing","activity"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Trayo's own ranking of this account, published so you do not have to rebuild it by counting events. Both members are null on an account Trayo has not scored yet. This route does not sort by them — page through and sort client-side on `scores.timing.score` or `scores.activity.total`."},"pointOfView":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"predictions":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"point":{"type":"string","description":"One sentence: where the company appears to be heading, and the need that follows from it. Deliberately hedged (\"likely\", \"appears to be\") — it is an outside-in reading of public events, not a confirmed internal plan."},"evidence":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"eventId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","description":"A public event id — read the whole event with `GET /v1/events/{id}`, or find it in `GET /v1/events?accountId=...`. The title, date and summary beside it are copies taken when the point of view was written, so fetch the event when you need its current form. That fetch can 404: the point of view is not rewritten when an event it cites is dismissed afterwards."},"eventTitle":{"type":"string"},"eventDate":{"type":"string","format":"date","description":"The date the event happened, `YYYY-MM-DD` — not a timestamp."},"eventSummary":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"connection":{"type":"string","description":"One line on how THIS event supports the prediction — the causal or strategic link, not a restatement of the title."}},"required":["eventId","eventTitle","eventDate","eventSummary","connection"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"The events the prediction rests on, at least one and at most three. A prediction with no evidence is never written, so this is never empty."}},"required":["point","evidence"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"At most three, strongest first. Empty when the events do not support a direction — an honest answer, not a failure."},"whyNow":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"signalKey":{"type":"string","description":"The signal whose recent firing makes the timing matter. Matches a `signalKey` on `GET /v1/signals` and on the cited events."},"point":{"type":"string","description":"One line on why the timing matters now."},"events":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"eventId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","description":"A public event id — read the whole event with `GET /v1/events/{id}`, or find it in `GET /v1/events?accountId=...`. The title, date and summary beside it are copies taken when the point of view was written, so fetch the event when you need its current form. That fetch can 404: the point of view is not rewritten when an event it cites is dismissed afterwards."},"eventTitle":{"type":"string"},"eventDate":{"type":"string","format":"date","description":"The date the event happened, `YYYY-MM-DD` — not a timestamp."}},"required":["eventId","eventTitle","eventDate"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"The last few events that matched this signal, most recent first."}},"required":["signalKey","point","events"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"At most three. Always empty when `predictions` is empty — timing means nothing without a direction it is timely for."},"generatedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"When this point of view was written."}},"required":["predictions","whyNow","generatedAt"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Trayo's reading of what this account is doing and why it matters to what your workspace sells — the \"why\" behind the account, where `scores.activity.summary` is the \"why\" behind the number. Every prediction cites the events it rests on, so you can check the reading against the record instead of taking it on trust.\n\nNull until the first discovery run produces events and the point of view is generated; regenerated when new events arrive. Also null when the stored copy predates the current shape — an out-of-date reading is withheld rather than served in pieces. Reading this route never generates one."},"createdAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"updatedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"}},"required":["id","name","url","logoUrl","linkedinHandle","starred","scores","pointOfView","createdAt","updatedAt"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Accounts, most recently created first."},"hasMore":{"type":"boolean","description":"Another page exists. When `false` you have reached the end — stop requesting pages."},"nextCursor":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Pass verbatim as the next request's `cursor` to fetch the next page. Null exactly when `hasMore` is false."}},"required":["data","hasMore","nextCursor"],"additionalProperties":false},"CreateAccountDto":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","maxLength":200,"description":"The company's display name. Matching falls back to this only after `linkedinHandle` and `url`, so supply the stronger identifiers whenever you have them. It is also this account's LAST deduplication key on `POST /v1/accounts/batch`, and it counts only against a stored account that has neither a usable website nor a handle — two companies that share a name but each have a website are both created."},"url":{"description":"The company website. Must include a scheme when given, e.g. `https://stripe.com` — `stripe.com` alone is rejected. The hostname is also this account's deduplication key on `POST /v1/accounts/batch`. A row WITHOUT a url is deduplicated by NAME instead (case-insensitive, within your workspace), so it is not created twice — but a url is the stronger key, because two different companies can share a name. After `linkedinHandle`, this is the next way to identify the company: send it whenever you have it.\n\nOPTIONAL since TRA-2077. An account you only have a NAME for is created with no website (`url: null` on reads) rather than refused — the same thing `POST /v1/people` does with a `company` that carries no `domain`, and the same thing Trayo's own importer has always done. Two enforcement levels for one policy was the bug: this route refused rows the people route created.","anyOf":[{"type":"string","format":"uri"},{"type":"null"}]},"linkedinHandle":{"description":"`linkedinHandle` is the bare LinkedIn company handle, e.g. `stripe` from `https://www.linkedin.com/company/stripe/`. Supply it whenever known: it is the strongest way to identify the company and is tried before `url` and `name`. It is also this account's SECOND deduplication key on `POST /v1/accounts/batch`, checked when the hostname does not match, so a row whose website is new to this workspace can still be skipped as a duplicate on its handle alone.","type":"string","maxLength":200}},"required":["name"],"description":"The created account is automatically assigned to the user your API key acts as, which is what makes it eligible for discovery — see `POST /v1/discoveries`. There is no way to create an unassigned account through this API.\n\n**Unknown fields are rejected** (`validation_failed`), not silently dropped — a misspelled field is an error, so you find out.\n\n**Supply `linkedinHandle` whenever you know the company page.** Use the bare company handle, not the full LinkedIn URL. It is the strongest way to identify the company and is tried before the website and name. Sending it at create time makes a `company_not_found` result less likely.\n\n**`name` is the only required field.** An account you have a name but no website for is created with `url: null` rather than refused, matching `POST /v1/people`'s `company`, and is deduplicated by that name. Send `url` whenever you have it: it is the stronger dedup key (two companies can share a name), and an account with no website cannot be matched to a company for `jobs` and `job_change` discovery by website either.\n\n**A `POST /v1/find` accounts row is NOT postable verbatim.** It carries `id`, `website`, `linkedinUrl`, `industry`, `headcount`, `hq`, `fundingStage`, `foundedYear`, `companyType`, `description`, `why`, `known`, `state` in addition to `name` and `url`, and every one of those is refused. This API stores a name, a URL and a LinkedIn handle for an account and nothing else; the firmographics on a find row are unverified, reported by the search, and have nowhere to live here. Refusing them is deliberate — accepting and discarding them would have you believe the workspace holds research it does not. Project the result before importing:\n\n```\njq '{accounts: [.data[] | select(.state == \"selectable\" and .url) | {name, url}]}'\n```\n\nIf you need the firmographics, keep them client-side or in your CRM — `GET /v1/accounts` will never return them.","additionalProperties":false},"AccountDto":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"name":{"type":"string"},"url":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","format":"uri"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The company's website as an absolute HTTP or HTTPS URL, or `null` when this workspace does not know one. `null` is expected rather than exceptional: an account created from a company NAME alone — by `POST /v1/people` with a `company` carrying no `domain`, or by a Trayo import — has no website until one is supplied. Set it with `PATCH /v1/accounts/{id}` (`trayo_update_account` over MCP). `logoUrl` is `null` for exactly these accounts, because it is derived from this field."},"logoUrl":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The account's logo URL. Derived from `url`, so it is present for every account whose `url` is a usable domain and `null` otherwise. Cannot be set through this API. The URL returns image bytes (200) or redirects to them (302), so it is usable directly as an `<img src>`; it answers 404 when no logo resolves for the domain. Fetching it needs no API key."},"linkedinHandle":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"starred":{"type":"boolean"},"scores":{"type":"object","properties":{"timing":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"score":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"0–100, NORMALIZED: this account's `raw` as a share of the highest `raw` in your workspace, rounded — the definition the product uses for its timing score. 100 is your hottest account right now, which means it moves when OTHER accounts move. Rank on this; threshold on `raw`."},"raw":{"type":"number","description":"The un-normalized score. How much your signals have fired at this account RECENTLY: each matched signal contributes its weight (1–3), decayed with a 30-day half-life, over a 90-day window, stacked and capped at 100. Stable for this account regardless of the rest of the workspace, so an absolute threshold on it holds still."},"calculatedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"}},"required":["score","raw","calculatedAt"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Null until Trayo has computed it. `calculatedAt` records when this score was last updated."},"activity":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"total":{"type":"number","description":"Weighted sum of event significance and relevance with recency decay and a diversity bonus, over `lookbackDays`. Scale depends on the workspace's scoring configuration — compare accounts within a workspace, not across workspaces."},"eventCount":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"Events that contributed."},"avgSignificance":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}]},"avgRelevance":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}]},"recencyBonus":{"type":"number"},"signalDiversityBonus":{"type":"number"},"lookbackDays":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991},"summary":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"A generated prose summary of what the contributing events add up to for this account — the \"why\", not just the number. Null until generated; regenerated when new events arrive."},"summaryGeneratedAt":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},{"type":"null"}]},"calculatedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"}},"required":["total","eventCount","avgSignificance","avgRelevance","recencyBonus","signalDiversityBonus","lookbackDays","summary","summaryGeneratedAt","calculatedAt"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Null until Trayo has computed it. Recomputed after discovery runs; nothing in this API triggers it."}},"required":["timing","activity"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Trayo's own ranking of this account, published so you do not have to rebuild it by counting events. Both members are null on an account Trayo has not scored yet. This route does not sort by them — page through and sort client-side on `scores.timing.score` or `scores.activity.total`."},"pointOfView":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"predictions":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"point":{"type":"string","description":"One sentence: where the company appears to be heading, and the need that follows from it. Deliberately hedged (\"likely\", \"appears to be\") — it is an outside-in reading of public events, not a confirmed internal plan."},"evidence":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"eventId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","description":"A public event id — read the whole event with `GET /v1/events/{id}`, or find it in `GET /v1/events?accountId=...`. The title, date and summary beside it are copies taken when the point of view was written, so fetch the event when you need its current form. That fetch can 404: the point of view is not rewritten when an event it cites is dismissed afterwards."},"eventTitle":{"type":"string"},"eventDate":{"type":"string","format":"date","description":"The date the event happened, `YYYY-MM-DD` — not a timestamp."},"eventSummary":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"connection":{"type":"string","description":"One line on how THIS event supports the prediction — the causal or strategic link, not a restatement of the title."}},"required":["eventId","eventTitle","eventDate","eventSummary","connection"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"The events the prediction rests on, at least one and at most three. A prediction with no evidence is never written, so this is never empty."}},"required":["point","evidence"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"At most three, strongest first. Empty when the events do not support a direction — an honest answer, not a failure."},"whyNow":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"signalKey":{"type":"string","description":"The signal whose recent firing makes the timing matter. Matches a `signalKey` on `GET /v1/signals` and on the cited events."},"point":{"type":"string","description":"One line on why the timing matters now."},"events":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"eventId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","description":"A public event id — read the whole event with `GET /v1/events/{id}`, or find it in `GET /v1/events?accountId=...`. The title, date and summary beside it are copies taken when the point of view was written, so fetch the event when you need its current form. That fetch can 404: the point of view is not rewritten when an event it cites is dismissed afterwards."},"eventTitle":{"type":"string"},"eventDate":{"type":"string","format":"date","description":"The date the event happened, `YYYY-MM-DD` — not a timestamp."}},"required":["eventId","eventTitle","eventDate"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"The last few events that matched this signal, most recent first."}},"required":["signalKey","point","events"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"At most three. Always empty when `predictions` is empty — timing means nothing without a direction it is timely for."},"generatedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"When this point of view was written."}},"required":["predictions","whyNow","generatedAt"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Trayo's reading of what this account is doing and why it matters to what your workspace sells — the \"why\" behind the account, where `scores.activity.summary` is the \"why\" behind the number. Every prediction cites the events it rests on, so you can check the reading against the record instead of taking it on trust.\n\nNull until the first discovery run produces events and the point of view is generated; regenerated when new events arrive. Also null when the stored copy predates the current shape — an out-of-date reading is withheld rather than served in pieces. Reading this route never generates one."},"createdAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"updatedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"}},"required":["id","name","url","logoUrl","linkedinHandle","starred","scores","pointOfView","createdAt","updatedAt"],"additionalProperties":false},"BatchCreateAccountsDto":{"type":"object","properties":{"accounts":{"maxItems":200,"type":"array","items":{},"description":"Up to 200 rows, each shaped like a `POST /v1/accounts` body. More than 200 is a `validation_failed` ERROR (`param: \"accounts\"`), never a silent truncation — dropping the excess would lose records you believe you created. This is the same rule as `POST /v1/find`'s `limit`, which is rejected above 100.\n\nIndividual rows are validated one at a time: a malformed row is reported in `skipped`, not raised as a request error."}},"required":["accounts"],"additionalProperties":false},"BatchCreateAccountsResultDto":{"type":"object","properties":{"created":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"name":{"type":"string"},"url":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","format":"uri"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The company's website as an absolute HTTP or HTTPS URL, or `null` when this workspace does not know one. `null` is expected rather than exceptional: an account created from a company NAME alone — by `POST /v1/people` with a `company` carrying no `domain`, or by a Trayo import — has no website until one is supplied. Set it with `PATCH /v1/accounts/{id}` (`trayo_update_account` over MCP). `logoUrl` is `null` for exactly these accounts, because it is derived from this field."},"logoUrl":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The account's logo URL. Derived from `url`, so it is present for every account whose `url` is a usable domain and `null` otherwise. Cannot be set through this API. The URL returns image bytes (200) or redirects to them (302), so it is usable directly as an `<img src>`; it answers 404 when no logo resolves for the domain. Fetching it needs no API key."},"linkedinHandle":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"starred":{"type":"boolean"},"scores":{"type":"object","properties":{"timing":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"score":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"0–100, NORMALIZED: this account's `raw` as a share of the highest `raw` in your workspace, rounded — the definition the product uses for its timing score. 100 is your hottest account right now, which means it moves when OTHER accounts move. Rank on this; threshold on `raw`."},"raw":{"type":"number","description":"The un-normalized score. How much your signals have fired at this account RECENTLY: each matched signal contributes its weight (1–3), decayed with a 30-day half-life, over a 90-day window, stacked and capped at 100. Stable for this account regardless of the rest of the workspace, so an absolute threshold on it holds still."},"calculatedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"}},"required":["score","raw","calculatedAt"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Null until Trayo has computed it. `calculatedAt` records when this score was last updated."},"activity":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"total":{"type":"number","description":"Weighted sum of event significance and relevance with recency decay and a diversity bonus, over `lookbackDays`. Scale depends on the workspace's scoring configuration — compare accounts within a workspace, not across workspaces."},"eventCount":{"type"