 this workspace only has prose; an empty array means no cards."},"stakeholderPersonas":{"anyOf":[{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"title":{"type":"string"},"seniority":{"type":"string","enum":["C-level","VP","Director","Manager"]},"buyingRole":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["economic_buyer","decision_maker","champion","technical_evaluator"]},{"type":"null"}]},"rationale":{"type":"string"},"icon":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]}},"required":["title","seniority","buyingRole","rationale","icon"],"additionalProperties":false}},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Editable buyer and stakeholder personas saved during onboarding. Null means only prose is available."},"buyerProfile":{"type":"object","properties":{"isB2b":{"type":"boolean"},"notB2bReason":{"type":"string"},"sellerMode":{"type":"string","enum":["horizontal","vertical","local_smb","smb_horizontal","enterprise"]},"modeReason":{"type":"string"},"geography":{"type":"object","properties":{"scope":{"type":"string","enum":["local","regional","national","global"]},"countries":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"regionLabel":{"type":"string"},"states":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"cities":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"radiusNote":{"type":"string"}},"required":["scope","countries","regionLabel","states","cities","radiusNote"],"additionalProperties":false},"sizeBand":{"type":"object","properties":{"min":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991},"max":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991}},"required":["min","max"],"additionalProperties":false},"sameIndustryBuyer":{"type":"boolean"},"rivalDefinition":{"type":"string"},"buyerThesis":{"type":"string"},"positiveSignals":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"industries":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"technologies":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"competitorTerms":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"categoryKeywords":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"existingCustomers":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"generationAngles":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["isB2b","notB2bReason","sellerMode","modeReason","geography","sizeBand","sameIndustryBuyer","rivalDefinition","buyerThesis","positiveSignals","industries","technologies","competitorTerms","categoryKeywords","existingCustomers","generationAngles"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"The ICP assumptions: buyer thesis, industries, size and geography, exclusions and search angles. Always present. This field was previously null when no profile was saved; it no longer is, so read `buyerProfileSource` instead of checking for null, and check it before treating this as fact."},"buyerProfileSource":{"type":"string","enum":["saved","partial","inferred","unreadable"],"description":"`saved`: read from onboarding's stored ICP. `partial`: the fields sent to this API are the caller's own; every field never sent is still the placeholder below. `inferred`: nothing was saved, so you got a fixed placeholder — the same wide defaults for every workspace, not read from your site or your name. `unreadable`: an ICP is saved but not in a shape this API can read, so you got that same placeholder and patching is refused; edit it in the Trayo app. Only `saved` fields and fields you supplied yourself are facts about this workspace; confirm the rest before relying on them."},"brand":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"domain":{"type":"string","description":"The website domain the brand belongs to, e.g. \"stripe.com\"."},"name":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The brand name."},"description":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"A one- or two-sentence description of the company."},"colors":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Brand colors as lowercase `#rrggbb`, most prominent first."},"socials":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"network":{"type":"string","description":"Network key, e.g. `linkedin`, `twitter`, `github`."},"url":{"type":"string","description":"Profile URL."}},"required":["network","url"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Social profiles found for the brand."},"logoUrl":{"type":"string","description":"Square logo image URL. Public, no key needed."},"brandmarkUrl":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Wide logo lockup image URL (800px wide PNG). Public, no key needed. Null when none."},"bannerUrl":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Social banner image URL (800px wide). Public, no key needed. Null when none."}},"required":["domain","name","description","colors","socials","logoUrl","brandmarkUrl","bannerUrl"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Your company brand, from your workspace website: name, description, colors, social profiles, and logo images you can embed. Null when no brand is known for the website."},{"type":"null"}]}},"required":["id","name","revision","stakeholderCriteria","solutions","solutionsBrief","solutionItems","stakeholderPersonas","buyerProfile","buyerProfileSource","brand"],"additionalProperties":false},"UpdateWorkspaceBodyDto":{"type":"object","properties":{"expectedRevision":{"description":"The revision returned by trayo_get_workspace or GET /v1/workspace. Required for full-list replacements. A stale revision returns 409; re-read and merge instead of retrying the old list.","type":"string","pattern":"^[a-f0-9]{64}$"},"stakeholderCriteria":{"description":"Plain prose describing the roles to find and the roles to skip, e.g. \"Heads of platform, infrastructure, DevOps or SRE, and the VP or Director of Engineering they report to. Not recruiters, not IT, not individual engineers.\" Send null to clear it.","anyOf":[{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":8000},{"type":"null"}]},"solutions":{"description":"What you sell, in prose. Send null to clear it.","anyOf":[{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":8000},{"type":"null"}]},"solutionsBrief":{"description":"A one- or two-sentence version of `solutions`. Send null to clear it. If solutions or solutionItems change and this is omitted, the old brief is cleared. Do not re-send an old brief that may be inaccurate after the change.","anyOf":[{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":8000},{"type":"null"}]},"solutionItems":{"description":"Replace the complete solution-card list. Requires expectedRevision. The prose `solutions` projection is regenerated atomically, and the old `solutionsBrief` is cleared unless a new one is sent. Send [] to clear the cards; icons are server-owned.","maxItems":100,"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"description":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2000},"url":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":2000},{"type":"null"}]}},"required":["name","description"],"additionalProperties":false}},"stakeholderPersonas":{"description":"Replace the complete buyer-persona list. Requires expectedRevision. `stakeholderCriteria` is regenerated atomically. Send [] to clear the personas; icons are server-owned.","maxItems":100,"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"title":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"seniority":{"type":"string","enum":["C-level","VP","Director","Manager"]},"buyingRole":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["economic_buyer","decision_maker","champion","technical_evaluator"]},{"type":"null"}]},"rationale":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2000}},"required":["title","seniority","rationale"],"additionalProperties":false}},"buyerProfile":{"description":"Correct only the supplied ICP assumptions; nested geography and sizeBand are partial too. Requires an existing saved profile. Tenant-domain identity is never writable.","type":"object","properties":{"isB2b":{"type":"boolean"},"notB2bReason":{"type":"string","maxLength":2000},"sellerMode":{"type":"string","enum":["horizontal","vertical","local_smb","smb_horizontal","enterprise"]},"modeReason":{"type":"string","maxLength":2000},"geography":{"type":"object","properties":{"scope":{"type":"string","enum":["local","regional","national","global"]},"countries":{"maxItems":100,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"regionLabel":{"type":"string","maxLength":2000},"states":{"maxItems":100,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"cities":{"maxItems":100,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"radiusNote":{"type":"string","maxLength":2000}},"additionalProperties":false},"sizeBand":{"type":"object","properties":{"min":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":1000000000},"max":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":1000000000}},"additionalProperties":false},"sameIndustryBuyer":{"type":"boolean"},"rivalDefinition":{"type":"string","maxLength":2000},"buyerThesis":{"type":"string","maxLength":2000},"positiveSignals":{"maxItems":100,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"industries":{"maxItems":100,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"technologies":{"maxItems":100,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"competitorTerms":{"maxItems":100,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"categoryKeywords":{"maxItems":100,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"existingCustomers":{"maxItems":100,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"generationAngles":{"maxItems":100,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}}},"additionalProperties":false}},"additionalProperties":false},"WhoamiDto":{"type":"object","properties":{"workspace":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","description":"The workspace this key acts in."},"name":{"type":"string"},"plan":{"type":"string","enum":["FREE","PRO","GROWTH","ENTERPRISE"]},"lifecycle":{"type":"string","enum":["trial_active","trial_grace","nurturing","purged","active"],"description":"`active` and `trial_active` can initiate metered work; the others are read-only. `canInitiate` is this, as a boolean."}},"required":["id","name","plan","lifecycle"],"additionalProperties":false},"actingAs":{"type":"object","properties":{"userId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"email":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"name":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]}},"required":["userId","email","name"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"The user your key acts as. Accounts and lists you create belong to this user and show up under them in the Trayo app."},"key":{"type":"object","properties":{"grantedScopes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Persisted key grants; not plan eligibility."},"effectiveScopes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Valid grants allowed by the owner’s current workspace permissions."},"expiresAt":{"description":"Key expiry; null means no scheduled expiry.","anyOf":[{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},{"type":"null"}]},"label":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The label the key was issued with, for telling keys apart. `null` when it has none."}},"required":["grantedScopes","effectiveScopes","expiresAt","label"],"additionalProperties":false},"restrictions":{"type":"object","properties":{"dataAccess":{"type":"object","properties":{"workspaceId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","description":"Workspace data stays within this tenant; endpoint-specific checks still apply."},"lists":{"type":"string","const":"created_by_key_owner","description":"List operations access only lists created by actingAs.userId."}},"required":["workspaceId","lists"],"additionalProperties":false},"rateLimits":{"type":"object","properties":{"defaultPerMinute":{"type":"integer","exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991},"expensivePerMinute":{"type":"integer","exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991}},"required":["defaultPerMinute","expensivePerMinute"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Effective workspace request budgets per rolling 60 seconds, shared by REST, MCP, all API keys and OAuth users. Daily and total usage quotas are disabled for now; support can adjust workspace throughput. `defaultPerMinute` and `expensivePerMinute` are separate buckets and a call spends one of them; each MCP tool names the bucket it spends in its description and `_meta[\"trayo/rateLimitBucket\"]`."}},"required":["dataAccess","rateLimits"],"additionalProperties":false},"capabilities":{"type":"object","properties":{"emailLookup":{"type":"object","properties":{"scopeAuthorized":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether this key and its owner currently authorize this lookup field."},"available":{"type":"boolean","description":"Passes scope, lifecycle and plan eligibility checks for a new lookup. Public REST/MCP usage quotas and the daily usage limit (`429 quota_daily_limit`) are disabled for now. Workspace request pacing, validation and per-network transport protection still apply."},"blockedBy":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","enum":["missing_key_scope","owner_permission_limit","lifecycle_blocked","plan_disabled","lookup_limit_reached"]},"description":"Which of these reasons block the field right now; an empty array means none of them do. Public REST/MCP lookup quotas and the daily usage limit (`429 quota_daily_limit`) are disabled for now. Workspace request pacing, row validation and per-network transport protection are checked when the lookup runs and do not appear in this list."}},"required":["scopeAuthorized","available","blockedBy"],"additionalProperties":false},"phoneLookup":{"type":"object","properties":{"scopeAuthorized":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether this key and its owner currently authorize this lookup field."},"available":{"type":"boolean","description":"Passes scope, lifecycle and plan eligibility checks for a new lookup. Public REST/MCP usage quotas and the daily usage limit (`429 quota_daily_limit`) are disabled for now. Workspace request pacing, validation and per-network transport protection still apply."},"blockedBy":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","enum":["missing_key_scope","owner_permission_limit","lifecycle_blocked","plan_disabled","lookup_limit_reached"]},"description":"Which of these reasons block the field right now; an empty array means none of them do. Public REST/MCP lookup quotas and the daily usage limit (`429 quota_daily_limit`) are disabled for now. Workspace request pacing, row validation and per-network transport protection are checked when the lookup runs and do not appear in this list."}},"required":["scopeAuthorized","available","blockedBy"],"additionalProperties":false}},"required":["emailLookup","phoneLookup"],"additionalProperties":false},"canInitiate":{"type":"boolean","description":"Workspace lifecycle permission to start metered work. This does not grant the key any scope or confirm plan entitlements, available quota or request eligibility."},"lookups":{"type":"object","properties":{"email":{"type":"object","properties":{"enabled":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether the plan allows this kind of lookup at all. `false` means every lookup is refused."},"limit":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Effective allowance for this field. `null` means unlimited. Public REST/MCP lookup quotas, workspace quota and the daily usage limit (`429 quota_daily_limit`, a rolling 24-hour ceiling) are disabled for now. Scope, lifecycle and request validation still apply."},"used":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"Recorded lookup usage, including lookups still in flight, even when no cap applies. Read `remaining` rather than subtracting this from `limit`."},"remaining":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Lookups left against an enabled allowance: `limit - used`, floored at 0. `null` when `limit` is `null`; public REST/MCP usage allowances are unlimited for now. The rolling 24-hour daily usage limit (`429 quota_daily_limit`) is disabled too. This is a snapshot that includes lookups still in flight; concurrent work changes `used`. Scope, lifecycle, per-network protection and row validation can still refuse a call. Handle the actual refusal code and, for a stopped MCP batch, `stoppedBy.retry`."},"period":{"type":"string","const":"lifetime","description":"The usage counting period. `lifetime`: recorded lookups do not reset. When a numeric allowance applies, it has no scheduled reset; `null` limits remain uncapped."}},"required":["enabled","limit","used","remaining","period"],"additionalProperties":false},"phone":{"type":"object","properties":{"enabled":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether the plan allows this kind of lookup at all. `false` means every lookup is refused."},"limit":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Effective allowance for this field. `null` means unlimited. Public REST/MCP lookup quotas, workspace quota and the daily usage limit (`429 quota_daily_limit`, a rolling 24-hour ceiling) are disabled for now. Scope, lifecycle and request validation still apply."},"used":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"Recorded lookup usage, including lookups still in flight, even when no cap applies. Read `remaining` rather than subtracting this from `limit`."},"remaining":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Lookups left against an enabled allowance: `limit - used`, floored at 0. `null` when `limit` is `null`; public REST/MCP usage allowances are unlimited for now. The rolling 24-hour daily usage limit (`429 quota_daily_limit`) is disabled too. This is a snapshot that includes lookups still in flight; concurrent work changes `used`. Scope, lifecycle, per-network protection and row validation can still refuse a call. Handle the actual refusal code and, for a stopped MCP batch, `stoppedBy.retry`."},"period":{"type":"string","const":"lifetime","description":"The usage counting period. `lifetime`: recorded lookups do not reset. When a numeric allowance applies, it has no scheduled reset; `null` limits remain uncapped."}},"required":["enabled","limit","used","remaining","period"],"additionalProperties":false}},"required":["email","phone"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Contact-lookup usage and any active allowances. `POST /v1/people/{id}/enrich`, `POST /v1/people/enrich/batch` and `POST /v1/contacts/lookup` all draw on these, one per field LOOKED UP — the draw happens when a lookup starts, whether or not it goes on to find a value. Usage is recorded even when `limit` and `remaining` are `null`, meaning no lookup cap applies. When a numeric allowance applies, budget on the people you send, not the addresses you expect back. A field that never starts a lookup (a value already on the record, one already running, the cooldown after a miss) costs nothing. When a numeric allowance applies, `402 lookup_limit_reached` is what exceeding one looks like."}},"required":["workspace","actingAs","key","restrictions","capabilities","canInitiate","lookups"],"additionalProperties":false},"StakeholderSearchBodyDto":{"type":"object","properties":{"company":{"type":"object","properties":{"companyId":{"description":"Trayo's own id for the company, as a number or numeric string: the `companyId` a post, post-engager or person-research result carries, or the `id` of a company find result. Not a workspace account UUID. When sent, it is the key: the company is read by this id and nothing else is tried, so an id Trayo does not hold is `company_not_found`. A `name`, `website` or `linkedinUrl` sent beside it is not used.","anyOf":[{"type":"integer","exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991},{"type":"string","pattern":"^[1-9]\\d*$"}]},"accountId":{"description":"An account in your workspace, on its own. Its existing match is used when it has one; otherwise the account is resolved from its website, LinkedIn handle and name exactly as the app would, so an account we have not yet matched still works when the company is in our data.","type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$","format":"uuid"},"website":{"description":"The company's own website, as a URL or a domain (`https://zapier.com`, `zapier.com`). The strongest key after the LinkedIn page: it is matched against our data, then, on a miss, followed through a cross-domain redirect, so a legacy or vanity domain that forwards to the current site still resolves. Sent on its own as the bare site (no path or subdomain), a data or social platform's domain names the platform itself (`zoominfo.com` is ZoomInfo); a page on such a site (`linkedin.com/company/acme`) is not a company website. When our data files the company under a different website, a website sent on its own is also tried as the LinkedIn page it spells (`gong.io` as `gong-io`), accepted only for an established company whose name matches the domain. An alias that does not forward to the company's current site is a miss: send the current website, the LinkedIn page or the name. Does not have to be in your workspace.","type":"string","minLength":3,"maxLength":2048},"linkedinUrl":{"description":"The company's LinkedIn page — the `linkedinUrl` a find result or a person row carries, copied through (`https://www.linkedin.com/company/zapier`); the bare handle (`zapier`) is accepted too. Tried first when present, and the most precise key there is. Showcase pages are not company pages: send the company's own. Copy the handle from a Trayo result or the company's own site rather than guessing it from the name — a slug that belongs to a different company resolves to that company.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048},"name":{"description":"The company name. Tried last and the weakest key, since a common name can match the wrong company — send the website when you have it. A name-only lookup finds only companies Trayo holds under that name; an employer that a Trayo person row names with `companyId: null` has no company record, and its name will usually miss.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"additionalProperties":false},"definition":{"description":"The stakeholder definition to search with, in plain prose: the roles that own or buy what you sell, the roles that influence the decision, and the roles to skip. Optional: when omitted, the workspace's own definition is used, and when that is unset too, a seniority-only seed (chiefs, VPs, directors of any function). `definition.source` in the response says which applied. Passing one here does not change the workspace setting.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":8000},"limit":{"description":"How many people to return, 5 by default, 10 at most. Fewer come back when fewer fit.","type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":10},"personas":{"description":"Persona names to label each person with, e.g. `[\"CISO\", \"IT leader\", \"Champion\"]`. Optional: when omitted and the workspace's own definition applies, the workspace's saved personas are used. A definition sent with the request has no persona names of its own, so without this field its people come back with `matchedPersona: null` and `coverage: []`.","minItems":1,"maxItems":20,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}}},"required":["company"],"additionalProperties":false},"StakeholderSearchResponseDto":{"type":"object","properties":{"company":{"type":"object","properties":{"companyId":{"type":"string","description":"Trayo's id for the company. Send it back as `companyId` to name this exact company again."},"name":{"type":"string","description":"The company as Trayo records it."},"website":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The company's website domain as Trayo files it."},"linkedinUrl":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The company's LinkedIn page, when Trayo has it."},"accountId":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The workspace account for this company: the one you sent, or the account that already holds its website or LinkedIn page. Null when the company is not in your workspace."},"resolvedBy":{"type":"string","enum":["account_match","company_id","linkedin","website","redirect","name"],"description":"Which key identified the company — the same resolver the Trayo app uses, in its order. `account_match`: the account's existing match. `linkedin`: the LinkedIn page, as sent or as spelled by a website sent on its own. `website`: the website domain. `redirect`: the website, after following a cross-domain redirect to the company's current site. `name`: the name, the weakest key.\n\nA match is exact on the key you sent, which is only the company you meant if the key was. A slug or name can belong to a different company than the one you mean, and the answer will then describe that company. Read `name` and `website` back before acting, and prefer `website` as the key — a domain resolves to whoever owns it."},"nameMatch":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["exact","approximate"]},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Set only when `resolvedBy` is `name`, null otherwise. `exact`: the company's name equals the name looked up once legal suffixes (Inc, GmbH, Ltd) are dropped. `approximate`: the closest name Trayo holds, which can be a different company (\"CR Management Consulting\" answered with \"m3 management consulting\"). Check an `approximate` match against what you know of the company before using it, and leave it out when it does not fit."}},"required":["companyId","name","website","linkedinUrl","accountId","resolvedBy","nameMatch"],"additionalProperties":false},"definition":{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string","description":"The definition the search actually ran with."},"source":{"type":"string","enum":["request","workspace","default"],"description":"`request`: you sent one. `workspace`: the workspace's own definition. `default`: neither existed, so a seniority-only seed was used — the results are senior people of any function, not your buying committee."}},"required":["text","source"],"additionalProperties":false},"candidates":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"How many people at the company the keyword search found before selection. Zero with `people: []` means Trayo has nobody matching the keywords; a positive number with `people: []` means the selection judged none of them to fit the definition."},"people":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"fullName":{"type":"string"},"title":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"headline":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"location":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"city":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"City, e.g. `San Diego`. Null when the profile names only a region or metro area."},"state":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"State, province or region, e.g. `California`."},"country":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code, e.g. `US`."},"raw":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The location as written on the profile, e.g. `Greater San Diego Area`. Usually present; the only populated field when the profile names just a metro area."}},"required":["city","state","country","raw"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Where the person says they are on their LinkedIn profile. Usually their home metro area, but it is the person's own statement, not a verified address, and it is not where their company is headquartered. Null when Trayo has no location for them. Breaking type change: this field used to be a string, usually null; it is now this object, the person's stated LinkedIn location."},"linkedinUrl":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Their LinkedIn profile URL, when Trayo has it. Send it to `POST /v1/contacts/lookup`, `POST /v1/research/person`, or as `linkedinUrl` to `POST /v1/people`."},"photoUrl":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The person's profile photo, as a directly loadable image URL. Null when Trayo holds no real photo for them — show initials then. Every route that returns a person carries this field under this name."},"otherCurrentEmployers":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Up to three other companies with current roles, including board or advisory affiliations. These names do not establish employment, salary or buying authority. An empty list is not proof of employment at the searched company."},"otherCurrentRoles":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"companyName":{"type":"string"},"title":{"type":"string"}},"required":["companyName","title"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Up to six current roles at the other companies, with titles for distinguishing employment from affiliations. Outside board or advisory seats do not disqualify a buyer employed at the searched company. Missing titles or an empty list mean there may be insufficient evidence; do not infer who pays the person."},"whyThisPerson":{"type":"string","description":"Why this person fits the definition, in the selection's own words. On a near-miss: what their role covers and what it lacks."},"matchedPersona":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The persona this person matched, one of the names in `coverage`. Checked after selection against the job's function and seniority, and replaced or cleared when it does not hold. Null when no persona holds, or when the search had no persona names (see `personas`)."},"belowThreshold":{"type":"boolean","description":"`false` on every row of `people`. `true` on every row of `nearMisses`: the selection judged this person NOT to fit the definition."}},"required":["fullName","title","headline","location","linkedinUrl","photoUrl","otherCurrentEmployers","otherCurrentRoles","whyThisPerson","matchedPersona","belowThreshold"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"The selected people, at most `limit`. Repeating a search within a week normally returns the same people. NOT written to your workspace: import the ones you want with `POST /v1/people/batch` (`fullName`, `title`, `linkedinUrl`, `photoUrl`, plus `accountId` or `company`)."},"nearMisses":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"fullName":{"type":"string"},"title":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"headline":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"location":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"city":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"City, e.g. `San Diego`. Null when the profile names only a region or metro area."},"state":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"State, province or region, e.g. `California`."},"country":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code, e.g. `US`."},"raw":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The location as written on the profile, e.g. `Greater San Diego Area`. Usually present; the only populated field when the profile names just a metro area."}},"required":["city","state","country","raw"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Where the person says they are on their LinkedIn profile. Usually their home metro area, but it is the person's own statement, not a verified address, and it is not where