 it is the key: the company is read by this id and nothing else is tried, so an id Trayo does not hold is `company_not_found`. A `name`, `website` or `linkedinUrl` sent beside it is not used.","anyOf":[{"type":"integer","exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991},{"type":"string","pattern":"^[1-9]\\d*$"}]},"accountId":{"description":"An account in your workspace, on its own. Its existing match is used when it has one; otherwise the account is resolved from its website, LinkedIn handle and name exactly as the app would, so an account we have not yet matched still works when the company is in our data.","type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$","format":"uuid"},"website":{"description":"The company's own website, as a URL or a domain (`https://zapier.com`, `zapier.com`). The strongest key after the LinkedIn page: it is matched against our data, then, on a miss, followed through a cross-domain redirect, so a legacy or vanity domain that forwards to the current site still resolves. Sent on its own as the bare site (no path or subdomain), a data or social platform's domain names the platform itself (`zoominfo.com` is ZoomInfo); a page on such a site (`linkedin.com/company/acme`) is not a company website. When our data files the company under a different website, a website sent on its own is also tried as the LinkedIn page it spells (`gong.io` as `gong-io`), accepted only for an established company whose name matches the domain. An alias that does not forward to the company's current site is a miss: send the current website, the LinkedIn page or the name. Does not have to be in your workspace.","type":"string","minLength":3,"maxLength":2048},"linkedinUrl":{"description":"The company's LinkedIn page — the `linkedinUrl` a find result or a person row carries, copied through (`https://www.linkedin.com/company/zapier`); the bare handle (`zapier`) is accepted too. Tried first when present, and the most precise key there is. Showcase pages are not company pages: send the company's own. Copy the handle from a Trayo result or the company's own site rather than guessing it from the name — a slug that belongs to a different company resolves to that company.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048},"name":{"description":"The company name. Tried last and the weakest key, since a common name can match the wrong company — send the website when you have it. A name-only lookup finds only companies Trayo holds under that name; an employer that a Trayo person row names with `companyId: null` has no company record, and its name will usually miss.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}},"additionalProperties":false},"description":"The companies to search, 1 to 50, each named the same way as `company` on `POST /v1/stakeholders/search`. Results come back by `index` into this array."},"definition":{"description":"The stakeholder definition to search with, in plain prose: the roles that own or buy what you sell, the roles that influence the decision, and the roles to skip. Optional: when omitted, the workspace's own definition is used, and when that is unset too, a seniority-only seed (chiefs, VPs, directors of any function). `definition.source` in the response says which applied. Passing one here does not change the workspace setting.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":8000},"limit":{"description":"How many people to return, 5 by default, 10 at most. Fewer come back when fewer fit.","type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":10},"personas":{"description":"Persona names to label each person with, e.g. `[\"CISO\", \"IT leader\", \"Champion\"]`. Optional: when omitted and the workspace's own definition applies, the workspace's saved personas are used. A definition sent with the request has no persona names of its own, so without this field its people come back with `matchedPersona: null` and `coverage: []`.","minItems":1,"maxItems":20,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200}}},"required":["companies"],"additionalProperties":false},"StakeholderBatchSearchResponseDto":{"type":"object","properties":{"definition":{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string","description":"The definition the search actually ran with."},"source":{"type":"string","enum":["request","workspace","default"],"description":"`request`: you sent one. `workspace`: the workspace's own definition. `default`: neither existed, so a seniority-only seed was used — the results are senior people of any function, not your buying committee."}},"required":["text","source"],"additionalProperties":false},"results":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"company":{"type":"object","properties":{"companyId":{"type":"string","description":"Trayo's id for the company. Send it back as `companyId` to name this exact company again."},"name":{"type":"string","description":"The company as Trayo records it."},"website":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The company's website domain as Trayo files it."},"linkedinUrl":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The company's LinkedIn page, when Trayo has it."},"accountId":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The workspace account for this company: the one you sent, or the account that already holds its website or LinkedIn page. Null when the company is not in your workspace."},"resolvedBy":{"type":"string","enum":["account_match","company_id","linkedin","website","redirect","name"],"description":"Which key identified the company — the same resolver the Trayo app uses, in its order. `account_match`: the account's existing match. `linkedin`: the LinkedIn page, as sent or as spelled by a website sent on its own. `website`: the website domain. `redirect`: the website, after following a cross-domain redirect to the company's current site. `name`: the name, the weakest key.\n\nA match is exact on the key you sent, which is only the company you meant if the key was. A slug or name can belong to a different company than the one you mean, and the answer will then describe that company. Read `name` and `website` back before acting, and prefer `website` as the key — a domain resolves to whoever owns it."},"nameMatch":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","enum":["exact","approximate"]},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Set only when `resolvedBy` is `name`, null otherwise. `exact`: the company's name equals the name looked up once legal suffixes (Inc, GmbH, Ltd) are dropped. `approximate`: the closest name Trayo holds, which can be a different company (\"CR Management Consulting\" answered with \"m3 management consulting\"). Check an `approximate` match against what you know of the company before using it, and leave it out when it does not fit."}},"required":["companyId","name","website","linkedinUrl","accountId","resolvedBy","nameMatch"],"additionalProperties":false},"candidates":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"How many people at the company the keyword search found before selection. Zero with `people: []` means Trayo has nobody matching the keywords; a positive number with `people: []` means the selection judged none of them to fit the definition."},"people":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"fullName":{"type":"string"},"title":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"headline":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"location":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"city":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"City, e.g. `San Diego`. Null when the profile names only a region or metro area."},"state":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"State, province or region, e.g. `California`."},"country":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code, e.g. `US`."},"raw":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The locat