,"signal_key_conflict","idempotency_key_reused","list_in_use","quota_daily_limit","quota_exceeded","lookup_limit_reached","lookup_start_failed","contact_lookup_not_found","phone_lookup_failed","phone_lookup_expired","contact_lookup_failed","company_not_found","company_resolution_timed_out","job_change_search_not_configured","job_change_search_failed","lookalike_search_not_configured","lookalike_search_failed","competitor_roster_not_configured","competitor_roster_failed","post_search_not_configured","post_search_failed","stakeholder_search_not_configured","stakeholder_search_failed","stakeholder_search_not_found","person_ask_not_configured","person_ask_failed","person_profile_not_found","person_profile_too_thin","research_not_configured","research_failed","find_needs_indexed_filter","rate_limited","internal_error","find_not_configured","find_response_failed","discovery_run_too_large","mcp_result_delivery_failed","mcp_result_not_found","mcp_result_expired","mcp_tool_removed","find_unavailable","find_timeout","app_not_found","deployment_not_found","app_slug_unavailable","app_not_ready","app_state_conflict","archive_upload_missing","archive_too_large","archive_rejected","public_mode_not_allowed","hosted_apps_unavailable"],"description":"Why this person failed, in the error envelope's `code` vocabulary, e.g. `person_not_found`. Usually the code a single call would return; `person_profile_too_thin` is the batch's own, for an overview that came back empty."},"retry":{"type":"string","enum":["fix_input","retry_later","do_not_retry"],"description":"What to do about the failure, and the only field you need in order to decide\nwhether to send the request again.\n\n`fix_input` — the request is wrong; change it and retry.\n\n`retry_later` — the request is right, the system is not ready; retry it\nunchanged, with backoff and a FINITE number of attempts. On a 500\n(`internal_error`) this especially does not mean retry indefinitely: the\nfailure is not known to be transient, only that nothing about your request\nneeds changing, so give up after a few attempts rather than looping.\n\n`do_not_retry` — retrying will never help.\n\nFixed per `code`; see the table above. Always present, on every error,\nincluding any code added after this document — so a client that does not\nrecognise a `code` can still act correctly by reading this field alone."},"message":{"type":"string"},"param":{"description":"Names the offending field, e.g. `people[2].personId`.","type":"string"}},"required":["index","code","retry","message"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"One entry per person this call could not produce an overview for."}},"required":["results","errors"],"additionalProperties":false},"ContactLookupBodyDto":{"type":"object","properties":{"fullName":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"description":"The person's full name, as it reads on their profile."},"linkedinUrl":{"description":"The person's LinkedIn profile, as its URL — the `linkedinUrl` a `POST /v1/find` contacts result carries, copied through — or as the bare username. Include it when known to improve the chance of finding contact details.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048},"company":{"description":"Where the person works. Include it when known to help identify the person.","type":"object","properties":{"name":{"description":"The employer's name. Used alongside the website, never instead of it.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"website":{"description":"The employer's website, as a URL or a domain (`https://zapier.com`, `zapier.com`). Required when you do not send a LinkedIn profile. Include the known employer website even with a profile so `email.identityConfidence` can check the employer too.","type":"string","minLength":3,"maxLength":2048}},"additionalProperties":false},"fields":{"description":"Which values to look up. Defaults to `[\"email\"]`, the synchronous one, so ask for `phone` explicitly. A request that includes `phone` comes back `202` with that field `pending` and a `lookupId` to poll. Phone lookups can take several minutes. Email in the same request is still answered inline.","minItems":1,"maxItems":2,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","enum":["email","phone"]}}},"required":["fullName"],"additionalProperties":false},"ContactLookupResultDto":{"type":"object","properties":{"person":{"type":"object","properties":{"fullName":{"type":"string"},"linkedinUrl":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The profile the lookup used, canonicalized from whatever form you sent."},"company":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"website":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The domain the lookup used, taken from the website you sent."}},"required":["name","website"],"additionalProperties":false}},"required":["fullName","linkedinUrl","company"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"The identity as the lookup understood it. Check it when the answer surprises you."},"email":{"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"What was found, or null."},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["found","not_found","pending","not_attempted","not_requested","failed","unconfirmed"],"description":"`found`: a value was found. `not_found`: the lookup finished without a value. A repeat request returns the saved result without another charge. `pending`: the lookup is running. Poll `lookupId`. `not_attempted`: the lookup is unavailable or the supplied details are insufficient. Nothing was searched or charged. For phone lookups, include `linkedinUrl`. `not_requested`: absent from `fields`. `failed`: this field failed. Read `error` for the reason and retry instructions. Nothing was charged for this field. If every requested field fails, the whole call returns an error. `unconfirmed` (email only): an address was found, but `identityConfidence` is `conflict`, so it may belong to someone else.